1
00:00:00,935 --> 00:00:03,505
♪ IN THE NOT-TOO-DISTANT
FUTURE ♪

2
00:00:03,538 --> 00:00:06,942
♪ NEXT SUNDAY A.D. ♪

3
00:00:06,975 --> 00:00:09,843
♪ THERE WAS
A GUY NAMED JOEL ♪

4
00:00:09,877 --> 00:00:13,013
♪ NOT TOO DIFFERENT
FROM YOU OR ME ♪

5
00:00:13,047 --> 00:00:16,150
♪ HE WORKED
AT GIZMONIC INSTITUTE ♪

6
00:00:16,183 --> 00:00:19,087
♪ JUST ANOTHER FACE
IN RED JUMP SUIT ♪

7
00:00:19,120 --> 00:00:22,123
♪ HE DID A GOOD JOB
CLEANING UP THE PLACE ♪

8
00:00:22,157 --> 00:00:23,925
♪ BUT HIS BOSSES
DIDN'T LIKE HIM ♪

9
00:00:23,958 --> 00:00:26,327
♪ SO THEY SHOT HIM
INTO SPACE! ♪

10
00:00:28,362 --> 00:00:31,532
♪ WE'LL SEND HIM
CHEESY MOVIES ♪

11
00:00:31,565 --> 00:00:33,367
♪ THE WORST WE CAN FIND ♪

12
00:00:33,400 --> 00:00:34,702
♪ LA! LA! LA! ♪

13
00:00:34,735 --> 00:00:37,572
♪ HE'LL HAVE TO SIT
AND WATCH THEM ALL ♪

14
00:00:37,605 --> 00:00:39,440
♪ THEN WE'LL MONITOR
HIS MIND ♪

15
00:00:39,473 --> 00:00:40,842
♪ LA! LA! LA! ♪

16
00:00:40,875 --> 00:00:43,978
♪ NOW KEEP IN MIND
JOEL CAN'T CONTROL ♪

17
00:00:44,012 --> 00:00:45,813
♪ WHEN THE MOVIES
BEGIN OR END ♪

18
00:00:45,847 --> 00:00:47,082
♪ LA! LA! LA! ♪

19
00:00:47,115 --> 00:00:49,983
♪ BECAUSE HE USED
THOSE SPECIAL PARTS ♪

20
00:00:50,017 --> 00:00:54,788
♪ TO MAKE HIS ROBOT FRIENDS ♪

21
00:00:54,822 --> 00:00:56,792
♪ ROBOT ROLL CALL ♪

22
00:00:56,825 --> 00:00:58,092
♪ CAMBOT ♪

23
00:00:58,125 --> 00:00:59,393
♪ GYPSY ♪

24
00:00:59,427 --> 00:01:01,262
♪ TOM SERVO ♪

25
00:01:01,295 --> 00:01:02,830
♪ CROW ♪

26
00:01:02,863 --> 00:01:05,967
♪ IF YOU'RE WONDERING
HOW HE EATS AND BREATHES ♪

27
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:07,735
♪ AND OTHER SCIENCE FACTS ♪

28
00:01:07,768 --> 00:01:09,203
♪ LA! LA! LA! ♪

29
00:01:09,237 --> 00:01:12,173
♪ THEN REPEAT TO YOURSELF
IT'S JUST A SHOW ♪

30
00:01:12,207 --> 00:01:14,842
♪ I SHOULD REALLY JUST RELAX ♪

31
00:01:14,875 --> 00:01:17,645
♪ FOR MYSTERY SCIENCE
THEATER ♪

32
00:01:17,678 --> 00:01:20,348
♪ 3000 ♪

33
00:01:29,323 --> 00:01:31,158
[FEMALE VOICE] 30 SECONDS
TO COMMERCIAL SIGN.

34
00:01:31,192 --> 00:01:32,793
HI, EVERYBODY. WELCOME
TO THE SATELLITE OF LOVE.

35
00:01:32,827 --> 00:01:35,163
MY NAME'S JOEL. I'M STILL
MAROONED OUT IN SPACE,

36
00:01:35,197 --> 00:01:37,898
AND IF YOU JUST TUNED IN,
I GUESS SO ARE YOU.

37
00:01:37,932 --> 00:01:40,435
UH, WE'RE EXPECTING A CALL
FROM THE NASTIES

38
00:01:40,468 --> 00:01:44,738
WHO SHOT US UP HERE
ANY SECOND NOW. ALL RIGHT?

39
00:01:44,772 --> 00:01:47,275
UH, BY THE WAY, IF YOU'RE GONNA
GO DURING THE COMMERCIAL

40
00:01:47,308 --> 00:01:48,475
AND MAKE A SNACK,

41
00:01:48,508 --> 00:01:50,378
UH, WHILE YOU'RE DIGGING
IN THE REFRIGERATOR,

42
00:01:50,412 --> 00:01:51,947
THINK OF ME.

43
00:01:51,980 --> 00:01:54,048
GET SOMETHING DELICIOUS
AND NUTRITIOUS,

44
00:01:54,082 --> 00:01:57,385
BECAUSE I'LL BE EATING
VICARIOUSLY THROUGH YOU, SO...

45
00:01:57,418 --> 00:02:01,255
COMMERCIAL SIGN IN FIVE,
FOUR, THREE, TWO...

46
00:02:01,288 --> 00:02:03,157
COMMERCIAL SIGN NOW.

47
00:02:03,190 --> 00:02:05,092
BE RIGHT BACK, OKAY?

48
00:02:12,567 --> 00:02:14,468
PUT IT THROUGH THE HOOP,
JOEL.

49
00:02:14,502 --> 00:02:17,605
YEAH. COOL.

50
00:02:19,340 --> 00:02:21,275
OOP. TRY NOT TO LOOK
SO HAPPY, YOU GUYS.

51
00:02:21,308 --> 00:02:23,443
HERE COME THE MAD SCIENTISTS.
THEY'RE CALLING.

52
00:02:23,477 --> 00:02:28,315
COME IN, JOEL, MY LITTLE
FREE-FLOATING VACUUM MONKEY.

53
00:02:28,348 --> 00:02:29,950
HEY, SIRS. WHAT'S UP?

54
00:02:29,983 --> 00:02:32,453
WELL, NOT MY HAIR.
IT'S LIMP AND LIFELESS.

55
00:02:32,487 --> 00:02:33,688
I DON'T KNOW WHAT TO DO.

56
00:02:33,722 --> 00:02:35,122
JUST GET ON WITH
THE INVENTION EXCHANGE.

57
00:02:35,155 --> 00:02:37,058
STOP LOOKING AT ME.

58
00:02:37,092 --> 00:02:39,593
YES, WHAT HAVE YOU
GOT FOR US, JOEL-ARINI?

59
00:02:39,627 --> 00:02:42,097
WELL, SIRS, THE THINGS
THAT I'VE BEEN WORKING ON

60
00:02:42,130 --> 00:02:44,898
IS THIS NEW WAY
OF TELEPORTING FOOD.

61
00:02:44,932 --> 00:02:46,333
IN THE FUTURE,

62
00:02:46,367 --> 00:02:48,335
THEY'RE NOT GONNA HAVE
DRIVE-THROUGH WINDOWS ANYMORE.

63
00:02:48,368 --> 00:02:50,238
THEY'LL HAVE DRIVE-BY WINDOWS.

64
00:02:50,272 --> 00:02:51,907
YOU JUST DRIVE YOUR CAR BY

65
00:02:51,940 --> 00:02:53,875
AND THEY TELEPORT THE FOOD
RIGHT INTO YOUR STOMACH

66
00:02:53,908 --> 00:02:55,343
USING SOMETHING LIKE THIS.

67
00:02:55,377 --> 00:02:59,347
OKAY, I PUT THIS ON, LOOK AT
AN ORDINARY COOKIE, AND...

68
00:02:59,380 --> 00:03:00,448
[CRUNCHING]

69
00:03:00,482 --> 00:03:01,482
WHOA.

70
00:03:01,515 --> 00:03:04,018
DELICIOUS. MM-MM.

71
00:03:04,052 --> 00:03:06,020
NOW HERE WE'LL TRY IT
WITH A GLASS OF MILK.

72
00:03:06,053 --> 00:03:08,022
THIS IS THE BIG SLURPEE SIZE.

73
00:03:08,055 --> 00:03:11,392
MM-MM-MM-MM-MM-MM-MM.

74
00:03:11,425 --> 00:03:13,962
- [GULPING]
- HEY.

75
00:03:13,995 --> 00:03:16,497
[SLURPING, GULPING
CONTINUES]

76
00:03:20,768 --> 00:03:22,303
IT WENT DOWN.

77
00:03:22,337 --> 00:03:23,872
MM-MM.

78
00:03:23,905 --> 00:03:25,807
TELEPORTATION.

79
00:03:25,840 --> 00:03:27,475
WHAT DO YOU THINK, SIRS?

80
00:03:27,508 --> 00:03:29,943
OH, VERY NICE, JOELEY CAKES.

81
00:03:29,977 --> 00:03:32,513
UH, LARRY, MAKE A NOTE
TO CALL JAMES DOOHAN.

82
00:03:32,547 --> 00:03:33,547
OH, HERE'S
OUR NEW DEVELOPMENT--

83
00:03:33,580 --> 00:03:36,117
AN ENTIRELY NEW CONCEPT
IN ORAL HYGIENE.

84
00:03:36,150 --> 00:03:38,887
YES, WE'VE EMPLOYED
SOME OF HOLLYWOOD'S TOP STARS

85
00:03:38,920 --> 00:03:42,057
TO HELP US WITH OUR
NEW MOUTH-TO-MOUTH
CELEBRITY TOOTHPASTE.

86
00:03:42,090 --> 00:03:44,725
FEEL THE CLEANING POWER
OF THE STARS' INTERNAL JUICES

87
00:03:44,758 --> 00:03:45,960
AS THEY GO TO WORK

88
00:03:45,993 --> 00:03:47,962
ON PLAQUE AND TARTAR BUILDUP
IN YOUR MOUTH.

89
00:03:47,995 --> 00:03:49,797
HERE'S JACK NICHOLSON
FROM WITCHES OF EASTWICK.

90
00:03:49,830 --> 00:03:51,232
BLAGH.

91
00:03:51,265 --> 00:03:54,168
MR. CREOSOTE FROM MONTY PYTHON'S
THE MEANING OF LIFE.

92
00:03:54,202 --> 00:03:56,103
"SOMEBODY GET A BUCKET.
I'M GONNA THROW UP."

93
00:03:56,137 --> 00:03:58,605
AND LINDA BLAIR WITH REAL
HEAD-CRANKING ACTION.

94
00:03:58,638 --> 00:03:59,940
"YOUR MOTHER
FLOSSES IN HELL."

95
00:03:59,973 --> 00:04:01,208
AAH!

96
00:04:01,242 --> 00:04:04,312
WELL, WHAT DO YOU THINK,
JOEL-ARINI?

97
00:04:04,345 --> 00:04:07,648
WELL, I THINK
FOUR OUT OF FIVE DENTISTS

98
00:04:07,682 --> 00:04:10,885
ARE GONNA RECOMMEND
PSYCHOTHERAPY FOR YOU TWO.

99
00:04:10,918 --> 00:04:11,885
[BOTH]
THANK YOU.

100
00:04:11,918 --> 00:04:14,388
WELL, JOEL,
YOUR FILM TODAY

101
00:04:14,422 --> 00:04:16,357
IS CALLED MOON ZERO TWO.

102
00:04:16,390 --> 00:04:18,125
IT'S A LATE '60s ROMP

103
00:04:18,158 --> 00:04:21,362
THROUGH THE THEN LUNAR-CRAZED
CONSCIOUSNESS OF AMERICA.

104
00:04:21,395 --> 00:04:24,965
AND BELIEVE ME, IT DOESN'T
STAND UP TO THE TEST OF TIME.

105
00:04:24,998 --> 00:04:27,735
STEW ON THE BROTH OF THIS ONE,
LUMPY BOY.

106
00:04:27,768 --> 00:04:28,903
ENJOY!

107
00:04:28,937 --> 00:04:31,338
OH, WE GOT MOVIE SIGN!

108
00:04:31,372 --> 00:04:33,708
HO!

109
00:04:40,882 --> 00:04:44,052
♪ MOON ZERO TWO ♪

110
00:04:44,085 --> 00:04:45,052
HEY, IT'S IN COLOR.

111
00:04:45,085 --> 00:04:46,187
YEAH.

112
00:04:46,220 --> 00:04:50,090
REALLY BAD MUSIC ALREADY.
THIS IS GREAT.

113
00:04:50,123 --> 00:04:53,027
HEY,
THE CARTOON HAS LANDED.

114
00:04:53,060 --> 00:04:55,195
IS THIS
A PINK PANTHER MOVIE?

115
00:04:55,228 --> 00:04:57,232
NO, UH, I THINK IT'S, UH,

116
00:04:57,265 --> 00:05:00,167
LIKE NASA SIMULATION,
KIND OF LIKE.

117
00:05:00,200 --> 00:05:01,968
WHY WOULD THEY
USE CARTOONS?

118
00:05:02,002 --> 00:05:04,905
WELL, SO ASTRONAUTS
COULD UNDERSTAND THEM.

119
00:05:04,938 --> 00:05:08,075
AH.

120
00:05:08,108 --> 00:05:10,712
♪ IT'S TIME
TO FLY DEEP SPACE... ♪

121
00:05:10,745 --> 00:05:13,313
HEY, I DIDN'T KNOW THE RUSSIANS
HAD CARTOONS.

122
00:05:13,347 --> 00:05:15,717
♪ GO FAR, GO WILD,
GO LONELY... ♪

123
00:05:15,750 --> 00:05:18,318
♪ NEW WORLDS ARE THERE
FOR THE TAKING ♪

124
00:05:18,352 --> 00:05:21,122
IS THIS PETULA CLARK
SINGING?

125
00:05:21,155 --> 00:05:22,290
PECULIAR CLARK.

126
00:05:22,323 --> 00:05:25,125
"PETULIAR"?

127
00:05:25,158 --> 00:05:28,228
TITLES MRS. REEDY'S
THIRD GRADE.

128
00:05:30,965 --> 00:05:32,967
WHOA.

129
00:05:40,140 --> 00:05:43,812
JUST, YOU GUYS,
I GOT THE BEAT.

130
00:05:43,845 --> 00:05:45,813
HEY, HE'S ON
THE OTHER SIDE.

131
00:05:45,847 --> 00:05:47,382
HE'S WHERE YOU WERE.

132
00:05:47,415 --> 00:05:51,452
CIRCLE THE MOON.
EXACTLY. GOOD.

133
00:05:51,485 --> 00:05:55,355
ROCK IT, JOEL.

134
00:05:55,388 --> 00:05:58,827
YOU LOOK LIKE GOLDIE HAWN
ON LAUGH-IN.

135
00:05:58,860 --> 00:06:00,327
EXCEPT FOR THE HAIR.

136
00:06:00,360 --> 00:06:04,098
AND THE BODY.

137
00:06:04,132 --> 00:06:09,503
HEY, IT'S '60'S GLASNOST.

138
00:06:09,537 --> 00:06:12,005
HEY, THAT'S OLD GLORY
HE JUST--

139
00:06:12,038 --> 00:06:13,808
OH.

140
00:06:13,842 --> 00:06:16,443
♪ ON THE MOON
WHERE I'M LIVIN' ♪

141
00:06:16,477 --> 00:06:19,880
♪ NEED SOME HELP
TO MAKE ME GROW ♪

142
00:06:19,913 --> 00:06:22,383
WHAT'D YOU THINK,
YOU GUYS?

143
00:06:22,417 --> 00:06:23,885
WE'LL LET YOU KNOW.

144
00:06:23,918 --> 00:06:29,590
♪ I COULD USE
A KIND OF LOVING... ♪

145
00:06:29,623 --> 00:06:30,692
OH, LOOK AT THAT.

146
00:06:30,725 --> 00:06:32,893
HE'S BEATING THE TITLES
OUT OF HIM.

147
00:06:32,927 --> 00:06:38,632
['60s POP MUSIC CONTINUES]

148
00:06:38,665 --> 00:06:42,303
♪ MOON ZERO TWO... ♪

149
00:06:46,307 --> 00:06:48,108
YOU STILL HAVE THE TELEPORTER
THING ON, JOEL.

150
00:06:48,142 --> 00:06:50,912
YEAH, I'M GONNA DO A THING
WHERE I PUT THIS ON

151
00:06:50,945 --> 00:06:54,015
AND EAT POPCORN THAT'S IN
THE GALLEY LATER.

152
00:06:57,752 --> 00:07:00,120
♪ WE'LL LOVE THE WORLD
WE LAND ON ♪

153
00:07:00,153 --> 00:07:01,222
♪ AND LOVE IS... ♪

154
00:07:01,255 --> 00:07:04,025
HEY, GREAT CLUB.
NO ATMOSPHERE.

155
00:07:04,058 --> 00:07:07,195
CAN'T BELIEVE THERE'S
A COVER CHARGE ON THE MOON.

156
00:07:10,998 --> 00:07:12,967
OH.

157
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:16,337
THEY'RE RIDING THE MOON.

158
00:07:16,370 --> 00:07:20,975
NO ATMOSPHERE.
NO ATMOSPHERE.

159
00:07:21,008 --> 00:07:23,010
IS THE WHOLE MOVIE
LIKE THIS, YOU GUYS?

160
00:07:23,043 --> 00:07:24,245
BOY, I HOPE NOT.

161
00:07:24,278 --> 00:07:26,480
I DON'T THINK I CAN TAKE
TWO HOURS OF THIS SONG.

162
00:07:26,513 --> 00:07:29,317
- THEY'RE TRASHED.
- CARTOON'S COOL, THOUGH.

163
00:07:29,350 --> 00:07:32,953
ARE THOSE THE BLUE MEANIES?

164
00:07:32,987 --> 00:07:36,090
NO, THAT'D BE--
THAT'D BE WRONG, PAUL.

165
00:07:36,123 --> 00:07:37,525
I'VE GOT A HOLE
IN ME POCKET.

166
00:07:37,558 --> 00:07:39,360
HEY, IT'S DONALD TRUMP.

167
00:07:39,393 --> 00:07:41,195
HE'S CHASING
THE GOOD GUYS AWAY.

168
00:07:41,228 --> 00:07:42,230
DOESN'T MAKE SENSE.

169
00:07:42,263 --> 00:07:43,865
IT MAKES PERFECT SENSE.

170
00:07:52,407 --> 00:07:54,508
HEY, LOOK.
IT'S THE FILM.

171
00:07:55,910 --> 00:08:00,615
♪ MOON ZERO TWO ♪

172
00:08:00,648 --> 00:08:05,218
♪ MOON ZERO TWO ♪

173
00:08:05,252 --> 00:08:07,087
WHOA.

174
00:08:07,120 --> 00:08:11,125
UH, HOUSTON, I JUST SPOTTED
AN ANIMATED CARTOON

175
00:08:11,158 --> 00:08:12,893
ON THE SURFACE OF THE MOON.

176
00:08:12,927 --> 00:08:15,128
[IMITATES STATIC]
COME IN.

177
00:08:25,505 --> 00:08:28,842
LOOKS LIKE THEY'RE SHOOTING THIS
OUT OF THE BACK OF A VAN.

178
00:08:28,875 --> 00:08:31,478
IT'S A RENEGADE
AIR-CONDITIONING UNIT.

179
00:08:31,512 --> 00:08:33,613
IT'S AN ORBITING
GARDEN WEASEL.

180
00:08:37,618 --> 00:08:41,055
AND AN ORBITING SPACE FERRET.

181
00:08:41,088 --> 00:08:42,290
[LAUGHS]

182
00:08:42,323 --> 00:08:44,292
SPACE FERRET. GET IT?

183
00:08:46,927 --> 00:08:49,063
HE'S GOING OUT
TO A SPACE GAZEBO.

184
00:08:49,097 --> 00:08:50,932
IT MUST BE COLD.

185
00:09:09,250 --> 00:09:10,652
THIS THING IS HUGE.

186
00:09:10,685 --> 00:09:12,920
HUH?

187
00:09:12,953 --> 00:09:16,190
LOOKS LIKE A LITTLE
ORBITING ICE MACHINE.

188
00:09:19,027 --> 00:09:20,895
HOUSTON,
OUR CENTRAL AIR IS HERE.

189
00:09:20,928 --> 00:09:23,130
BUT THEY DIDN'T SEND
THE DUCT WORK, OVER.

190
00:09:27,267 --> 00:09:29,270
BOY, I HOPE
IT'S UNDER WARRANTY.

191
00:09:29,303 --> 00:09:32,172
THAT'S A PRETTY BIG HOLE
IN THAT THING.

192
00:09:32,205 --> 00:09:34,908
HE'S GOT THE NINTENDO
POWER GLOVE THERE.

193
00:09:38,578 --> 00:09:40,380
OH, THEY PUT
THE DANGER WARNING LIGHT

194
00:09:40,413 --> 00:09:44,352
RIGHT ON THE MIDDLE
OF HIS BACK.

195
00:09:44,385 --> 00:09:46,720
SPACE IS A GAMBLE.

196
00:09:49,157 --> 00:09:50,623
DARN THOSE SPACE COONS.

197
00:09:50,657 --> 00:09:53,960
THEY GOT INTO
THE GARBAGE AGAIN.

198
00:09:53,993 --> 00:09:56,597
HONEY, WE'RE GETTING
THOSE RUBBERMAID CANS.

199
00:09:56,630 --> 00:09:57,865
THIS ISN'T
GONNA HAPPEN AGAIN.

200
00:09:57,898 --> 00:10:01,502
I'M NOT GOING IN FOR THIS.

201
00:10:09,877 --> 00:10:12,713
BOY, IT'S REALLY QUIET
IN SPACE, ISN'T IT?

202
00:10:12,747 --> 00:10:14,148
YEAH.

203
00:10:14,182 --> 00:10:17,150
EXCEPT FOR THE DISTANT
SOUND OF TRUMPETS.

204
00:10:19,187 --> 00:10:21,122
MAYNARD FERGUSON'S
OUT THERE SOMEWHERE.

205
00:10:21,155 --> 00:10:24,292
SO, WAS IT THE RACCOONS,
HONEY?

206
00:10:30,097 --> 00:10:32,065
SORT OF SEEMS LIKE
A WASTE OF CARGO SPACE

207
00:10:32,098 --> 00:10:33,967
TO BRING ALONG A CONGA BAND.

208
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:35,803
DARN COONS
IN MY RICKEN' FRACKIN'

209
00:10:35,837 --> 00:10:38,838
SOOMIN' HOOMIN'...

210
00:10:47,848 --> 00:10:50,752
OH, HE'S GOT V.P.L.
IN A BAD WAY.

211
00:10:52,420 --> 00:10:54,522
WHY DON'T WE EVER
TALK ANYMORE?

212
00:10:59,593 --> 00:11:01,362
HEY, WERE YOU MESSING
WITH MY STEREO?

213
00:11:01,395 --> 00:11:03,797
THE TREBLE'S
ALL THROWN OFF HERE.

214
00:11:22,450 --> 00:11:23,883
SILENCE.

215
00:11:23,917 --> 00:11:26,053
LET'S GO BACK
AND LOOK AT THE MOON.

216
00:11:26,087 --> 00:11:29,857
MAYBE THEY'RE SHOWING
THE FEATURE NOW.

217
00:11:29,890 --> 00:11:32,560
MOON ZERO TWO
CALLING MOON CONTROL.

218
00:11:32,593 --> 00:11:35,897
[RADIO]
MOON ZERO TWO,
THIS IS MOON CONTROL.

219
00:11:35,930 --> 00:11:37,932
ZERO TWO TO MOON CONTROL.

220
00:11:37,965 --> 00:11:39,867
MOON CONTROL TO MAJOR TOM.

221
00:11:39,900 --> 00:11:41,568
TWO MINUTES
FROM OUTER APPROACH.

222
00:11:41,602 --> 00:11:43,470
REQUEST
LANDING INSTRUCTIONS.

223
00:11:43,503 --> 00:11:44,972
HE'S GOT
PLAYTEX LIVING ELBOWS.

224
00:11:45,005 --> 00:11:46,507
LOOK AT THAT.

225
00:11:46,540 --> 00:11:48,908
...BEAR 157.

226
00:11:48,942 --> 00:11:52,078
DECELERATE AT 1.8 G.

227
00:11:52,112 --> 00:11:53,480
ZERO TWO UNDERSTAND.

228
00:11:53,513 --> 00:11:56,683
157 AT 1.8 G. OVER.

229
00:11:56,717 --> 00:11:58,552
SNAP IT UP, ZERO TWO.

230
00:11:58,585 --> 00:11:59,853
THIS IS PAN AM
MOON EXPRESS,

231
00:11:59,887 --> 00:12:01,288
AND WE'RE JUST
TEN MINUTES OUT.

232
00:12:01,322 --> 00:12:03,923
THAT IS YOUR HARD LUCK,
MOON EXPRESS.

233
00:12:03,957 --> 00:12:05,558
FIRST COME, FIRST DOWN.

234
00:12:05,592 --> 00:12:07,462
AND YOU ARE

235
00:12:07,495 --> 00:12:10,397
AN HOUR BEHIND SCHEDULE.

236
00:12:10,430 --> 00:12:11,765
HEY, HE FLIPPED 'EM OFF.

237
00:12:11,798 --> 00:12:13,600
WE'RE GONNA HAVE
TO JETTISON YOUR MUSTACHE,

238
00:12:13,633 --> 00:12:15,302
YOU REALIZE.

239
00:12:15,335 --> 00:12:17,472
HERE WE GO THEN.

240
00:12:20,607 --> 00:12:23,443
HEY, LOOK.
THERE IS A MAN IN THE MOON.

241
00:12:38,292 --> 00:12:39,927
...ANNOUNCE THE ARRIVAL
OF FLIGHT--

242
00:12:39,960 --> 00:12:41,695
THERE'S A SPACE
BLUE LIGHT SPECIAL

243
00:12:41,728 --> 00:12:43,063
ON QUADRANT B-9.

244
00:12:43,097 --> 00:12:44,698
IF YOU'RE MOON ZERO TWO,

245
00:12:44,732 --> 00:12:46,167
I WISH YOU'D SELL
THAT THING ALONG WITH

246
00:12:46,200 --> 00:12:48,068
ALL THE OTHER SPACE RUBBISH
YOU COLLECT.

247
00:12:48,102 --> 00:12:50,003
DON'T SAY HI.

248
00:12:50,037 --> 00:12:51,305
I DON'T THINK
I CAUGHT THE NAME.

249
00:12:51,338 --> 00:12:53,840
I'M THE SECOND OFFICER
OF THE MOON EXPRESS.

250
00:12:53,873 --> 00:12:55,408
YOU DELAYED US
FOR NEARLY TWO MINUTES.

251
00:12:55,442 --> 00:12:58,378
IF YOU TOOK OFF ON TIME,
YOU MIGHT LAND ON TIME.

252
00:12:58,412 --> 00:12:59,713
- I DON'T SEE THAT--
- I THOUGHT YOU WERE SEEING

253
00:12:59,747 --> 00:13:01,282
OUR PASSENGERS
THROUGH CUSTOMS.

254
00:13:01,315 --> 00:13:02,717
- I WAS JUST
TELLING THIS MAN--
- YOU CAN'T

255
00:13:02,750 --> 00:13:04,752
TELL THIS MAN
ANYTHING ABOUT ANYTHING.

256
00:13:04,785 --> 00:13:06,787
BUT FEEL FREE TO TELL HIM
SOMETHING ABOUT NOTHING

257
00:13:06,820 --> 00:13:09,957
OR A LITTLE ABOUT A LOT.

258
00:13:09,990 --> 00:13:11,392
UH, YOU'LL HAVE
TO EXCUSE MY FRIEND.

259
00:13:11,425 --> 00:13:13,393
HE'S KIND OF A WEENIE.

260
00:13:13,427 --> 00:13:16,497
THANK GOD
NOT ALL OF THEM MAKE IT.

261
00:13:16,530 --> 00:13:19,600
DAN, GET THIS
OVER TO THE SCRAPYARD.

262
00:13:19,633 --> 00:13:21,635
OH, WITH YOUR PERMISSION.

263
00:13:21,668 --> 00:13:22,903
AND DON'T TAKE
ANYTHING LESS THAN

264
00:13:22,937 --> 00:13:24,972
12,000 MOON DOLLARS FOR IT.

265
00:13:25,005 --> 00:13:26,207
I'LL TRY.

266
00:13:26,240 --> 00:13:28,075
I'VE JUST GOT TIME
FOR A SHOWER.

267
00:13:28,108 --> 00:13:29,777
I WANNA TALK TO YOU
A MINUTE.

268
00:13:29,810 --> 00:13:31,145
COME ON THEN.

269
00:13:31,178 --> 00:13:32,613
- MY NAME IS TAPLIN--
- PLEASE.

270
00:13:32,647 --> 00:13:34,415
TURN AND FACE
THE IMMIGRATION IDENTIFICATION

271
00:13:34,448 --> 00:13:35,615
COMPUTER PLEASE, MISS.

272
00:13:35,648 --> 00:13:38,385
I'M HERE FOR
THE GUMBY WEDDING.

273
00:13:38,418 --> 00:13:40,787
TEST YOUR LOVE.
FLAMING! GREAT.

274
00:13:40,820 --> 00:13:42,188
IS THERE A MESSAGE FOR ME?

275
00:13:42,222 --> 00:13:43,890
THE MESSAGE DESK'S
OVER THERE, MISS.

276
00:13:43,923 --> 00:13:46,360
THANK YOU.

277
00:13:46,393 --> 00:13:47,562
GOOD EVENING, MR. HUBBARD.

278
00:13:47,595 --> 00:13:51,098
WOW, IT'S CASTRO.

279
00:13:51,132 --> 00:13:53,000
I'M SORRY, MR. HUBBARD.

280
00:13:53,033 --> 00:13:54,402
I HOPE YOU ENJOYED
YOUR TRIP, SIR.

281
00:13:54,435 --> 00:13:57,137
NO MORE OR LESS THAN A HUNDRED
OTHER TRIPS I'VE TAKEN.

282
00:13:57,170 --> 00:13:58,905
WHERE'S THE ARMOR ALL?

283
00:14:02,008 --> 00:14:03,777
THAT'S A NIFTY
LITTLE CHARMER.

284
00:14:03,810 --> 00:14:05,178
J.J. HUBBARD.

285
00:14:05,212 --> 00:14:07,447
SO THAT'S 100% HUBBARD.

286
00:14:07,480 --> 00:14:09,583
- IS HE ALWAYS LIKE THAT?
- SURE, TO THE LIKES OF US.

287
00:14:09,617 --> 00:14:11,085
SOMETIMES HE'S 50%.

288
00:14:11,118 --> 00:14:12,518
WHAT DOES HE WANT UP HERE?

289
00:14:12,552 --> 00:14:15,322
- OH, I DON'T KNOW--
- ARE YOU GETTING SHORTER, BILL?

290
00:14:15,355 --> 00:14:18,392
IF IT WAS MINE,
HE COULD HAVE IT.

291
00:14:18,425 --> 00:14:21,228
CHEAP.

292
00:14:21,262 --> 00:14:23,530
LISTEN, I WAS...

293
00:14:23,563 --> 00:14:25,398
TALKING TO PERSONNEL
BACK AT EARTH BASE.

294
00:14:25,432 --> 00:14:26,700
[ALL MAKE WIND SOUNDS]

295
00:14:26,733 --> 00:14:28,102
[JOEL COUGHS]

296
00:14:28,135 --> 00:14:29,403
--BACK IN
THE CORPORATION, BILL.

297
00:14:29,437 --> 00:14:30,972
THEY STARTING
EXPLORATION FLIGHTS AGAIN?

298
00:14:31,005 --> 00:14:33,007
- NO.
- NO, SORTING BOXES.

299
00:14:33,040 --> 00:14:35,408
- BUT, UH--
- WHEN THEY OUTFIT
THE FIRST FLIGHT TO MERCURY.

300
00:14:35,442 --> 00:14:36,810
TELL THEM TO CALL ME.

301
00:14:36,843 --> 00:14:39,913
COME ON, BILL.
YOU KNOW THE ANSWER TO THAT ONE.

302
00:14:39,947 --> 00:14:42,048
WE DON'T HAVE YOUR NUMBER.
IT'S NOT LISTED.

303
00:14:42,082 --> 00:14:45,218
--TO LINE THE ROCKET TUBES
FOR JOURNEYS LIKE THAT.

304
00:14:45,252 --> 00:14:48,155
WE'VE GOT REGULAR FLIGHTS
TO MARS AND VENUS.

305
00:14:48,188 --> 00:14:49,757
- WHAT MORE DO YOU WANT?
- I'M NOT

306
00:14:49,790 --> 00:14:51,358
COMING BACK
INTO THE CORPORATION--

307
00:14:51,392 --> 00:14:54,060
WOW, DID HE GET THAT SHIRT AT
A MOLLY HATCHET CONCERT?

308
00:14:54,093 --> 00:14:57,632
--NOT A MECHANICALLY-MINDED
WET NURSE.

309
00:14:57,665 --> 00:15:00,300
THANK YOU VERY MUCH.

310
00:15:00,333 --> 00:15:02,035
[ALL COUGH]

311
00:15:02,068 --> 00:15:05,338
SOMEONE HAS TO BE
A PASSENGER PILOT.

312
00:15:05,372 --> 00:15:07,073
WHAT'S THAT YOU SAY?

313
00:15:07,107 --> 00:15:08,975
I SAID, SOMEONE

314
00:15:09,008 --> 00:15:11,378
HAS TO BE
A PASSENGER PILOT.

315
00:15:11,412 --> 00:15:14,247
CAN'T HEAR YOU.

316
00:15:14,280 --> 00:15:15,915
FORGET IT.

317
00:15:15,948 --> 00:15:18,885
I'LL GO GET THE REST
OF YOUR SHOWER DOOR.

318
00:15:23,190 --> 00:15:25,325
- HEY, THUMBELINA.
- I'M SORRY, MISS.

319
00:15:25,358 --> 00:15:27,493
THIS AREA'S OUT OF BOUNDS
TO PASSENGERS.

320
00:15:27,527 --> 00:15:30,130
- UM, I'M LOOKING FOR MR.--
- GOODBAR?

321
00:15:30,163 --> 00:15:33,167
CAPTAIN KEMP.

322
00:15:33,200 --> 00:15:34,802
OH.

323
00:15:34,835 --> 00:15:36,403
UH, WELL HE'S IN THERE.

324
00:15:36,437 --> 00:15:37,938
HE'S...

325
00:15:37,972 --> 00:15:39,473
DOING SOMETHING
JUST AT THE MOMENT,

326
00:15:39,507 --> 00:15:41,042
BUT HE WON'T BE LONG.

327
00:15:41,075 --> 00:15:42,777
[JOEL LAUGHS]

328
00:15:42,810 --> 00:15:46,047
- THANK YOU.
- HEY, YOUR CALCULATOR'S ON.

329
00:15:46,080 --> 00:15:48,382
OH BOY, IS SHE EVER GONNA--

330
00:15:48,415 --> 00:15:49,983
WHERE'S THE DRY--

331
00:15:50,017 --> 00:15:51,785
HEY, WHAT ARE YOU
LOOKING AT?

332
00:15:51,818 --> 00:15:55,155
OOPS.

333
00:15:55,188 --> 00:15:58,025
WHAT ARE YOU DOING HERE?

334
00:15:58,058 --> 00:16:00,360
I WAS LOOKING FOR
A CAPTAIN KEMP.

335
00:16:00,393 --> 00:16:02,528
THIS PLACE IS RESERVED

336
00:16:02,562 --> 00:16:04,097
FOR SPACE PERSONNEL ONLY.

337
00:16:04,130 --> 00:16:07,533
I'M SORRY.

338
00:16:07,567 --> 00:16:10,037
- ARE YOU CAPTAIN KEMP?
- WILL YOU GO AWAY?

339
00:16:10,070 --> 00:16:12,372
LOOK AT MY STRIPES,
OF COURSE I'M CAPTAIN KEMP.

340
00:16:12,405 --> 00:16:14,542
GO!

341
00:16:14,575 --> 00:16:16,143
[P.A.]
MONORAIL TO MOON CITY

342
00:16:16,177 --> 00:16:18,312
WILL DEPART
IN SEVEN MINUTES.

343
00:16:20,380 --> 00:16:22,348
OH. HI, GUMBY.

344
00:16:29,490 --> 00:16:32,025
OTTO? OTTO GOT KILLED?

345
00:16:32,058 --> 00:16:35,662
COUPLE OF DAYS AGO.

346
00:16:35,695 --> 00:16:37,998
YEAH, WE'RE DEDICATING
A LOCKER ROOM TO HIM.

347
00:16:38,032 --> 00:16:39,500
HOW?

348
00:16:39,533 --> 00:16:41,202
RETRO ENGINES
FAILED ON LANDING.

349
00:16:41,235 --> 00:16:43,170
THAT'S WHAT I HEARD.
WENT STRAIGHT IN.

350
00:16:43,203 --> 00:16:46,038
CRUNCH.

351
00:16:46,072 --> 00:16:49,208
BETTER PUT THAT THING OUTSIDE
WHERE PEOPLE CAN READ IT.

352
00:16:49,242 --> 00:16:50,877
PASSENGERS WOULDN'T LIKE IT.

353
00:16:50,910 --> 00:16:52,578
IT WOULD WORRY THEM.

354
00:16:52,612 --> 00:16:53,813
YEAH, BUT TO MAKE IT

355
00:16:53,847 --> 00:16:57,417
A SPLASH GUARD FOR A URINAL?

356
00:16:57,450 --> 00:16:59,520
DID YOU GET THE 12,000?

357
00:17:04,825 --> 00:17:06,593
HERE, I DON'T NEED IT.
I ALREADY HAVE PETE ROSE.

358
00:17:06,627 --> 00:17:08,662
HEY,

359
00:17:08,695 --> 00:17:10,430
HE FLEW THE SAME
SORT OF SPACE FERRY

360
00:17:10,463 --> 00:17:13,067
- YOU GOT, DIDN'T HE?
- MM-HMM.

361
00:17:13,100 --> 00:17:15,568
HIS WAS A LITTLE BIT OLDER,
THAT'S ALL.

362
00:17:15,602 --> 00:17:17,905
LITTLE BIT WISER.
SOMETHING TO THINK ABOUT.

363
00:17:23,943 --> 00:17:26,780
THEY DRESSED THEIR STEWARDESSES
LIKE NAZIS.

364
00:17:26,813 --> 00:17:28,682
LEAVING RIGHT AWAY,
MR. HUBBARD.

365
00:17:28,715 --> 00:17:30,150
- MAGAZINE?
- YES, IT IS.

366
00:17:30,183 --> 00:17:32,618
COFFEE? FOR YOU, SIR?

367
00:17:32,652 --> 00:17:34,120
HE DOESN'T DRINK,
AND HE CAN'T READ.

368
00:17:34,153 --> 00:17:36,957
BUT HE STILL
HAS FEELINGS, JEEZ.

369
00:17:36,990 --> 00:17:38,492
THEY'RE SO RICH
THEY GO TO MOVIES,

370
00:17:38,525 --> 00:17:41,528
AND THEY DON'T EVEN
WATCH THEM.

371
00:17:41,562 --> 00:17:43,763
- TRINIE.
- HELLO, BILL.

372
00:17:43,797 --> 00:17:45,098
YOU LOOK GREAT.

373
00:17:45,132 --> 00:17:46,467
WHEN'D YOU JOIN THE GUARD?

374
00:17:46,500 --> 00:17:48,435
RIGHT AFTER I TURNED IN
THE VON TRAPP FAMILY.

375
00:17:48,468 --> 00:17:51,605
SAME OLD ME
ON THE INSIDE, THOUGH.

376
00:17:51,638 --> 00:17:53,340
GOT A SEAT?

377
00:17:53,373 --> 00:17:55,708
ONE UP FRONT
FOR THE CAPTAIN.

378
00:17:59,547 --> 00:18:02,382
THIS IS CAPTAIN KEMP,
MS. TAPLIN.

379
00:18:02,415 --> 00:18:04,752
- YOU SAID--
- I'M ALWAYS AT A DISADVANTAGE

380
00:18:04,785 --> 00:18:06,687
WHEN I HAVEN'T
GOT ANY CLOTHES ON.

381
00:18:06,720 --> 00:18:07,988
I NEVER NOTICED IT.

382
00:18:08,022 --> 00:18:09,757
WELL? WHAT DID YOU--

383
00:18:09,790 --> 00:18:12,092
DO YOU THINK I LOOK
LIKE A ZUCCHINI?

384
00:18:12,125 --> 00:18:14,193
SHE LOOKS LIKE DOT VADER.

385
00:18:14,227 --> 00:18:16,863
--TOLD ME YOU'D FLY OVER
TO FAR SIDE OCCASIONALLY.

386
00:18:16,897 --> 00:18:19,098
- MM-HMM.
- I WONDERED

387
00:18:19,132 --> 00:18:20,800
- IF YOU KNOW MY BROTHER.
- GARY LARSON.

388
00:18:20,833 --> 00:18:24,203
WALLY TAPLIN. HE'S A MINER.

389
00:18:24,237 --> 00:18:26,072
NO, NO, I DON'T THINK
I KNOW HIM.

390
00:18:26,105 --> 00:18:27,807
HE WAS SUPPOSED TO MEET ME
AT THE SPACE PORT.

391
00:18:27,840 --> 00:18:30,110
HE'S PROBABLY WAITING
AT MOON CITY.

392
00:18:30,143 --> 00:18:31,612
MM-HMM,
THAT'S WHAT THE MAN SAID.

393
00:18:31,645 --> 00:18:34,047
DON'T YOU LISTEN
TO WHAT THE MAN SAYS.

394
00:18:34,080 --> 00:18:35,382
YOUR FIRST TIME UP HERE?

395
00:18:35,415 --> 00:18:37,417
THAT WOULD EXPLAIN
THE STUPID HAT.

396
00:18:37,450 --> 00:18:39,485
THEN I SUGGEST
YOU LOOK UP FRONT.

397
00:18:39,518 --> 00:18:42,055
WHILE I CHECK OUT THE REAR.

398
00:18:42,088 --> 00:18:43,723
MM.

399
00:18:46,660 --> 00:18:49,128
MY GOD, IT'S SO BLEAK.

400
00:18:49,162 --> 00:18:52,198
NO AIR. NO VEGETATION.

401
00:18:52,232 --> 00:18:54,333
ONE-SIXTH GRAVITY.

402
00:18:54,367 --> 00:18:57,070
YEAH, BUT ON THE GOOD SIDE,
THERE'S NO HOWIE MANDEL.

403
00:18:57,103 --> 00:18:59,707
--FOURTEEN DAYS OF NIGHT.

404
00:18:59,740 --> 00:19:00,973
I SUPPOSE BLEAK IS

405
00:19:01,007 --> 00:19:03,710
AS GOOD A WAY AS ANY
TO DESCRIBE IT.

406
00:19:03,743 --> 00:19:05,745
YEAH, AND EVERYBODY
GETS THEIR OWN MOVIE.

407
00:19:05,778 --> 00:19:07,747
--FOREIGNERS HERE.

408
00:19:07,780 --> 00:19:09,482
WE ALWAYS WILL BE.

409
00:19:09,515 --> 00:19:11,318
SOME ARE MORE FOREIGN
THAN OTHERS, VELVET-HEAD.

410
00:19:11,352 --> 00:19:13,920
PERHAPS WE SHOULD
NEVER HAVE COME.

411
00:19:20,127 --> 00:19:23,163
IN THE FUTURE,
BRAS WILL GROW ON THE MOON.

412
00:19:23,197 --> 00:19:25,532
CROSS MY HEART.

413
00:19:32,172 --> 00:19:34,407
HEY, IT'S THE ORIGINAL
SPACE MOUNTAIN.

414
00:19:34,440 --> 00:19:35,808
WHAT DO YOU KNOW? AND LOOK,

415
00:19:35,842 --> 00:19:37,912
THE LINE'S STILL LONG.

416
00:19:39,780 --> 00:19:41,748
THE MONUMENT THERE
IS WHERE NEIL ARMSTRONG

417
00:19:41,782 --> 00:19:43,650
LANDED BACK IN 1969.

418
00:19:43,683 --> 00:19:45,085
COURSE, THAT'S JUST A MODEL.

419
00:19:45,118 --> 00:19:48,288
THE REAL THING'S
A LOT BIGGER.

420
00:19:48,322 --> 00:19:49,590
AND THE ICE MINES.

421
00:19:49,623 --> 00:19:51,958
- THE WHAT?
- ICE MINES.

422
00:19:53,960 --> 00:19:56,430
THEY'RE LAYERS OF ICE
A MILE DOWN.

423
00:19:56,463 --> 00:19:58,632
MELT IT INTO WATER,
AND YOU DRINK IT.

424
00:19:58,665 --> 00:20:01,568
BREAK IT INTO OXYGEN,
YOU BREATHE IT.

425
00:20:01,602 --> 00:20:04,905
CRUSH IT AND FLAVOR IT,
YOU GOT A SLURPEE.

426
00:20:04,938 --> 00:20:06,840
D-CUPS AS FAR
AS THE EYE CAN SEE.

427
00:20:06,873 --> 00:20:08,642
--PROCESS OXYGEN.

428
00:20:08,675 --> 00:20:11,512
WHEN THEY DIE, WE EAT THEM.

429
00:20:11,545 --> 00:20:15,315
THERE IS NOTHING LIKE IT
ANYWHERE ELSE.

430
00:20:15,348 --> 00:20:18,018
IT'S FUNNY TO THINK THAT,
WITH NO AIR OUT THERE,

431
00:20:18,052 --> 00:20:21,755
NOBODY CAN JUST
OPEN UP A WINDOW.

432
00:20:21,788 --> 00:20:24,925
OH, WE'VE DONE THAT, BUT YOU
JUST HAVE TO BE REALLY FAST.

433
00:20:24,958 --> 00:20:27,827
CAPTAIN KEMP, I'M AFRAID
WE HAVE NO RESERVATION

434
00:20:27,860 --> 00:20:30,397
IN THE NAME
OF MR. WALLACE TAPLIN.

435
00:20:30,430 --> 00:20:34,267
NOR HAVE WE ANY MESSAGES
FOR A MS. CLEMENTINE TAPLIN.

436
00:20:34,300 --> 00:20:36,102
YEAH YEAH, SURE,
DON'T YOU HAVE

437
00:20:36,135 --> 00:20:38,872
TO GO MAKE
SOME ELFIN COOKIES?

438
00:20:38,905 --> 00:20:40,507
SHE LOOKS LIKE
AN OOMPA LOOMPA.

439
00:20:40,540 --> 00:20:42,708
WELL, IT COULD BE
HE'S JUST LATE.

440
00:20:42,742 --> 00:20:44,778
THE MONORAIL DOESN'T GO
ANY FARTHER THAN MOON CITY.

441
00:20:44,812 --> 00:20:46,980
SO HE'D BE COMING BY BUG.

442
00:20:47,013 --> 00:20:49,148
BUG?

443
00:20:49,182 --> 00:20:51,183
IT'S A WAY YOU
GET AROUND UP HERE.

444
00:20:51,217 --> 00:20:53,320
THEY RUN CONVOYS OF THEM
OVER TO FAR SIDE--

445
00:20:53,353 --> 00:20:55,055
IT'S LEGO MOON BASE.

446
00:20:55,088 --> 00:20:57,257
- IT'S A SLOW BUSINESS.
- VROOM VROOM.

447
00:20:57,290 --> 00:20:58,792
WHERE'S HIS CLAIM?

448
00:20:58,825 --> 00:21:00,927
SPECTACLE CRATER.

449
00:21:05,665 --> 00:21:07,300
WELL, THE WATER'S TURNED OFF
ON THE FOUNTAIN,

450
00:21:07,333 --> 00:21:10,003
SO I CAN SHOW YOU
WHERE HE IS HERE.

451
00:21:10,037 --> 00:21:11,638
- RIGHT THERE.
- THE NEAREST BASE

452
00:21:11,672 --> 00:21:14,073
IS FAR SIDE FIVE.

453
00:21:14,107 --> 00:21:17,277
NOW, THAT'S
AT LEAST 2,000 MILES

454
00:21:17,310 --> 00:21:18,612
TO MOON CITY.

455
00:21:18,645 --> 00:21:20,880
SIX DAYS BY CONVOY.

456
00:21:20,913 --> 00:21:22,148
THAT MEANS
IT TAKES LONGER TO GET

457
00:21:22,182 --> 00:21:23,750
FROM ONE SIDE OF THE MOON
TO THE OTHER.

458
00:21:23,783 --> 00:21:25,418
UH, NO, BUT THANKS
FOR PLAYING.

459
00:21:25,452 --> 00:21:26,687
THAT'S RIGHT.

460
00:21:26,720 --> 00:21:28,522
WHAT ABOUT YOUR SPACESHIP?

461
00:21:28,555 --> 00:21:30,790
FERRY.
IT'S ONLY A MOON FERRY.

462
00:21:30,823 --> 00:21:32,058
AT LEAST HE'S OPEN ABOUT IT.

463
00:21:32,092 --> 00:21:34,560
-- IN 20 MINUTES.

464
00:21:34,593 --> 00:21:37,263
- I SUPPOSE--
- THAT'S BECAUSE
THIS IS THE FUTURE.

465
00:21:37,297 --> 00:21:38,798
BUT I CAN SEND
A RADIO MESSAGE, CAN'T I?

466
00:21:38,832 --> 00:21:40,133
- UH-HUH.
- TO SEE IF HE'S LEFT?

467
00:21:40,167 --> 00:21:42,635
OH, NO. WELL,
YOU COULD'VE LAST WEEK.

468
00:21:42,668 --> 00:21:45,138
YOU SEE, WE USE A RING
OF COMMUNICATION SATELLITES

469
00:21:45,172 --> 00:21:46,807
FOR RELAYING WAVES
AROUND THE CURVE,

470
00:21:46,840 --> 00:21:48,675
BUT ONE WAS HIT
BY A METEORITE.

471
00:21:48,708 --> 00:21:51,412
SO WE'RE OUT OF TOUCH
WITH FAR SIDE RIGHT NOW.

472
00:21:53,012 --> 00:21:54,915
21ST CENTURY.

473
00:21:54,948 --> 00:21:57,683
IT'LL STILL BE THE SAME
IN THE 25TH.

474
00:21:57,717 --> 00:21:58,952
I SUPPOSE SO.

475
00:21:58,985 --> 00:22:01,187
UM, WE'RE ALMOST
WALKING OFF THE SET.

476
00:22:01,220 --> 00:22:03,490
WOULD YOU MIND, UH,
GOING THE OTHER WAY?

477
00:22:03,523 --> 00:22:05,358
--AS ALL THAT.
SPLURGE OUT.

478
00:22:05,392 --> 00:22:07,127
BUY YOURSELF A NEW OUTFIT.
YOU'LL FEEL BETTER.

479
00:22:07,160 --> 00:22:08,995
OH, WE'D BETTER
GET OUT OF HERE, TOO.

480
00:22:09,028 --> 00:22:11,197
WELCOME TO
THE GALAXY BOUTIQUE.

481
00:22:11,230 --> 00:22:14,300
- CAN I HELP YOU?
- LOOK AT THAT, A BARE MIDRIFF.

482
00:22:24,277 --> 00:22:26,613
ON JULY 22ND, 1969,

483
00:22:26,647 --> 00:22:29,783
A MAN FIRST SET FOOT
ON THE SURFACE OF THE MOON.

484
00:22:29,817 --> 00:22:32,452
HIS NAME? VINCE LOMBARDI.

485
00:22:32,485 --> 00:22:35,255
OH, SORRY,
IT'S NEIL ARMSTRONG.

486
00:22:35,288 --> 00:22:37,057
THIS IS OUR TRIBUTE
TO ASTRONAUT ARMSTRONG

487
00:22:37,090 --> 00:22:39,092
AND THE MEN WHO BROUGHT HIM
TO THE MOON.

488
00:22:39,125 --> 00:22:41,828
CROW WILL PLAY THE PART
OF NEIL ARMSTRONG.

489
00:22:41,862 --> 00:22:43,530
THAT'S ONE SMALL STEP
FOR MAN.

490
00:22:43,563 --> 00:22:45,532
- SAVE IT!
- WHAT? OH.

491
00:22:45,565 --> 00:22:46,733
SORRY.

492
00:22:46,767 --> 00:22:48,067
JOEL WILL PLAY THE PART

493
00:22:48,100 --> 00:22:51,103
OF THE SECOND MAN ON THE MOON,
EDWIN "BUZZ" ALDRIN,

494
00:22:51,137 --> 00:22:54,975
AND PRESIDENT
JOHN F. KENNEDY.

495
00:22:55,008 --> 00:22:56,408
I'LL PLAY THE PART
OF MISSION CONTROL

496
00:22:56,442 --> 00:22:57,877
AND ASTRONAUT
MICHAEL COLLINS

497
00:22:57,910 --> 00:23:00,513
ORBITING THE MOON.

498
00:23:00,547 --> 00:23:02,982
- OKAY.
- READY? OKAY.

499
00:23:03,015 --> 00:23:04,550
CUE JOEL.

500
00:23:04,583 --> 00:23:07,953
ASK NOT WHAT YOUR COUNTRY
CAN DO FOR YOU.

501
00:23:07,987 --> 00:23:11,825
RATHER WHAT YOU CAN DO
FOR YOUR COUNTRY.

502
00:23:11,858 --> 00:23:14,260
IT WAS 1962,
AND A YOUNG PRESIDENT,

503
00:23:14,293 --> 00:23:17,997
JOHN F. KENNEDY,
MAKES A BOLD PROMISE.

504
00:23:18,030 --> 00:23:19,833
BY THE END OF THIS DECADE,

505
00:23:19,867 --> 00:23:22,402
WE WILL SEND A MAN
SAFELY TO THE MOON

506
00:23:22,435 --> 00:23:24,703
AND RETURN HIM SAFELY HOME.

507
00:23:27,207 --> 00:23:29,775
UH, NOT BAD, JOEL,
BUT YOU KNOW, YOU SOUND

508
00:23:29,808 --> 00:23:31,945
A LITTLE BIT LIKE
CLIFF FROM CHEERS.

509
00:23:31,978 --> 00:23:33,247
[CROW STRAINS]

510
00:23:33,280 --> 00:23:35,748
- THIS IS MY BIG SCENE.
- "NOT QUITE TEN YEARS LATER."

511
00:23:35,782 --> 00:23:38,985
THANK YOU.

512
00:23:39,018 --> 00:23:41,622
30 FEET. TWO AND A HALF.

513
00:23:41,655 --> 00:23:43,423
PICKING UP SOME DUST.

514
00:23:43,457 --> 00:23:44,925
30 SECONDS.

515
00:23:44,958 --> 00:23:46,392
CONTACT LIGHT. OKAY.

516
00:23:46,425 --> 00:23:47,960
ENGINE STOP.

517
00:23:47,993 --> 00:23:50,130
WE COPY YOU DOWN, EAGLE.

518
00:23:50,163 --> 00:23:52,432
HOUSTON,
TRANQUILITY BASE HERE.

519
00:23:52,465 --> 00:23:54,868
THE EAGLE HAS LANDED.

520
00:23:54,902 --> 00:23:56,737
ROGER, TRANQUILITY,
WE COPY YOU ON THE GROUND.

521
00:23:56,770 --> 00:23:59,038
YOU GOT A BUNCH OF GUYS
DOWN HERE ABOUT TO TURN BLUE.

522
00:23:59,072 --> 00:24:01,040
WE'RE BREATHING AGAIN,
THANKS A LOT.

523
00:24:01,073 --> 00:24:02,842
THANK YOU.

524
00:24:02,875 --> 00:24:06,212
NO? NO. OKAY,
I'M ON THE PAD NOW.

525
00:24:06,245 --> 00:24:09,415
I'M JUMPING OFF.

526
00:24:09,448 --> 00:24:12,285
THAT'S ONE SMALL STEP
FOR A MAN.

527
00:24:12,318 --> 00:24:16,255
ONE GIANT LEAP FOR MANKIND.

528
00:24:16,288 --> 00:24:17,490
UGH.

529
00:24:17,523 --> 00:24:19,860
OKAY, HERE I COME.
I'M COMING DOWN OUT OF

530
00:24:19,893 --> 00:24:21,962
THE LUNAR MODULE.

531
00:24:21,995 --> 00:24:24,497
HEY, JOEL, HOW COME
YOUR COSTUME'S NOT VERY GOOD?

532
00:24:24,530 --> 00:24:27,033
WELL, I HAD TO BE THE PRESIDENT
AND BUZZ ALDRIN,

533
00:24:27,067 --> 00:24:29,668
- SO, OKAY? JEEZ.
- OH, OKAY.

534
00:24:29,702 --> 00:24:31,503
OH MAN, DID--
DO YOU HAVE YOUR KEYS?

535
00:24:31,537 --> 00:24:32,938
I JUST LOCKED OURSELVES
OUT OF THE LEM.

536
00:24:32,972 --> 00:24:34,740
NO-- YOU WHAT?

537
00:24:34,773 --> 00:24:37,943
OH, WOW, THAT'S ONE SMALL
SCREW-UP FOR YOU,

538
00:24:37,977 --> 00:24:39,913
ONE GIANT SCREW-UP FOR YOU.

539
00:24:39,947 --> 00:24:41,915
- I'M GONNA HAVE TO GO--
- THUS ENDS OUR PROJECT.

540
00:24:41,948 --> 00:24:43,483
...FIND THAT THING.

541
00:24:52,225 --> 00:24:53,727
WHAT'S THAT?

542
00:24:53,760 --> 00:24:57,163
WHOA.

543
00:24:57,197 --> 00:24:58,565
YOWZA.

544
00:24:58,598 --> 00:25:01,400
THEY'RE WEARING OTHELLO
GAME PIECES ON THEIR HEAD.

545
00:25:01,433 --> 00:25:04,938
OTHELLO.

546
00:25:04,972 --> 00:25:08,375
YOU KNOW, I KIND OF
MISS THE MOON, YOU GUYS.

547
00:25:08,408 --> 00:25:09,642
I CAN SEE WHY.

548
00:25:09,675 --> 00:25:11,778
HEY, CROW, YOU CAN'T
BE WEARING THAT, HERE.

549
00:25:11,812 --> 00:25:14,180
OW-- OW!

550
00:25:14,213 --> 00:25:16,082
OH, THANK YOU.

551
00:25:16,115 --> 00:25:18,552
HEY, IT LOOKS LIKE LIZA MINELLI
AND LOLA FALANA

552
00:25:18,585 --> 00:25:20,953
HAD A GARAGE SALE.

553
00:25:20,987 --> 00:25:22,522
I MISS HIM, TOO.

554
00:25:22,555 --> 00:25:24,958
HE WAS A VERY GOOD CUSTOMER.
AND A GOOD MAN.

555
00:25:24,992 --> 00:25:27,960
AND A GOOD PILOT.

556
00:25:27,993 --> 00:25:29,895
AS PILOTS GO,

557
00:25:29,928 --> 00:25:31,430
HE WENT.

558
00:25:31,463 --> 00:25:32,965
MOON FLOWER, DOUBLE.

559
00:25:32,998 --> 00:25:35,568
UH, THE NAME'S BOB,
IF YOU DON'T MIND.

560
00:25:35,602 --> 00:25:37,170
IT'S AN OLD-FASHIONED
PAMPAS PUNCH.

561
00:25:37,203 --> 00:25:39,472
PAMPERS PUNCH? ICK.

562
00:25:45,212 --> 00:25:46,980
FIRST ONE'S ON THE HOUSE.

563
00:25:47,013 --> 00:25:49,848
YOU DIDN'T BUY ME A DRINK.

564
00:25:49,882 --> 00:25:52,418
NICE BAR, REALLY CRUMMY
ATMOSPHERE THOUGH.

565
00:25:52,452 --> 00:25:53,653
[BOTS LAUGH]

566
00:25:53,687 --> 00:25:55,322
THAT ONE WILL LIVE FOREVER.

567
00:25:55,355 --> 00:25:57,657
LOT OF MILEAGE THERE.

568
00:26:03,295 --> 00:26:05,765
STILL TASTES LIKE
DISTILLED ROCKET FUEL.

569
00:26:05,798 --> 00:26:09,368
IT IS DISTILLED ROCKET FUEL.

570
00:26:09,402 --> 00:26:10,737
THAT'S EASY FOR YOU TO SAY.

571
00:26:10,770 --> 00:26:12,238
HOW MUCH IT COST THIS WEEK?

572
00:26:12,272 --> 00:26:13,773
$35 A SHOT.

573
00:26:13,807 --> 00:26:15,042
YOU SEE,
WE'RE A LONG WAY FROM--

574
00:26:15,075 --> 00:26:17,810
A LONG WAY FROM SCOTLAND,
I KNOW.

575
00:26:17,843 --> 00:26:19,612
HEY, PAL,
I'VE GOT A SMALL PART.

576
00:26:19,645 --> 00:26:22,082
LET ME FINISH MY OWN LINES,
IF YOU DON'T MIND.

577
00:26:22,115 --> 00:26:25,085
--BUT I HAVEN'T GOT
$35 A SHOT.

578
00:26:25,118 --> 00:26:28,120
ISN'T IT ABOUT TIME
YOU GOT HUNGRY?

579
00:26:28,153 --> 00:26:31,423
A GOOD POINT, MICHAEL.

580
00:26:31,457 --> 00:26:34,693
AND SO THE GROUND-SPACE
ENGINEER

581
00:26:34,727 --> 00:26:36,528
PASSES ITO THE GREAT UNKNOWN

582
00:26:36,562 --> 00:26:39,632
UNKNOWN OF JOE'S OLD TIME--

583
00:26:39,665 --> 00:26:41,768
PIZZA-TIME THEATER.

584
00:26:41,802 --> 00:26:45,705
PERHAPS NEVER TO RETURN.

585
00:26:45,738 --> 00:26:47,273
HE WAS OTTO VON BECK'S
ENGINEER

586
00:26:47,307 --> 00:26:50,243
FOR A COUPLE OF YEARS,
BEFORE HE CAME TO ME.

587
00:26:50,277 --> 00:26:52,478
MAYBE HE'S JUST
GLAD TO BE ALIVE.

588
00:26:52,512 --> 00:26:54,380
SURE, ALL ENGINEERS
ARE CRAZY.

589
00:26:54,413 --> 00:26:57,483
HEY, THAT'S A PRETTY
BROAD STATEMENT, PAL.

590
00:26:57,517 --> 00:26:59,918
WHAT DID YOU CALL THIS?
PAMPAS PUNCH?

591
00:26:59,952 --> 00:27:01,220
NO, IT'S BILE. WHY?

592
00:27:01,253 --> 00:27:04,123
TASTES MORE LIKE
TIJUANA BRASS POLISH.

593
00:27:04,157 --> 00:27:05,392
GOOD ONE.

594
00:27:05,425 --> 00:27:07,527
[BOTS LAUGH]

595
00:27:14,867 --> 00:27:17,437
IT'S MOON ZERO MOSTEL.

596
00:27:18,838 --> 00:27:21,140
YOU KNOW WHAT
THEIR ANSWER IS.

597
00:27:23,008 --> 00:27:25,245
HAIRPIECES BY
ALEXANDER CALDER.

598
00:27:25,278 --> 00:27:28,180
THEY'RE DOING THE NO-DANCE.

599
00:27:28,213 --> 00:27:31,350
♪ NO-NO-NO-NO-NO ♪

600
00:27:31,383 --> 00:27:33,953
[BEEPING]

601
00:27:36,990 --> 00:27:39,392
HEY, YOU COULD'VE
JUST SAID "HELLO."

602
00:27:46,432 --> 00:27:48,868
HEY, HOW ARE THEY MAKING
THAT NOISE, JOEL?

603
00:27:50,803 --> 00:27:53,372
THAT'S NO WAY TO TREAT
A PHONE, FRIEND.

604
00:27:53,405 --> 00:27:55,642
I BOUGHT IT A DRINK.
WHAT MORE CAN A MAN DO?

605
00:27:55,675 --> 00:27:56,910
WELL, MAYBE GET IT
SOME DINNER.

606
00:27:56,943 --> 00:27:58,945
A GENTLEMAN WANTS
A WORD WITH YOU.

607
00:27:58,978 --> 00:28:01,180
YOU CAN TELL HIM
TO GO TO HELL AND STAY.

608
00:28:01,213 --> 00:28:04,217
MR. HUBBARD
WANTS TO SEE YOU.

609
00:28:04,250 --> 00:28:05,885
OLD 100% HUBBARD?

610
00:28:05,918 --> 00:28:08,788
L. RON HUBBARD?
OLD MOTHER HUBBARD?

611
00:28:08,822 --> 00:28:10,857
--HE CAN GO 100% TO HELL.

612
00:28:10,890 --> 00:28:12,858
LET'S JUST GO
AND SEE MR. HUBBARD.

613
00:28:12,892 --> 00:28:14,793
CONVINCE ME.

614
00:28:14,827 --> 00:28:17,230
I'M CONVINCED!
OH, IT'S A GUN.

615
00:28:18,998 --> 00:28:21,533
I'M CONVINCED.

616
00:28:33,345 --> 00:28:35,548
WELL, THROW.

617
00:28:37,450 --> 00:28:40,120
- OOH, STUPID.
- OH BROTHER.

618
00:28:40,153 --> 00:28:43,757
LET'S MOON HIM, COME ON.

619
00:28:43,790 --> 00:28:44,957
HONEY, FIX YOUR DRESS.

620
00:28:44,990 --> 00:28:47,493
COMMUNITY CHEST.

621
00:28:47,527 --> 00:28:48,962
YEAH.

622
00:28:48,995 --> 00:28:50,497
GO TO JAIL.

623
00:28:50,530 --> 00:28:54,467
MOVE DIRECTLY TO JAIL.

624
00:28:54,500 --> 00:28:56,635
DO NOT PASS GO.

625
00:28:56,668 --> 00:28:58,303
DO NOT COLLECT

626
00:28:58,337 --> 00:29:01,040
$500.

627
00:29:05,110 --> 00:29:06,712
WOULD YOU STOP
SUCKING YOUR THUMB?

628
00:29:06,745 --> 00:29:10,115
OOPS.

629
00:29:10,148 --> 00:29:12,185
WHAT ARE YOU GOING TO DO?

630
00:29:12,218 --> 00:29:13,452
I'LL GO TO JAIL.

631
00:29:13,485 --> 00:29:14,753
NOW, WHILE YOU ARE IN JAIL,

632
00:29:14,787 --> 00:29:16,288
I FORECLOSE ON THE MORTGAGE,

633
00:29:16,322 --> 00:29:18,525
AND I BANKRUPT YOU.

634
00:29:18,558 --> 00:29:20,260
- NEAT.
- WELL, THEN I'M NOT GONNA BE

635
00:29:20,293 --> 00:29:22,095
COMMUNITY CHEST ANYMORE.

636
00:29:24,530 --> 00:29:27,633
THAT LEAVES YOU
19,000 SHORT.

637
00:29:27,667 --> 00:29:30,403
WOW, NICE POCKET CALCULATOR.

638
00:29:30,437 --> 00:29:32,005
YEAH, IF YOU'RE A KANGAROO.

639
00:29:32,038 --> 00:29:34,107
AND DON'T FORGET
THE INTEREST.

640
00:29:34,140 --> 00:29:36,275
- I'M NOT INTERESTED
IN INTEREST.
- [DOORBELL RINGS]

641
00:29:36,308 --> 00:29:39,645
HMM. THAT WOULD BE HARRY
WITH OUR GUEST.

642
00:29:43,348 --> 00:29:44,650
DO YOU BATHE?

643
00:29:44,683 --> 00:29:46,418
FOURTH FLOOR,
TYRANNICAL TYCOONS.

644
00:29:46,452 --> 00:29:48,120
LOOSE WOMEN.

645
00:29:50,990 --> 00:29:53,527
WORKS EVERY TIME.

646
00:29:56,963 --> 00:29:58,932
DON'T ANYONE TALK.

647
00:30:05,538 --> 00:30:07,273
OH, SCOTCH.

648
00:30:07,307 --> 00:30:09,108
NOW, WHY DIDN'T YOU SAY SO?

649
00:30:09,142 --> 00:30:11,510
OH, I WAS CONCENTRATING
ON MY LINES.

650
00:30:11,543 --> 00:30:13,178
--PLAY WITH GUNS
ON THE SURFACE FLOOR.

651
00:30:13,212 --> 00:30:15,682
ONE SHOT, AND WE'D ALL
HAVE BEEN BREATHING EMPTY SPACE.

652
00:30:15,715 --> 00:30:18,183
SO THAT'S WHY YOU DIDN'T
TRY TO TAKE IT OFF ME UP THERE.

653
00:30:18,217 --> 00:30:19,852
WELL, THERE HAD TO BE
A REASON, DIDN'T THERE?

654
00:30:19,885 --> 00:30:22,055
NOT NECESSARILY, SOMETIMES
PEOPLE TAKE IT FOR NO REASON.

655
00:30:22,088 --> 00:30:25,692
OH, YOUR REPUTATION DIDN'T
EXAGGERATE, MR. KEMP.

656
00:30:25,725 --> 00:30:29,062
PERHAPS I SHOULD APOLOGIZE
FOR SENDING A MAN LIKE HARRY--

657
00:30:29,095 --> 00:30:31,063
NO, I'M JUST WILD
ABOUT HARRY.

658
00:30:31,097 --> 00:30:33,567
--FIRST MAN ON MARS.

659
00:30:33,600 --> 00:30:37,003
IS THAT HIM?

660
00:30:37,037 --> 00:30:39,338
SWEETENER?

661
00:30:39,372 --> 00:30:41,307
A LONG TIME AGO.

662
00:30:41,340 --> 00:30:43,810
AND NOW YOU'RE FLYING
A TEN-YEAR-OLD SPACE FERRY

663
00:30:43,843 --> 00:30:47,380
AND SALVAGING DEAD SATELLITES
TO SELL TO THE JUNKYARDS.

664
00:30:47,413 --> 00:30:49,815
DON'T TALK ABOUT SARAH
THAT WAY.

665
00:30:49,848 --> 00:30:51,317
--HARDLY.

666
00:30:51,350 --> 00:30:53,052
WILL YOU STOP FIDDLING
WITH THAT THING?

667
00:30:53,085 --> 00:30:55,555
- EH.
- BUT I'VE NEVER
BEEN TO SWITZERLAND.

668
00:30:55,588 --> 00:30:58,625
WELL, THE ONLY THING
WORTH SEEING ARE THE BANKS.

669
00:30:58,658 --> 00:31:00,860
GRR.

670
00:31:00,893 --> 00:31:03,528
I THINK YOU KNEW
OTTO VON BECK.

671
00:31:03,562 --> 00:31:04,763
AN OTTO ON THE SURFACE
OF THE MOON?

672
00:31:04,797 --> 00:31:06,098
IT'LL NEVER WORK.

673
00:31:06,132 --> 00:31:07,533
AND I BELIEVE YOU ARE
THE ONLY OTHER PILOT

674
00:31:07,567 --> 00:31:10,670
ON THE MOON
WITH A SHIP FOR CHARTER.

675
00:31:10,703 --> 00:31:14,673
OTTO WAS GOING
TO DO A LITTLE JOB FOR ME.

676
00:31:14,707 --> 00:31:16,242
NOW.

677
00:31:16,275 --> 00:31:17,943
NOW?

678
00:31:17,977 --> 00:31:20,212
- NOW?
- DO YOU KNOW
ASTEROIDS, MR. KEMP?

679
00:31:20,245 --> 00:31:22,315
- SURE, I HAVE ATARI.
- THE REMAINS OF A PLANET

680
00:31:22,348 --> 00:31:24,883
WHICH EXPLODED
OR WAS NEVER FORMED.

681
00:31:24,917 --> 00:31:26,485
SOME OF THEM GRAINS OF DUST,

682
00:31:26,518 --> 00:31:28,822
SOME THE SIZE
OF SMALL MOONS.

683
00:31:28,855 --> 00:31:31,890
AND EVERYTHING IN BETWEEN.
HUNDREDS OF--

684
00:31:31,923 --> 00:31:33,727
YOU'RE MAKING A SPECTACLE
OUT OF YOURSELF.

685
00:31:33,760 --> 00:31:35,362
SORRY.

686
00:31:35,395 --> 00:31:37,530
DOESN'T HE LOOK LIKE
THE HEAD OF K.A.O.S?

687
00:31:37,563 --> 00:31:38,965
YEAH, I WAS JUST
THINKING THAT.

688
00:31:38,998 --> 00:31:40,633
SOME NEVER NAMED,
NEVER CHARTED.

689
00:31:40,667 --> 00:31:42,168
BERNIE KOPPEL?

690
00:31:42,202 --> 00:31:44,937
THE ORPHANS OF
THE SOLAR SYSTEM, MR. KEMP.

691
00:31:44,970 --> 00:31:48,407
THE GUY FROM MAD GIRL.

692
00:31:48,440 --> 00:31:49,975
IS THAT HOW IT WORKS?

693
00:31:50,008 --> 00:31:52,312
YOU CAN'T SET UP
A MINE ON AN ASTEROID.

694
00:31:52,345 --> 00:31:54,347
COST OF FLYING
THE EQUIPMENT UP.

695
00:31:54,380 --> 00:31:56,715
THE SUPPLIES,
BRINGING THE ORE BACK.

696
00:31:56,748 --> 00:31:58,317
IT NEVER PAYS.

697
00:31:58,350 --> 00:32:00,252
NOT MINE IT, MR. KEMP.

698
00:32:00,285 --> 00:32:02,755
LAND IT ON THE MOON.

699
00:32:02,788 --> 00:32:04,823
LAND IT?

700
00:32:04,857 --> 00:32:06,125
YOU MEAN CRASH IT,
AND THAT'S

701
00:32:06,158 --> 00:32:07,793
AGAINST THE LAW
IN A BIG WAY.

702
00:32:07,827 --> 00:32:09,895
HE'S RIGHT,
JUST ASK JOHN LANDIS.

703
00:32:09,928 --> 00:32:13,098
--PILOT MIGHT
DROP IT ON MOON CITY.

704
00:32:15,333 --> 00:32:17,937
WELL, WE DON'T
DO THINGS THAT WAY.

705
00:32:17,970 --> 00:32:19,272
YOU WOULD HAVE THE RESULTS

706
00:32:19,305 --> 00:32:22,208
OF TWO YEARS' RESEARCH
TO HELP YOU.

707
00:32:22,242 --> 00:32:24,743
- WE WOULD--
- GOOD LORD, HE'S UGLY.

708
00:32:24,777 --> 00:32:26,745
--EXPERIENCED
PILOT ON THE MOON.

709
00:32:26,778 --> 00:32:28,313
HE'S SO IMMENSE.

710
00:32:28,347 --> 00:32:31,517
SO WHAT'S SO SPECIAL
ABOUT ONE ASTEROID?

711
00:32:31,550 --> 00:32:34,053
IT'S WORTH BONUS POINTS.
YOU GO ON TO THE NEXT SCREEN.

712
00:32:34,087 --> 00:32:36,788
--WHEN YOU GET THERE,
SO I MAY AS WELL TELL YOU NOW.

713
00:32:39,092 --> 00:32:41,027
WHITSUN.

714
00:32:44,397 --> 00:32:47,333
I DON'T EVEN KNOW MY NAME.

715
00:32:47,367 --> 00:32:49,902
TOO SMALL TO HAVE
EITHER A NAME OR A NUMBER.

716
00:32:49,935 --> 00:32:52,438
THE ASTEROID WAS
FIRST PHOTOGRAPHED IN 1998

717
00:32:52,472 --> 00:32:54,607
WHEN IT HAPPENED TO PASS
CLOSE TO THE EARTH.

718
00:32:54,640 --> 00:32:57,577
BUT IT WAS NEVER
INVESTIGATED OR PLOTTED.

719
00:32:57,610 --> 00:33:00,613
UNTIL TWO YEARS AGO.

720
00:33:00,647 --> 00:33:02,415
THIS FILM WAS TAKEN
BY MR. HUBBARD'S

721
00:33:02,448 --> 00:33:03,682
ASTRONOMICAL DIVISION.

722
00:33:03,715 --> 00:33:05,818
I'M SORRY,
THAT'S MY GALLSTONE.

723
00:33:05,852 --> 00:33:07,420
60 FEET BY 30 BY 30,

724
00:33:07,453 --> 00:33:10,355
ESTIMATED MASS,
APPROXIMATELY 6,000 TONS.

725
00:33:10,388 --> 00:33:12,325
HEAVY.

726
00:33:12,358 --> 00:33:14,160
THIS IS ME PLAYING BREAKOUT.

727
00:33:14,193 --> 00:33:17,263
DO YOU READ SPECTROGRAMS,
MR. KEMP?

728
00:33:17,297 --> 00:33:20,633
SOME OF THE EASY ONES.

729
00:33:20,667 --> 00:33:23,002
THIS LOOKS LIKE ALUMINUM.

730
00:33:23,035 --> 00:33:24,803
THAT'S VERY GOOD.

731
00:33:24,837 --> 00:33:27,607
IT'S QUITE SIMILAR
TO ALUMINUM.

732
00:33:27,640 --> 00:33:30,342
- BUT AN ALUMINUM--
- IS THAT RICHARD KIEL'S
STUPIDER BROTHER?

733
00:33:30,375 --> 00:33:32,078
--THE HEART
OF AN EXPLODING PLANET

734
00:33:32,112 --> 00:33:35,347
HUNDREDS OF MILLIONS
OF YEARS AGO.

735
00:33:35,380 --> 00:33:37,350
WHAT IS THE NAME AGAIN,
WHITSUN?

736
00:33:37,383 --> 00:33:38,885
A CERAMIC CRYSTALLINE FORM

737
00:33:38,918 --> 00:33:40,653
OF CORUNDUM-ALUMINUM OXIDE.

738
00:33:40,687 --> 00:33:44,157
OR SOMETHING LIKE THAT.

739
00:33:44,190 --> 00:33:47,193
SAPPHIRE, MR. KEMP.

740
00:33:47,227 --> 00:33:48,895
I LOVE SAPPHIRE.

741
00:33:48,928 --> 00:33:51,097
- SAPPHIRE.
- SHE'S GREAT.

742
00:33:51,130 --> 00:33:53,232
6,000 TONS

743
00:33:53,265 --> 00:33:55,735
OF GEMSTONE SAPPHIRE.

744
00:33:55,768 --> 00:33:57,035
OKAY.

745
00:33:57,068 --> 00:34:00,272
THAT'S WHAT'S SO SPECIAL
ABOUT THIS ASTEROID.

746
00:34:02,242 --> 00:34:04,577
WELL, THAT'S MY BIRTHSTONE.

747
00:34:04,610 --> 00:34:06,612
I'LL DO IT.

748
00:34:06,645 --> 00:34:08,247
WELL?

749
00:34:08,280 --> 00:34:10,783
SOUNDS LIKE A NICE,
PROFITABLE IDEA.

750
00:34:10,817 --> 00:34:12,952
BUT IT'S STILL
AGAINST THE LAW.

751
00:34:15,387 --> 00:34:17,657
SO'S YOUR FOREHEAD, THOUGH.

752
00:34:17,690 --> 00:34:20,993
WE UNDERSTAND THAT YOU'RE
ALREADY IN TROUBLE WITH THE LAW.

753
00:34:21,027 --> 00:34:22,262
- HUH?
- HUH?

754
00:34:22,295 --> 00:34:24,197
--THE BUREAU
WANTS TO GROUND YOU.

755
00:34:24,230 --> 00:34:26,432
OH, COME NOW, WHITSUN.

756
00:34:26,465 --> 00:34:28,400
THAT'S NO WAY
TO TREAT OUR GUEST.

757
00:34:28,433 --> 00:34:29,968
YEAH, HE'S TOO OLD
FOR GROUNDING.

758
00:34:30,002 --> 00:34:32,405
MR. KEMP MUST BE
ENTIRELY FREE

759
00:34:32,438 --> 00:34:33,772
TO MAKE UP HIS OWN MIND.

760
00:34:33,805 --> 00:34:35,273
WHICH IS GREAT FOR HIM.

761
00:34:35,307 --> 00:34:36,942
AND JUST SUPPOSE I FREELY

762
00:34:36,975 --> 00:34:38,443
MAKE UP MY MIND TO COME IN.

763
00:34:38,477 --> 00:34:39,812
WHAT DO I GET OUT OF IT?

764
00:34:39,845 --> 00:34:43,515
DON PARDO, SHOW HIM
WHAT HE'LL WIN.

765
00:34:43,548 --> 00:34:46,385
A BRAND NEW SPACE FERRY.

766
00:34:46,418 --> 00:34:48,387
- HELLO.
- COULD COME IN HANDY.

767
00:34:48,420 --> 00:34:52,258
ORDER ONE TOMORROW.

768
00:34:52,292 --> 00:34:53,860
BUT AT THAT PRICE,
YOU COULD GET YOUR OWN SHIP.

769
00:34:53,893 --> 00:34:55,995
GET YOUR OWN CREW.

770
00:34:56,028 --> 00:34:58,497
BUT NOT SECRETLY.

771
00:34:58,530 --> 00:35:00,833
YOU SEE, SOMEONE LIKE MYSELF

772
00:35:00,867 --> 00:35:03,435
STARTS TO OUTFIT
AN EXPEDITION INTO SPACE,

773
00:35:03,468 --> 00:35:05,605
WELL, IT ATTRACTS
QUESTIONS, SNOOPERS.

774
00:35:05,638 --> 00:35:07,173
SNOOPERS AND BLABBERS!

775
00:35:07,207 --> 00:35:10,242
INVESTIGATIONS
FROM THE BUREAU.

776
00:35:10,275 --> 00:35:11,677
BUT YOU.

777
00:35:11,710 --> 00:35:15,380
YOU JUST POP OFF INTO SPACE
ON ONE OF YOUR--

778
00:35:15,413 --> 00:35:16,715
HEY!

779
00:35:16,748 --> 00:35:18,852
--NO QUESTIONS ASKED.

780
00:35:18,885 --> 00:35:21,220
AND A FEW DAYS LATER,

781
00:35:21,253 --> 00:35:23,957
AN ASTEROID JUST HAPPENS

782
00:35:23,990 --> 00:35:26,492
TO LAND ON THE FAR SIDE
OF THE MOON.

783
00:35:26,525 --> 00:35:29,628
AND SINCE NOBODY'S
BOTHERED TO PLOT IT,

784
00:35:29,662 --> 00:35:32,698
- NOBODY CAN SAY THAT--
- OH, THANK YOU, VIDAL SASSOON.

785
00:35:32,732 --> 00:35:35,300
I DON'T LOOK GOOD,
AND YOU DON'T LOOK GOOD.

786
00:35:46,212 --> 00:35:48,547
FLIGHT A-E-3
WILL LIFT OFF--

787
00:35:48,580 --> 00:35:50,382
HEY, HER BOOTS
ARE EATING HER.

788
00:35:50,415 --> 00:35:52,150
WILL PASSENGERS PLEASE

789
00:35:52,183 --> 00:35:53,785
IT'S HER TRIBUTE
TO BRONCO NAGURSKI.

790
00:35:53,818 --> 00:35:55,087
- YOU'RE LEAVING AGAIN
PRETTY QUICKLY.
- SHE WAS IN

791
00:35:55,120 --> 00:35:57,055
YARDS OF LEATHER, I THINK.

792
00:35:57,088 --> 00:36:00,158
US UN-SALARIED WORKERS
HAVE TO KEEP WORKING.

793
00:36:00,192 --> 00:36:01,493
- [ALL] OUCH.
- THAT LOOKS LIKE

794
00:36:01,527 --> 00:36:03,795
QUITE A HEAVY LOAD
YOU HAVE THERE.

795
00:36:03,828 --> 00:36:05,230
WHAT IS IT?

796
00:36:05,263 --> 00:36:07,233
OH, SOME EXPERIMENTAL
PROPULSION EQUIPMENT

797
00:36:07,267 --> 00:36:09,468
I WANT TO TEST IN SPACE.

798
00:36:09,502 --> 00:36:12,203
SURE, DID YOU GET IT FROM
A HONEYMOON CATALOGUE?

799
00:36:12,237 --> 00:36:15,273
SECTION 47-C, PARAGRAPH ONE.

800
00:36:15,307 --> 00:36:18,945
NO INFORMATION ABOUT COMMERCIAL
OR INDUSTRIAL SECRETS

801
00:36:18,978 --> 00:36:20,813
NEED BE DISCLOSED
WITHOUT THE AUTHORITY

802
00:36:20,847 --> 00:36:23,348
OF THE MOON COURT WARRANT.

803
00:36:23,382 --> 00:36:25,117
BUT I'M PARAPHRASING,
OF COURSE.

804
00:36:25,150 --> 00:36:26,985
THERE'S MORE THAN ONE WAY
TO SKIN A CAT.

805
00:36:27,018 --> 00:36:29,022
EVERYONE SAYS THAT, BUT NO ONE
EVER TELLS ME THE OTHER WAY.

806
00:36:29,055 --> 00:36:32,023
GOOD LUCK, BILL.

807
00:36:33,125 --> 00:36:34,927
YOU HAVE TO MARRY
THAT GIRL, BILL.

808
00:36:34,960 --> 00:36:36,195
WHAT DO YOU MEAN, "HAVE TO"?

809
00:36:36,228 --> 00:36:39,332
IT MIGHT BE BETTER THAN
HER THROW YOU IN JAIL.

810
00:36:39,365 --> 00:36:41,267
LOOKS LIKE THESE GUYS
GOT SUITED UP

811
00:36:41,300 --> 00:36:42,735
FOR A FOOSBALL GAME.

812
00:36:42,768 --> 00:36:44,270
--MARRY HER ANYWAY.

813
00:36:44,303 --> 00:36:45,537
YOU GOTTA MARRY HER, BILL.

814
00:36:45,570 --> 00:36:47,740
SHE'S GOT
THE WEDDING BELL BLUES.

815
00:36:47,773 --> 00:36:51,510
UP UP AND AWAY.

816
00:36:51,543 --> 00:36:53,278
I'LL JUST THROW THIS
BACK HERE.

817
00:36:55,882 --> 00:36:57,983
AH, I'M INTRINSICALLY EVIL.

818
00:36:58,017 --> 00:37:00,653
AND I'VE GOT A NEW JOGGING SUIT
I'M SHOWING OFF.

819
00:37:00,687 --> 00:37:03,688
--OF EARTH EXPRESS.

820
00:37:03,722 --> 00:37:05,390
WE UNDERSTAND IT'S A SIGHT

821
00:37:05,423 --> 00:37:08,527
NO TOURIST SHOULD MISS.

822
00:37:08,560 --> 00:37:10,495
WHEN WOULD YOU
BE READY TO LIFT-OFF?

823
00:37:10,528 --> 00:37:13,832
YES, THIS TIME,
WE CAN PAY THE BILL, OKAY?

824
00:37:13,865 --> 00:37:17,470
[ALL] OKAY, MEESTER FAWLTY.

825
00:37:17,503 --> 00:37:19,272
THE PUMP-VALVE
ON NUMBER TWO.

826
00:37:19,305 --> 00:37:22,040
WE ARE READY NOW.

827
00:37:22,073 --> 00:37:23,408
PASSENGERS?

828
00:37:23,442 --> 00:37:25,510
HE'S GOT A COMPUTER
IN THAT BRIEFCASE.

829
00:37:25,543 --> 00:37:26,778
- AND HE'S NOT AFRAID
TO USE IT.
- DUCK!

830
00:37:26,812 --> 00:37:28,213
--WITH THE HEAVY WORK.

831
00:37:28,247 --> 00:37:31,817
I'LL GET OVER THERE.

832
00:37:31,850 --> 00:37:33,718
THAT'S MR. KAMINSKI,
ISN'T IT?

833
00:37:33,752 --> 00:37:35,888
YOUR ENGINEER?

834
00:37:35,922 --> 00:37:37,757
WHAT NATIONALITY IS HE?

835
00:37:37,790 --> 00:37:40,458
HE'S FROM BARCELONA.

836
00:37:40,492 --> 00:37:42,227
THAT WASN'T QUITE
WHAT I ASKED.

837
00:37:42,260 --> 00:37:44,297
WE'RE ALL FOREIGNERS
UP HERE.

838
00:37:44,330 --> 00:37:46,932
SOME MORE THAN OTHERS.

839
00:37:46,965 --> 00:37:48,800
READY TO GO?

840
00:37:48,833 --> 00:37:50,102
WITHOUT THE PISTOL, PLEASE.

841
00:37:50,135 --> 00:37:52,137
YOU DON'T TAKE THIS
OFF ME TWICE.

842
00:37:52,170 --> 00:37:53,472
THEN THE TRIP'S OFF.
IF THAT THING

843
00:37:53,505 --> 00:37:54,840
GOES OFF IN THE SHIP,
WE'D NEVER GET BACK

844
00:37:54,873 --> 00:37:57,710
TO EXPLAIN WHY.

845
00:37:57,743 --> 00:37:59,812
GIVE IT TO ME, HARRY.

846
00:38:01,080 --> 00:38:03,015
BUT I FEEL TOTALLY NAKED
WITHOUT IT.

847
00:38:03,048 --> 00:38:06,085
IT'S MY ONLY ACCESSORY.

848
00:38:06,118 --> 00:38:09,122
GIVE HIM THE PEARL
EARRINGS TOO, HARRY.

849
00:38:09,155 --> 00:38:12,023
LET'S HOPE WE ALL HAVE
A PROFITABLE TRIP.

850
00:38:12,057 --> 00:38:14,960
LET YOU KNOW
IN ABOUT FOUR DAYS.

851
00:38:14,993 --> 00:38:17,028
POW, SLUGGO.

852
00:38:24,437 --> 00:38:27,773
SHUT UP.

853
00:38:27,807 --> 00:38:29,075
THAT'S THE COFFEE.
THAT SHOULD BE READY

854
00:38:29,108 --> 00:38:31,043
IN A MINUTE OR TWO.

855
00:38:33,978 --> 00:38:36,482
OKAY, WE'RE PRESSURIZED.
YOU CAN TAKE YOUR HELMETS OFF.

856
00:38:36,515 --> 00:38:38,183
JUST KIDDING.

857
00:38:38,217 --> 00:38:40,052
WHITSUN,
I WANT THE MAIN COURSE

858
00:38:40,085 --> 00:38:43,155
EXACTLY 90 SECONDS
AFTER BLASTOFF.

859
00:38:43,188 --> 00:38:45,523
YOU ARE A HUNGRY LITTLE GUY.

860
00:38:45,557 --> 00:38:48,027
ARE WE LETTING HIM NAVIGATE?

861
00:38:48,060 --> 00:38:50,462
HE'S GOT A BETTER COMPUTER
THAN WE HAVE.

862
00:38:50,495 --> 00:38:52,532
- CAN HE USE IT?
- HE FIGURES THAT COUNTING

863
00:38:52,565 --> 00:38:54,100
MILES PER HOUR
ISN'T SO DIFFERENT

864
00:38:54,133 --> 00:38:57,168
THAN DOLLARS PER SECOND.

865
00:38:57,202 --> 00:38:58,770
AS LONG AS HE REMEMBERS
YOU CAN'T GET

866
00:38:58,803 --> 00:39:00,472
MILES PER HOUR ON CREDIT.

867
00:39:00,505 --> 00:39:03,642
I LOVE YOUR WRY, NAIVE WIT,
MY EUROPEAN FRIEND.

868
00:39:03,675 --> 00:39:05,243
--ZERO TWO.

869
00:39:05,277 --> 00:39:08,613
REQUEST TAKEOFF CLEARANCE.

870
00:39:08,647 --> 00:39:10,415
ROUND TRIP, NO LANDING AWAY,

871
00:39:10,448 --> 00:39:12,918
AS USUAL.

872
00:39:12,952 --> 00:39:14,587
FIRST CLASS OR COACH?

873
00:39:14,620 --> 00:39:16,255
SMOKING OR NON?

874
00:39:19,892 --> 00:39:22,193
ZERO TWO, YOU'RE CLEAR.

875
00:39:22,227 --> 00:39:24,363
MARS EXPRESS
DUE IN 20 MINUTES.

876
00:39:24,397 --> 00:39:25,730
BUT ARE WE CLEAR?

877
00:39:25,763 --> 00:39:27,433
ZERO TWO.

878
00:39:27,467 --> 00:39:29,835
I'LL TRY TO MISS HIM. OUT.

879
00:39:29,868 --> 00:39:33,138
THEY REALLY DID A GREAT JOB
OF ANTIQUING THAT SHIP.

880
00:39:33,172 --> 00:39:34,973
SLAP IN THE ROAD TAPE, DUDE,

881
00:39:35,007 --> 00:39:37,743
AND GET THE J.D.
FROM UNDER THE SEAT.

882
00:39:40,778 --> 00:39:43,215
HEY, MELON-HEAD,
GET OFF MY FOOT.

883
00:39:49,087 --> 00:39:50,790
TRAVELS WITH
ROLLER DERBY QUEENS.

884
00:39:50,823 --> 00:39:52,725
IT'S GREAT.

885
00:39:52,758 --> 00:39:54,793
OH, IT'S ESTHER WILLIAMS.

886
00:39:54,827 --> 00:39:56,028
SHE'S IN A FISH BOWL.

887
00:39:56,062 --> 00:39:58,463
GOT THAT COURSE YET,
WHITSUN?

888
00:39:58,497 --> 00:39:59,732
RELATIVE TO THE ELLIPTIC,

889
00:39:59,765 --> 00:40:01,867
I WANT A COURSE
OF ALPHA 351,

890
00:40:01,900 --> 00:40:05,537
METER 179,
SPEED 17,500.

891
00:40:05,570 --> 00:40:06,972
THEN A SHERRY, MEDIUM DRY.

892
00:40:07,005 --> 00:40:08,373
--AS IF HE KNOWS.

893
00:40:08,407 --> 00:40:11,277
IT DOES, DOESN'T IT?

894
00:40:11,310 --> 00:40:14,680
- DO YOU THINK HE MEANS--
- WOOP WOOP! WOOP WOOP!

895
00:40:14,713 --> 00:40:16,815
OH, MORE OR LESS, I SUPPOSE.

896
00:40:19,452 --> 00:40:21,920
I HOPE IT'S NOT
TOO DIFFICULT FOR YOU.

897
00:40:21,953 --> 00:40:23,755
NOT AT ALL, MR. WHITSUN.

898
00:40:23,788 --> 00:40:25,290
WELL, IF YOU HAVE IT
ON BETA-GRAPH,

899
00:40:25,323 --> 00:40:27,693
I HOPE I CAN MAKE
THE SITUATION CLEAR TO YOU.

900
00:40:27,727 --> 00:40:31,063
IT'S OVER THERE.

901
00:40:31,097 --> 00:40:33,932
WELL, IT'S NOT NEW,
BUT I THINK IT WORKS.

902
00:40:33,965 --> 00:40:36,702
ARE WE TALKING ABOUT
THE SAME THING HERE?

903
00:40:40,305 --> 00:40:43,375
WOULD YOU TURN OFF
"PETER AND THE WOLF," PLEASE?

904
00:40:49,815 --> 00:40:52,885
THE EARTH, THE MOON
REVOLVING AROUND IT.

905
00:40:52,918 --> 00:40:55,020
NOW, THIS YEAR, THIS WEEK,

906
00:40:55,053 --> 00:40:57,557
THE ASTEROID IS MAKING
ITS CLOSEST APPROACH TO THE MOON

907
00:40:57,590 --> 00:41:00,692
SINCE 1998 ON THIS COURSE.

908
00:41:00,725 --> 00:41:02,595
IT'S THE CLOSEST APPROACH
SINCE I GREW

909
00:41:02,628 --> 00:41:04,128
MY BUSHY-WUSHY SIDEBURNS.

910
00:41:04,162 --> 00:41:07,298
--ADJUST AND ADJUST HERE.

911
00:41:07,332 --> 00:41:08,533
45 HOURS FROM NOW.

912
00:41:08,567 --> 00:41:10,135
THE IMPORTANCE
OF BEING EARNEST.

913
00:41:10,168 --> 00:41:11,903
THAT'S WHERE I SAW HIM.

914
00:41:11,937 --> 00:41:13,472
A GENTLEMAN CALLER,
ACTUALLY,

915
00:41:13,505 --> 00:41:15,307
BUT THESE ROCKETS,
AS I WAS SAYING.

916
00:41:15,340 --> 00:41:17,710
--WILL CHANGE TO THIS ORBIT.

917
00:41:19,378 --> 00:41:20,947
YOU WILL OBSERVE
THAT ITS SPEED

918
00:41:20,980 --> 00:41:22,915
RELATIVE TO THE MOON
IS QUITE SLOW.

919
00:41:22,948 --> 00:41:25,150
AND THAT IT IS ONLY VISIBLE
FROM FAR SIDE.

920
00:41:25,183 --> 00:41:28,287
THE RADAR STATIONS
ON NEAR SIDE CANNOT SEE IT.

921
00:41:28,320 --> 00:41:29,955
YOU APPRECIATE
THE IMPORTANCE OF THIS.

922
00:41:29,988 --> 00:41:31,457
WELL, IF THEY COULD,
WE'D BE IN JAIL

923
00:41:31,490 --> 00:41:33,558
- THE MOMENT WE GOT BACK.
- EXACTLY.

924
00:41:33,592 --> 00:41:35,227
HAVE YOU EVER BEEN IN JAIL?

925
00:41:35,260 --> 00:41:36,628
YOU'D LIKE IT QUITE A LOT.

926
00:41:36,662 --> 00:41:37,997
--THE ASTEROID WILL
HAVE COME TO WITHIN

927
00:41:38,030 --> 00:41:39,298
10,000 MILES OF THE MOON.

928
00:41:39,332 --> 00:41:41,633
WE SHALL RETURN TO IT,
TAKE NEW MEASUREMENTS,

929
00:41:41,667 --> 00:41:43,835
RESET THE ENGINES,
AND FIRE THEM AGAIN.

930
00:41:43,868 --> 00:41:45,537
- AM I BORING YOU?
- THE ASTEROID LANDS

931
00:41:45,570 --> 00:41:47,038
ON THE MOON.

932
00:41:47,072 --> 00:41:49,875
CRUNCH. I GET THE PICTURE.

933
00:41:49,908 --> 00:41:52,310
[INDISTINCT]...
FROM FAR SIDE FIVE!

934
00:41:52,343 --> 00:41:53,512
HUH?

935
00:41:53,545 --> 00:41:55,948
WELL, I'M GLAD THEY KNOW
WHAT SHE SAID.

936
00:41:58,750 --> 00:42:00,018
HEY, THERE'S A SELL
AT PENNEY'S.

937
00:42:00,052 --> 00:42:02,253
HIDE THE GARNISHES, QUICK!

938
00:42:02,287 --> 00:42:05,457
ALL THE KNICK-KNACKS
GOTTA BE MOVED.

939
00:42:09,695 --> 00:42:11,630
SURE ARE A SHINY BUNCH.

940
00:42:11,663 --> 00:42:13,498
HEY, IT'S RANDOLPH MANTOOTH.

941
00:42:13,532 --> 00:42:16,968
SORRY, I THOUGHT WERE--

942
00:42:19,203 --> 00:42:20,772
IS THAT RAYON
THEY'RE WEARING?

943
00:42:20,805 --> 00:42:22,107
NAUGAHYDE!

944
00:42:22,140 --> 00:42:25,077
HEY, IT'S HEE-HAW 1999.

945
00:42:28,213 --> 00:42:30,182
PRETTY SOON THEY'LL GET
THOSE BIG FOAM

946
00:42:30,215 --> 00:42:32,183
"WE'RE NUMBER ONE" HANDS.

947
00:42:38,723 --> 00:42:40,125
ANYBODY KNOW
WHERE A GUY CAN GET

948
00:42:40,158 --> 00:42:41,927
SOME ARMOR-ALL AROUND HERE?

949
00:42:41,960 --> 00:42:44,095
HEY, IT'S THE SAME DANCE
WITH DIFFERENT HATS,

950
00:42:44,128 --> 00:42:46,465
BUT IT'S A COMPLETELY
DIFFERENT EXPERIENCE.

951
00:42:49,735 --> 00:42:51,370
EXCUSE ME, MA'AM.

952
00:42:51,403 --> 00:42:53,005
SOMEONE DIDN'T
FINISH YOUR HAIRCUT.

953
00:42:53,038 --> 00:42:55,573
OH MY. I'M IN LOVE.

954
00:42:55,607 --> 00:42:57,608
EXCUSE ME AGAIN,
BUT DO YOU KNOW

955
00:42:57,642 --> 00:42:58,877
MR. WALLACE TAPLIN?

956
00:42:58,910 --> 00:43:00,712
WALLY? YES, I KNOW WALLY.

957
00:43:00,745 --> 00:43:01,780
SEEMS LIKE
THE BENNY HILL SHOW.

958
00:43:01,813 --> 00:43:03,415
NOT WELL ENOUGH, APPARENTLY.

959
00:43:03,448 --> 00:43:04,883
ARE YOU A FRIEND OF HIS?

960
00:43:04,917 --> 00:43:07,653
- NO, I'M HIS SISTER.
- THAT'S A GREAT RELIEF.

961
00:43:07,687 --> 00:43:09,187
WAS HE ON THIS CONVOY?

962
00:43:09,220 --> 00:43:10,455
WELL, IF HE WAS,
I DIDN'T SEE HIM.

963
00:43:10,488 --> 00:43:12,457
WELL, WHAT WAS HIS HANDLE?

964
00:43:12,490 --> 00:43:13,925
--SIT DOWN, TAKE A DRINK?

965
00:43:13,958 --> 00:43:15,260
YES, YES, JOIN US. COME ON.

966
00:43:15,293 --> 00:43:17,228
THREE MORE
ROCKET FUELS, PLEASE.

967
00:43:17,262 --> 00:43:19,163
AND AN AIR FRESHENER.
YOU KNOW, THEIR ROCKET FUEL

968
00:43:19,197 --> 00:43:20,565
CONTAINS NO ETHANOL.

969
00:43:20,598 --> 00:43:22,935
--HAVEN'T SEEN WALLY IN,
OH, MAYBE FOUR MONTHS.

970
00:43:22,968 --> 00:43:25,403
HAND-CHECK.

971
00:43:25,437 --> 00:43:26,838
- YOU'RE JUST UP FROM EARTH.
- YEAH.

972
00:43:26,872 --> 00:43:28,540
HAVE YOU TRIED RADIOING HIM?
OF COURSE, YOU CAN'T.

973
00:43:28,573 --> 00:43:30,642
THAT SATELLITE'S OUT,
ISN'T IT?

974
00:43:30,675 --> 00:43:33,212
YOU'D THINK THEY'D HAVE
DECENT COMMUNICATIONS
HERE ON THE MOON.

975
00:43:33,245 --> 00:43:36,715
NO GOVERNMENT EVER SPENT
ONE DOLLAR TILL THEY LOST FIVE.

976
00:43:36,748 --> 00:43:40,252
- YEAH, FIVE--
- HEY, IT'S BUFFALO BOB!

977
00:43:40,285 --> 00:43:41,720
--WAY WE ARE
AROUND THE BACK THERE.

978
00:43:41,753 --> 00:43:43,422
WHY ARE THEY ALL ENGLISH?

979
00:43:43,455 --> 00:43:44,890
CHEESE IT,
IT'S THE GATOR BABE!

980
00:43:44,923 --> 00:43:46,892
'CAUSE THEY'RE
THE ONLY ONES PALE ENOUGH

981
00:43:46,925 --> 00:43:50,328
TO SIMULATE BEING
OUT OF THE DIRECT SUNLIGHT.

982
00:43:52,030 --> 00:43:53,465
ANY NEWS, MS. TAPLIN?

983
00:43:53,498 --> 00:43:54,833
SOMETHING MUST HAVE
HAPPENED TO HIM.

984
00:43:54,867 --> 00:43:56,568
NOBODY'S SEEN HIM
FOR MONTHS.

985
00:43:56,602 --> 00:43:58,570
WELL, HE MAY HAVE
JUST MISSED THE CONVOY.

986
00:43:58,603 --> 00:44:00,205
I LOVE THAT WOMAN.

987
00:44:00,238 --> 00:44:01,540
OUT AT FAR SIDE FIVE.

988
00:44:01,573 --> 00:44:03,208
YES, THAT'S--
OH, WE'D BETTER GO.

989
00:44:03,242 --> 00:44:05,577
- I'VE NEVER KNOWN--
- COME ON, YOU GUYS.

990
00:44:05,610 --> 00:44:07,512
I WANNA STAY
AND WATCH MY BABE.

991
00:44:07,545 --> 00:44:09,915
--WANT ANY HELP,
EXCEPT NOW.

992
00:44:18,357 --> 00:44:19,658
YOU KNOW, YOU GUYS,
I WAS JUST THINKING

993
00:44:19,692 --> 00:44:21,293
ABOUT THAT KIND OF DUMB
MOON-OPOLY JOKE

994
00:44:21,327 --> 00:44:23,228
THEY GOT IN THERE.
IT'S JUST A STUPID PUN,

995
00:44:23,262 --> 00:44:24,930
BUT, YOU KNOW,
IN THE FUTURE,

996
00:44:24,963 --> 00:44:27,767
THE GAMES WE PLAY NOW
ARE GONNA BE A LOT DIFFERENT

997
00:44:27,800 --> 00:44:29,468
WITH THE FUTURE ELEMENT
INVOLVED, YOU KNOW.

998
00:44:29,502 --> 00:44:31,570
LIKE TWISTER WILL PROBABLY

999
00:44:31,603 --> 00:44:33,905
BE PLAYED ON YOUR TONGUE.

1000
00:44:33,938 --> 00:44:37,542
UH, YEAH, AND NINTENDO
WOULD BE MOON-TENDO.

1001
00:44:37,575 --> 00:44:40,112
WITH THE SUPER LUNAR
MARIO BROTHERS.

1002
00:44:40,145 --> 00:44:41,913
- IT'S POSSIBLE.
- WELL, RISK IS RISKIER.

1003
00:44:41,947 --> 00:44:45,117
RIGHT, AND SORRY WILL SEEM
TO BE THE HARDEST GAME.

1004
00:44:45,150 --> 00:44:46,785
AND, UH, SAY YOU'RE
PLAYING CLUE,

1005
00:44:46,818 --> 00:44:48,953
AND THE ANSWER
MIGHT BE COLONEL MUSTARD

1006
00:44:48,987 --> 00:44:50,388
IN THE COMMAND MODULE

1007
00:44:50,422 --> 00:44:52,457
WITH LASER BOLOS.

1008
00:44:52,490 --> 00:44:54,392
'CAUSE IT'S A SPACESHIP.

1009
00:44:54,425 --> 00:44:56,060
PARCHEESI
WILL BE GREENCHEESI.

1010
00:44:56,093 --> 00:44:57,595
SKITTLE-BOWL
WILL BE THE SAME,

1011
00:44:57,628 --> 00:44:59,765
BUT IT WILL TAKE
EVEN LONGER TO SET UP

1012
00:44:59,798 --> 00:45:01,233
BECAUSE OF NO GRAVITY.

1013
00:45:01,267 --> 00:45:03,868
CHUTES AND LADDERS
IS REPLACED BY VACUUM TUBES,

1014
00:45:03,902 --> 00:45:05,637
YOU KNOW, LIKE ON THE JETSONS,
'CAUSE THAT'S THE ONLY WAY

1015
00:45:05,670 --> 00:45:06,905
THEY CAN GET AROUND
FROM PLACE TO PLACE.

1016
00:45:06,938 --> 00:45:08,440
CANDYLAND'S THE SAME,
BUT YOU SHOULD SEE

1017
00:45:08,473 --> 00:45:09,942
THE NEW FLAVORS THEY'VE GOT.

1018
00:45:09,975 --> 00:45:11,210
RIGHT.

1019
00:45:11,243 --> 00:45:13,412
KABOOM! IS CALLED
DON'T SMOKE ON THE SHIP

1020
00:45:13,445 --> 00:45:15,213
BECAUSE IT'S
AN OXYGEN-RICH ATMOSPHERE,

1021
00:45:15,247 --> 00:45:18,117
AND YOU COULD BLOW UP,
AND THAT WOULD BE...

1022
00:45:18,150 --> 00:45:19,852
- BAD.
- RIGHT, AND THEY WON'T
HAVE MICE,

1023
00:45:19,885 --> 00:45:21,953
BECAUSE THEY'LL NEED
TO USE THEM FOR RESEARCH.

1024
00:45:21,987 --> 00:45:24,388
- SO NO MOUSE TRAP. RIGHT.
- YOU KNOW, YOU CAN'T
PLAY MOUSE TRAP.

1025
00:45:24,422 --> 00:45:25,890
ETCH-A-SKETCH WILL
FINALLY BE ABLE TO DRAW

1026
00:45:25,923 --> 00:45:27,625
CURVED LINES, I BET.

1027
00:45:27,658 --> 00:45:30,328
SCRUPLES AREN'T AROUND ANYMORE
BECAUSE PEOPLE WON'T HAVE ANY.

1028
00:45:30,362 --> 00:45:32,998
TRIVIAL PURSUIT WILL BE
TRIVIAL MOON SUIT

1029
00:45:33,032 --> 00:45:34,767
YEAH, NOW WIN, LOSE, OR DRAW

1030
00:45:34,800 --> 00:45:36,668
IS CALLED
WIN, LOSE, AND DRAW OXYGEN.

1031
00:45:36,702 --> 00:45:38,003
RIGHT.

1032
00:45:38,037 --> 00:45:41,105
PASSWORD HAS BEEN REPLACED
BY GAMES HIGHER IN FIBER.

1033
00:45:41,138 --> 00:45:44,042
WELL, I GOT A GAME FORM MY PAST
THAT'S IN MY PRESENT,

1034
00:45:44,075 --> 00:45:46,145
AND I THINK WE'LL KEEP
GOING INTO THE FUTURE.

1035
00:45:46,178 --> 00:45:49,047
YOU KNOW HOW IT WORKS, GUYS,
IT'S ROCK 'EM SOCK 'EM ROBOTS.

1036
00:45:49,080 --> 00:45:51,683
[BOTS SCREAM]

1037
00:45:53,385 --> 00:45:55,853
ALL RIGHT, I KNOCKED
HIS BLOCK OFF.

1038
00:45:55,887 --> 00:45:57,588
BUT YOU CAN PUSH IT BACK DOWN,
AND IT'S--

1039
00:45:57,622 --> 00:45:59,758
WHOA, MOVIE SIGN!

1040
00:45:59,792 --> 00:46:02,327
LET'S GO!

1041
00:46:09,133 --> 00:46:11,303
THREE... TWO...

1042
00:46:11,337 --> 00:46:15,040
GIVE HER THE WORKS-- CUT!

1043
00:46:15,073 --> 00:46:16,708
DON'T ROCK 'EM SOCK 'EM US
ANY MORE.

1044
00:46:16,742 --> 00:46:18,577
- STOP IT.
- HEY, LET ME AT HIM.
LET ME AT HIM.

1045
00:46:18,610 --> 00:46:20,112
- COME ON, YOU GUYS.
- I'LL MURDER HIM.

1046
00:46:20,145 --> 00:46:21,880
BREAK IT UP.

1047
00:46:26,083 --> 00:46:29,053
A 6,000 TON JEWEL.

1048
00:46:29,087 --> 00:46:30,588
HOW WOULD YOU
LIKE TO MEET THE BROAD

1049
00:46:30,622 --> 00:46:31,890
WHO COULD HANG THAT
AROUND HER NECK?

1050
00:46:31,923 --> 00:46:34,893
UH, SHE'S PROBABLY
GOT A BOYFRIEND.

1051
00:46:46,905 --> 00:46:50,775
WHAT DO YOU THINK
OF BEING IN SPACE?

1052
00:46:52,010 --> 00:46:53,845
HEY, IT'S MAJOR KONG.

1053
00:46:53,878 --> 00:46:57,715
IS THAT WHAT THEY CALL
A CROTCH-ROCKET?

1054
00:46:57,748 --> 00:46:59,985
WOW, I NEVER KNEW

1055
00:47:00,018 --> 00:47:03,155
OUTER SPACE WAS SO WELL-LIT.

1056
00:47:17,102 --> 00:47:19,503
IN SPACE, NO ONE
CAN HEAR YOU YAWN.

1057
00:47:19,537 --> 00:47:21,205
--EXACTLY DO YOU
WANT THIS ATTACHED?

1058
00:47:21,238 --> 00:47:23,342
- ON THE CRADLE.
- TREAT IT GENTLY.

1059
00:47:23,375 --> 00:47:24,677
THIS IS NUMBER THREE.

1060
00:47:24,710 --> 00:47:26,378
THIS IS LIABLE TO GO OFF
EARLY AS LATE.

1061
00:47:26,412 --> 00:47:28,747
FASTEN YOUR SAFETY LINE,
HARRY.

1062
00:47:35,687 --> 00:47:38,857
I'LL GO DOWN AND GET THE LEADS
FROM THE OTHER ENGINES.

1063
00:47:42,995 --> 00:47:44,830
HEY, GET SOME TAPE
WHILE YOU'RE AT IT.

1064
00:47:44,863 --> 00:47:46,898
AND BRING ME BACK A SODA.

1065
00:47:46,932 --> 00:47:48,933
ANYTHING BUT MR. PIBB.

1066
00:47:55,307 --> 00:47:58,377
JOEL, ISN'T THAT THE SAME SHOT
DONE UPSIDE-DOWN?

1067
00:47:58,410 --> 00:47:59,978
WELL, KIND OF.
WHAT THEY DO IS

1068
00:48:00,012 --> 00:48:01,547
THEY TURN
THE CAMERA OVER TWICE,

1069
00:48:01,580 --> 00:48:04,717
AND THEY SHOOT IT BACKWARDS
AT HIGH-SPEED INTO A MIRROR.

1070
00:48:04,750 --> 00:48:07,585
OH. SEEMS LIKE IT'D BE EASIER
TO JUST SHOOT IT UPSIDE-DOWN.

1071
00:48:07,618 --> 00:48:09,788
YEAH, PROBABLY.

1072
00:48:22,167 --> 00:48:24,202
NOW, IF EACH ENGINE IS SET

1073
00:48:24,235 --> 00:48:26,270
FOR EXACTLY...

1074
00:48:26,303 --> 00:48:28,873
100,000 POUNDS THRUST,

1075
00:48:28,907 --> 00:48:31,042
- THEN--
- HEY, IT'S A MEAT SCALE.

1076
00:48:31,075 --> 00:48:33,912
MAYBE HE'S TRYING
TO PRICE THAT BOULDER.

1077
00:48:33,945 --> 00:48:35,513
LOOKS PRETTY WELL MARBLED.

1078
00:48:35,547 --> 00:48:37,415
QUARTER-INCH TRIM.

1079
00:48:37,448 --> 00:48:39,083
--ONE HOUR AND 18 MINUTES.

1080
00:48:39,117 --> 00:48:41,320
IF NUMBER THREE
GOES OFF RIGHT ON TIME.

1081
00:48:41,353 --> 00:48:43,988
IF IT DOESN'T, IT'LL RUIN
THE WHOLE OPERATION.

1082
00:48:44,022 --> 00:48:45,623
YEAH, BUT IF IT DOES,
IT'LL WORK.

1083
00:48:45,657 --> 00:48:47,425
IF IT DOESN'T, JUST DO IT.

1084
00:48:47,458 --> 00:48:50,195
--SO DO ALL THE REST.

1085
00:48:50,228 --> 00:48:51,830
SHOULDN'T THEY HAVE FIGURED
ALL THIS OUT ON THE SHIP?

1086
00:48:51,863 --> 00:48:53,165
I'LL STAY HERE
AND GIVE IT A THUMP

1087
00:48:53,198 --> 00:48:54,332
WHEN YOU GIVE ME
THE COUNTDOWN.

1088
00:48:54,365 --> 00:48:55,700
WHEN THEY DO FIRE,

1089
00:48:55,733 --> 00:48:58,237
SHE WON'T MAKE
LIKE A SPACESHIP,

1090
00:48:58,270 --> 00:49:00,372
BUT SHE'LL BE
BUILDING UP THRUST.

1091
00:49:00,405 --> 00:49:02,373
- WILL YOU BE OKAY?
- PROVIDED I GET OFF

1092
00:49:02,407 --> 00:49:04,408
IN THE FIRST
TEN SECONDS, YES.

1093
00:49:04,442 --> 00:49:06,512
ALL RIGHT.

1094
00:49:06,545 --> 00:49:07,845
ARE YOU SURE YOU'LL BE
ALL RIGHT, MR. KEMP?

1095
00:49:07,878 --> 00:49:09,982
YOU TAKE CARE OF YOUR
CALCULATIONS.

1096
00:49:10,015 --> 00:49:12,250
I'LL TAKE CARE OF MYSELF.

1097
00:49:12,283 --> 00:49:14,185
BUT LET'S JUST TRY
TO WORK TOGETHER, OKAY?

1098
00:49:14,218 --> 00:49:16,422
- THANK YOU FOR ASKING ANYWAY.
- GRR.

1099
00:49:16,455 --> 00:49:18,057
MY PLEASURE, GLAD TO DO IT.

1100
00:49:18,090 --> 00:49:20,592
LET'S DO LUNCH.

1101
00:49:23,295 --> 00:49:25,897
DON'T LOSE
YOUR HAPPY THOUGHTS.

1102
00:49:28,400 --> 00:49:30,868
CAN'T TELL IF THEY'RE JUST
DANGLING FROM WIRES THERE.

1103
00:49:30,902 --> 00:49:32,970
THEY LOOK LIKE BAIT.

1104
00:49:33,003 --> 00:49:36,408
♪ IT'S NOT EASY
BEING GREEN ♪

1105
00:49:36,442 --> 00:49:40,078
I'M CURIOUS BUT YELLOW.

1106
00:49:40,112 --> 00:49:42,580
AH, FROG AND A BEAR,
TOGETHER AGAIN.

1107
00:49:42,613 --> 00:49:45,083
WOCKA WOCKA WOCKA!

1108
00:49:45,117 --> 00:49:47,018
WHAT?

1109
00:49:53,592 --> 00:49:55,427
HERE'S THE MEAT SCALE
YOU ORDERED.

1110
00:49:55,460 --> 00:49:57,528
YEAH, WHERE'S MY MR. PIBB,
THOUGH?

1111
00:49:57,562 --> 00:49:59,497
OOPS.

1112
00:50:05,103 --> 00:50:06,638
HEY.

1113
00:50:09,273 --> 00:50:11,777
SEE THAT?
MEANS ABSOLUTELY NOTHING.

1114
00:50:14,578 --> 00:50:18,317
15 SECONDS, MR. KEMP.

1115
00:50:18,350 --> 00:50:20,318
NOT BY MY WATCH.

1116
00:50:22,620 --> 00:50:24,355
- TEN...
- THIRTEEN.

1117
00:50:24,388 --> 00:50:26,190
- NINE...
- EIGHT.

1118
00:50:26,223 --> 00:50:27,792
- EIGHT...
- TWO MILLION.

1119
00:50:27,825 --> 00:50:29,995
- 49.
- SEVEN.
- ONE, THREE,

1120
00:50:30,028 --> 00:50:32,697
- FIVE.
- HUT HUT HIKE!

1121
00:50:32,730 --> 00:50:35,967
- FOUR.
- 867-5309.

1122
00:50:36,000 --> 00:50:37,602
- TWO...
- ONE.

1123
00:50:37,635 --> 00:50:39,503
- ONE.
- THUMP. THUMP!

1124
00:50:49,447 --> 00:50:52,083
SPACE SOUNDS
BY CHUCK MANGIONE.

1125
00:50:53,952 --> 00:50:56,455
YAHOO.

1126
00:50:56,488 --> 00:50:58,490
A REAL YAHOO.

1127
00:51:02,193 --> 00:51:05,130
YOU'VE GOT FIVE SECONDS
TO GET FREE.

1128
00:51:05,163 --> 00:51:08,333
FIVE, FOUR, THREE...

1129
00:51:08,367 --> 00:51:10,968
PHEW.

1130
00:51:11,002 --> 00:51:13,238
HEY, IT LOOKS LIKE
HIS STONE PASSED HIM.

1131
00:51:13,272 --> 00:51:16,073
I WOULD'VE

1132
00:51:16,107 --> 00:51:18,543
HE WOULD'VE ENDED UP
IN HIS SOCKS.

1133
00:51:18,577 --> 00:51:19,812
YOU KNOW, AT LEAST
HE WOULD'VE DIED WITH

1134
00:51:19,845 --> 00:51:22,847
HIS BIRTHSTONE, THOUGH.

1135
00:51:22,880 --> 00:51:24,582
ARE YOU OKAY, BILL?

1136
00:51:24,615 --> 00:51:28,153
OH, I'VE BEEN BETTER.

1137
00:51:28,187 --> 00:51:31,155
ONLY IT'S A LITTLE LONELY
OUT HERE.

1138
00:51:31,188 --> 00:51:33,325
ARE YOU WALKING HOME,
OR WOULD YOU LIKE A LIFT?

1139
00:51:33,358 --> 00:51:35,093
I THINK I'LL TAKE A LIFT.

1140
00:51:35,127 --> 00:51:37,662
HAVE YOU BACK DOWN THERE
BEFORE YOU KNOW IT.

1141
00:51:37,695 --> 00:51:40,565
TRY TO MAKE IT
BEFORE THE BAR SHUTS.

1142
00:51:42,833 --> 00:51:44,368
WOW, THEY'RE SO VERSATILE.

1143
00:51:44,402 --> 00:51:47,138
IT'S KIND OF LIKE
SWAN LAKE A-GO-GO.

1144
00:51:48,607 --> 00:51:51,142
WHEN DOES WONDER BOY RECKON
WE SHOULD GO OUT AGAIN?

1145
00:51:51,175 --> 00:51:52,477
THREE DAYS.

1146
00:51:52,510 --> 00:51:55,113
ACCORDING TO HIS
BOX OF TRICKS.

1147
00:51:55,147 --> 00:51:56,715
WANT A DRINK?

1148
00:51:56,748 --> 00:51:59,117
LATER. I AM GOING TO EAT.

1149
00:51:59,150 --> 00:52:01,252
THEY MADE SOME EXTRA CASH
BY SELLING THIS SET

1150
00:52:01,285 --> 00:52:03,788
TO DONNY AND MARIE.

1151
00:52:03,822 --> 00:52:05,957
A DOUBLE MOON FLOWER
PLEASE, LEN.

1152
00:52:05,990 --> 00:52:07,525
IN A DIRTY SPACE TUMBLER.

1153
00:52:07,558 --> 00:52:09,962
BUFFALO STAMPEDE.

1154
00:52:13,698 --> 00:52:15,667
IS THAT NORM CROSBY?

1155
00:52:15,700 --> 00:52:17,168
OR CORM NOSBY.

1156
00:52:17,202 --> 00:52:19,938
THERE'S A LADY BEEN ASKING FOR
YOU FOR THE PAST COUPLE OF DAYS.

1157
00:52:19,972 --> 00:52:22,140
SPACE GET-UP
WORKS EVERY TIME.

1158
00:52:22,173 --> 00:52:24,008
WHAT'S SHE DRINKING?

1159
00:52:24,042 --> 00:52:26,745
- GREEN MARY.
- WHAT?

1160
00:52:28,078 --> 00:52:29,948
ROCKET FUEL
AND CABBAGE JUICE.

1161
00:52:29,982 --> 00:52:33,285
AND A SHOT OF BILE.

1162
00:52:33,318 --> 00:52:36,087
WHICH TAKES THE TASTE AWAY
FROM WHICH?

1163
00:52:36,120 --> 00:52:37,622
I DON'T KNOW.

1164
00:52:37,655 --> 00:52:39,723
I ONLY SERVE IT.

1165
00:52:39,757 --> 00:52:41,627
AND TAKE YOUR MONEY.

1166
00:52:43,962 --> 00:52:46,263
THINK HE TIPS HIMSELF
OUT OF THAT?

1167
00:52:46,297 --> 00:52:47,865
I DON'T KNOW.
HE'S GONNA HAVE TO FILE

1168
00:52:47,898 --> 00:52:50,535
A CHAPTER 13 WITH
ALL THOSE MOON DRINKS.

1169
00:52:50,568 --> 00:52:52,470
WELL, YOU'RE PAYING
FOR THE GARNISHES.

1170
00:52:52,503 --> 00:52:55,307
YEAH.

1171
00:52:55,340 --> 00:52:57,908
HEY, HOW'S THE EGG COMING?

1172
00:52:57,942 --> 00:52:59,410
FOUND YOUR BROTHER YET?

1173
00:52:59,443 --> 00:53:00,978
NO.

1174
00:53:01,012 --> 00:53:02,347
NOT ON THE CONVOY?

1175
00:53:02,380 --> 00:53:03,815
NOT ON TWO CONVOYS.

1176
00:53:03,848 --> 00:53:05,983
AND NOBODY SEEMS TO HAVE SEEN
HIM IN NEARLY FOUR MONTHS.

1177
00:53:06,017 --> 00:53:07,652
WELL, FAR SIDE IS
A BIG PLACE.

1178
00:53:07,685 --> 00:53:09,687
YOU JUST DON'T
GO VISITING SOMEONE

1179
00:53:09,720 --> 00:53:11,857
WHEN IT'S A HUNDRED MILES
OF ROUGH COUNTRY

1180
00:53:11,890 --> 00:53:14,325
AND IN A MOON BUG, WHICH--

1181
00:53:14,358 --> 00:53:16,127
HEY, FLORENCE HENDERSON
HAIRDO.

1182
00:53:16,160 --> 00:53:17,928
LOOKS LIKE SHE DID IT
WITH WESSON OIL.

1183
00:53:21,967 --> 00:53:24,702
MR. KEMP, DO YOU KNOW ANYTHING
ABOUT MOON MINING LAWS?

1184
00:53:24,735 --> 00:53:25,837
MM, A LITTLE.

1185
00:53:25,870 --> 00:53:28,340
CAN YOU EXPLAIN
THE TWO-YEAR RULE?

1186
00:53:28,373 --> 00:53:29,773
WELL, YOU GOT A CLAIM
FOR TWO YEARS,

1187
00:53:29,807 --> 00:53:30,975
AND IF YOU HAVEN'T
FOUND ANYTHING

1188
00:53:31,008 --> 00:53:32,510
AT THE END OF THAT TIME,
YOU GET THROWN OUT.

1189
00:53:32,543 --> 00:53:33,845
SOMEBODY ELSE GETS IT.

1190
00:53:33,878 --> 00:53:35,480
THERE'S QUITE
A WAITING LIST.

1191
00:53:35,513 --> 00:53:36,882
SEEMS A BIT UNFAIR.

1192
00:53:36,915 --> 00:53:40,318
MAYBE, BUT THE MOON COSTS
A LOT OF MONEY TO GET STARTED.

1193
00:53:40,352 --> 00:53:41,753
AND THEY CAN'T HAVE
PEOPLE JUST

1194
00:53:41,787 --> 00:53:43,855
DIGGING HOLES
AND NOT FINDING ANYTHING.

1195
00:53:43,888 --> 00:53:45,057
WELL, UNLESS THEY
CALL THEM CRATERS.

1196
00:53:45,090 --> 00:53:46,590
--BROTHER HAD HIS CLAIM?

1197
00:53:46,623 --> 00:53:49,093
- TWO YEARS--
IN THREE DAYS' TIME.
- YEAH, WELL, UH,

1198
00:53:49,127 --> 00:53:50,795
WHO'S GOT THE DEED
ON THE FOREHEAD?

1199
00:53:50,828 --> 00:53:52,330
THAT'S WHAT
I'D LIKE TO KNOW.

1200
00:53:52,363 --> 00:53:54,065
--CABLE,
THAT'S WHY I'M UP HERE.

1201
00:53:54,098 --> 00:53:55,900
WELL, YOU'D BETTER TELL HIM
TO GET OVER HERE AND PROVE IT.

1202
00:53:55,933 --> 00:53:59,137
- BEFORE HE LOSES HIS CLAIM.
- I RADIOED.

1203
00:53:59,170 --> 00:54:00,405
HE'S TALKING TO A LADY.

1204
00:54:00,438 --> 00:54:02,407
BUT THE CONVOYS...

1205
00:54:02,440 --> 00:54:04,742
NO, THEY WOULDN'T
BE QUICK ENOUGH.

1206
00:54:04,775 --> 00:54:07,112
MR. KEMP, WILL YOU
FLY ME OVER THERE?

1207
00:54:07,145 --> 00:54:08,647
I DON'T KNOW,
HOW FAST DO YOU GO?

1208
00:54:08,680 --> 00:54:11,082
I KNOW I HAVEN'T
GOT $10,000 ON ME NOW.

1209
00:54:11,115 --> 00:54:12,917
BUT IF WALLY'S
FOUND SOMETHING,

1210
00:54:12,950 --> 00:54:15,087
WE'LL PAY YOU BACK
AS SOON AS WE'RE SELLING IT.

1211
00:54:15,120 --> 00:54:16,788
I COULDN'T LAND
ON YOUR BROTHER'S CLAIM.

1212
00:54:16,822 --> 00:54:20,458
- THAT WOULD HURT.
- IT'S MUCH TOO ROUGH COUNTRY.

1213
00:54:20,492 --> 00:54:22,227
BUT WE COULD GO
TO FAR SIDE FIVE.

1214
00:54:22,260 --> 00:54:26,063
IT'S A 24-HOUR RIDE
IN A BUG FROM THERE.

1215
00:54:26,097 --> 00:54:27,565
YOU CAN OWE IT TO ME.

1216
00:54:27,598 --> 00:54:29,967
YEAH, WHAT THE HELL,
I'M NEARLY RICH ANYWAY.

1217
00:54:30,000 --> 00:54:31,302
LET'S HAVE ANOTHER DRINK.

1218
00:54:31,335 --> 00:54:34,005
UH, CAN'T I FINISH
THE ONE I'VE GOT?

1219
00:54:34,038 --> 00:54:37,208
LEN, I'D LIKE TWO MORE
OF WHATEVER THEY ARE.

1220
00:54:37,242 --> 00:54:38,943
SEWAGE BILGE.

1221
00:54:38,977 --> 00:54:41,212
YOU WEREN'T THINKING OF TAKING
THE YOUNG LADY FOR A RIDE,

1222
00:54:41,245 --> 00:54:44,215
WERE YOU, MR. KEMP?

1223
00:54:44,248 --> 00:54:45,950
I'M A PILOT FOR HIRE.

1224
00:54:45,983 --> 00:54:47,418
YOU'RE ALREADY HIRED.

1225
00:54:47,452 --> 00:54:49,187
DROP HER.

1226
00:54:49,220 --> 00:54:50,622
IT'LL ONLY BE
A THREE DAY TRIP.

1227
00:54:50,655 --> 00:54:52,123
I'LL BE BACK IN TIME.

1228
00:54:52,157 --> 00:54:53,958
THAT'S WHAT
THE SKIPPER SAID.

1229
00:54:53,992 --> 00:54:56,093
DROP HER.

1230
00:54:56,127 --> 00:54:57,628
- THAT WOULD HURT HER.
- YOU SEEM TO HAVE YOUR HAND

1231
00:54:57,662 --> 00:54:58,863
ON ME.

1232
00:54:58,897 --> 00:55:01,265
I'M NO DOCTOR,
BUT I'M PRETTY SURE

1233
00:55:01,298 --> 00:55:02,667
YOU GOT YOUR HAND ON ME.

1234
00:55:02,700 --> 00:55:05,103
--REALLY OWNS.

1235
00:55:15,213 --> 00:55:17,782
HEY, WATCH THE SLUSH PUPPIE
MACHINE.

1236
00:55:17,815 --> 00:55:20,652
IF WE'RE GONNA PLAY...

1237
00:55:20,685 --> 00:55:22,820
WE'RE GONNA PLAY
BY MY RULES.

1238
00:55:22,853 --> 00:55:25,957
YEAH, BUT NOBODY KNOWS
WHAT YOUR RULES ARE.

1239
00:55:28,358 --> 00:55:31,428
ALWAYS HAVE YOUR HAIR CUT
BY A MACHINE.

1240
00:55:31,462 --> 00:55:33,598
AND I ALWAYS LOOK LIKE
DENNIS HOPPER.

1241
00:55:33,632 --> 00:55:35,032
OOH, HE GAVE HIM A SNUGGIE.

1242
00:55:35,065 --> 00:55:37,902
IN SPACE, NO ONE
CAN HEAR A WEDGIE.

1243
00:55:45,377 --> 00:55:47,512
LOOK OUT, BIG BIRD!

1244
00:55:48,780 --> 00:55:51,648
OH, MAGIC SCREEN.

1245
00:55:58,923 --> 00:56:02,027
OH, HE SHOULD'VE
SEEN THAT COMING.

1246
00:56:10,435 --> 00:56:12,870
PICKED UP A SPARE.

1247
00:56:25,717 --> 00:56:28,787
TOUCHDOWN IN 17 MINUTES.

1248
00:56:31,655 --> 00:56:33,223
BE CAREFUL,
WE'VE JUST GONE WEIGHTLESS.

1249
00:56:33,257 --> 00:56:34,792
I KNOW.

1250
00:56:34,825 --> 00:56:37,362
JUST LIKE THE MOON EXPRESS.

1251
00:56:37,395 --> 00:56:38,930
THOUGH YOUR SHIP

1252
00:56:38,963 --> 00:56:40,832
IS DIFFERENT IN OTHER WAYS.

1253
00:56:40,865 --> 00:56:43,400
YOU MEAN NO TOILET PAPER?
YEAH, SORRY ABOUT THAT.

1254
00:56:43,433 --> 00:56:47,272
YOU ARE IN FOR A NICE, LONG
NIGHT DRIVE IN A MOON-BUG.

1255
00:56:47,305 --> 00:56:49,740
JUST BUILT FOR TWO.

1256
00:56:49,773 --> 00:56:52,143
I'LL STAY WITH THE SHIP
AND GIVE HER A SPRINKLING.

1257
00:56:52,177 --> 00:56:53,578
AND GET SOME SLEEP.

1258
00:56:53,612 --> 00:56:55,747
AND GIVE HER A SPRINKLING.

1259
00:56:58,683 --> 00:57:00,852
APPROACHING RE-ENTRY POINT.

1260
00:57:00,885 --> 00:57:02,887
THAT'S OUR CUE, DOLL-FACE.

1261
00:57:07,258 --> 00:57:09,127
COOL.

1262
00:57:13,998 --> 00:57:16,367
HEY, COULD YOU TURN DOWN
THAT STEREO?

1263
00:57:21,205 --> 00:57:22,873
THE OLD WEST.

1264
00:57:22,907 --> 00:57:25,108
IN SPACE,
NO ONE CAN ART-DIRECT.

1265
00:57:25,142 --> 00:57:27,245
--HAVEN'T SEEN
WALLY HERE IN, OH,

1266
00:57:27,278 --> 00:57:30,248
MUST BE NEARLY
FOUR MONTHS BY NOW.

1267
00:57:30,282 --> 00:57:32,050
WE TRIED TO RADIO HIM
A COUPLE OF TIMES.

1268
00:57:32,083 --> 00:57:35,453
BUT IT'S ALWAYS CHANCY
IN THE MOUNTAIN COUNTRY.

1269
00:57:35,487 --> 00:57:37,488
HOW ABOUT RELAYING IT?

1270
00:57:37,522 --> 00:57:39,790
WELL, I COULD
ASK NICK HUNTER

1271
00:57:39,823 --> 00:57:41,825
TO ASK LOUIS GRENIER

1272
00:57:41,858 --> 00:57:44,028
TO ASK TAD CONNELL
TO PASS ON A MESSAGE.

1273
00:57:44,062 --> 00:57:46,263
- BUT--
- BUT THEY'RE ALL DEAD.
IT'D BE SILLY.

1274
00:57:46,297 --> 00:57:48,265
--KIDNEY TROUBLE
THE LAST FORTNIGHT.

1275
00:57:48,298 --> 00:57:50,368
AND I KNOW THAT NICK
WENT OVER TO MOON CITY

1276
00:57:50,402 --> 00:57:52,403
ON THE LAST CONVOY.

1277
00:57:52,437 --> 00:57:54,105
- ON THE OTHER HAND--
- DO I NEED TO KNOW THIS?

1278
00:57:54,138 --> 00:57:57,408
WE MIGHT BE ABLE
TO CONTACT BILL WIRTER.

1279
00:57:57,442 --> 00:57:58,677
OH, NO.

1280
00:57:58,710 --> 00:58:01,512
HE'S OFF-RADIO FOR
THE NEXT COUPLE OF DAYS.

1281
00:58:01,545 --> 00:58:03,982
SORRY, THERE DOESN'T
SEEM TO BE ANY WAY.

1282
00:58:04,015 --> 00:58:05,350
WELL, WHEN YOU
DIDN'T HEAR FROM HIM,

1283
00:58:05,383 --> 00:58:07,252
DIDN'T YOU THINK
OF DECLARING AN EMERGENCY?

1284
00:58:07,285 --> 00:58:08,653
DO YOU THINK
THIS PERMANENT WAVE

1285
00:58:08,687 --> 00:58:10,388
IS A GOOD IDEA FOR MY HAIR?

1286
00:58:10,422 --> 00:58:11,822
LOOKS LIKE BIG BOY.

1287
00:58:11,855 --> 00:58:14,292
THE SATELLITE'S
ONLY BEEN DEAD FOR 12 DAYS.

1288
00:58:14,325 --> 00:58:16,895
I KNOW THAT, BUT...

1289
00:58:16,928 --> 00:58:19,130
NOBODY DIES SLOWLY
ON THE MOON.

1290
00:58:19,163 --> 00:58:20,698
YOU KNOW THAT.

1291
00:58:20,732 --> 00:58:23,533
HMM, WELL,
CAN I TAKE A BUG, THEN?

1292
00:58:23,567 --> 00:58:25,270
WELL, ONE'S OUT.

1293
00:58:25,303 --> 00:58:26,905
- I SAID "BUG LIGHT."
- I WAS HOPING TO DO AN OVERHAUL

1294
00:58:26,938 --> 00:58:29,173
ON THE OTHER.

1295
00:58:29,207 --> 00:58:32,043
I'D NEED
A THOUSAND DOLLARS DEPOSIT.

1296
00:58:33,410 --> 00:58:36,047
OH, I HAVE THAT IN MY SHOE.

1297
00:58:37,882 --> 00:58:40,352
YOUR ODOR-EATER.
THANK YOU VERY MUCH.

1298
00:58:43,688 --> 00:58:45,523
I'M AFRAID YOU'RE
OVER YOUR CREDIT LIMIT.

1299
00:58:45,557 --> 00:58:48,058
DO YOU HAVE
A DR. SCHOLL'S PAD ON YOU?

1300
00:58:50,528 --> 00:58:51,828
IS IT READY?

1301
00:58:51,862 --> 00:58:53,430
AS READY AS SHE'LL EVER BE.

1302
00:58:53,463 --> 00:58:55,633
I GUESS
SHE'LL GET YOU THERE.

1303
00:58:55,667 --> 00:58:57,102
AND BACK?

1304
00:58:57,135 --> 00:58:59,770
SURE DO HOPE SO.

1305
00:58:59,803 --> 00:59:01,905
CLIMB ABOARD.

1306
00:59:01,938 --> 00:59:04,142
OH MAN, SHE'S CHERRY, MAN.

1307
00:59:04,175 --> 00:59:07,012
PUT ON SOME
THRUSH GLASSPACKS, MAN.

1308
00:59:07,045 --> 00:59:10,915
HE'S GOT SOME TWIN HEADERS
WITH A .44 BARREL.

1309
00:59:10,948 --> 00:59:12,550
SCREAMS.

1310
00:59:12,583 --> 00:59:14,985
- THE VAN'S PRETTY NICE, TOO.
- UH, MOVE OVER.

1311
00:59:15,018 --> 00:59:17,155
UNLESS YOU WANT TO DRIVE.

1312
00:59:17,188 --> 00:59:20,023
HEY, HOW MANY GIRLS
HAVE YOU HAD IN YOUR MOON BUG?

1313
00:59:23,327 --> 00:59:26,297
WELL, IF YOU'VE GOTTA GO,
YOU'D BETTER DO IT NOW.

1314
00:59:29,600 --> 00:59:31,435
HOW DO YOU LIKE MY NEW
"MOON SOUNDS" TAPE

1315
00:59:31,468 --> 00:59:33,103
BY PHILIP GLASS?

1316
00:59:40,177 --> 00:59:42,580
HEY, I KNOW,
LET'S SING CAR SONGS.

1317
00:59:42,613 --> 00:59:44,215
YOU KNOW, LIKE
THE WIENER-MAN SONG, YEAH.

1318
00:59:44,248 --> 00:59:45,750
♪ I KNOW A WIENER MAN ♪

1319
00:59:45,783 --> 00:59:47,285
♪ HE OWNS A HOT DOG STAND ♪

1320
00:59:47,318 --> 00:59:49,787
♪ HE-- SORRY.

1321
00:59:49,820 --> 00:59:51,622
HOW ABOUT ANOTHER ONE?

1322
00:59:58,562 --> 01:00:00,498
AND SO THEY SET OUT

1323
01:00:00,532 --> 01:00:03,802
IN THE WIENER CAR IN SEARCH
OF THE GIANT KIELBASA.

1324
01:00:07,572 --> 01:00:09,307
HUH, WE'RE OUT OF GAS.

1325
01:00:17,615 --> 01:00:19,250
HEY, THERE'S
JACQUES COUSTEAU.

1326
01:00:24,222 --> 01:00:25,990
I'M SORRY, BUT THIS
IS A PART OF THE MOON

1327
01:00:26,023 --> 01:00:27,258
THAT TOURISTS
DON'T USUALLY SEE.

1328
01:00:27,292 --> 01:00:28,893
IF WE PULL THE WRONG LEVER
OUT HERE,

1329
01:00:28,927 --> 01:00:30,728
THERE'S NO GUARANTEE
WE'LL EVEN BE FOUND.

1330
01:00:30,762 --> 01:00:32,797
I'M SORRY.

1331
01:00:32,830 --> 01:00:34,765
BUT I'M NOT A TOURIST,
MR. KEMP.

1332
01:00:34,798 --> 01:00:36,800
I'M HERE TO STAY AND WORK
WITH MY BROTHER.

1333
01:00:36,833 --> 01:00:38,368
I KNOW, IT'S
A LITTLE BIT ROUGH NOW,

1334
01:00:38,402 --> 01:00:39,837
BUT IT'LL BE BETTER
WHEN WE FALL IN LOVE

1335
01:00:39,870 --> 01:00:41,272
LATER IN THE PICTURE.

1336
01:00:41,305 --> 01:00:44,375
I UNDERSTAND.

1337
01:00:44,408 --> 01:00:46,310
HOW LONG DOES IT STAY DARK?

1338
01:00:46,343 --> 01:00:47,912
- ALL NIGHT.
- IT'LL BE...

1339
01:00:47,945 --> 01:00:50,548
...SUN-UP IN 40 HOURS.

1340
01:00:52,583 --> 01:00:54,685
SO THAT'S LIKE
A HUNDRED HOURS.

1341
01:00:54,718 --> 01:00:57,922
200 DEGREES BELOW ZERO.

1342
01:00:57,955 --> 01:01:01,092
AND UP ABOVE BOILING POINT
WHEN THE SUN'S OUT.

1343
01:01:01,125 --> 01:01:02,593
DON'T WORRY,
THESE BUGS HAVE EFFICIENT

1344
01:01:02,627 --> 01:01:04,662
HEATING AND COOLING
SYSTEMS.

1345
01:01:04,695 --> 01:01:06,397
WE'VE ALWAYS
GOT THE MOON SUITS.

1346
01:01:06,430 --> 01:01:07,732
YEAH, I GUESS
IF I HAD TO DO IT OVER,

1347
01:01:07,765 --> 01:01:09,667
I'D PROBABLY BUY FOREIGN.

1348
01:01:09,700 --> 01:01:11,702
I SEE WHAT YOU MEAN ABOUT

1349
01:01:11,735 --> 01:01:13,170
WE'LL ALWAYS BE FOREIGNERS.

1350
01:01:13,203 --> 01:01:15,807
NO, I SAID I'D BUY FOREIGN.

1351
01:01:17,942 --> 01:01:20,243
WHY'D YOUR BROTHER
PICK THIS END OF THE MOON?

1352
01:01:20,277 --> 01:01:22,713
HE DIDN'T, IT WAS THE ONLY CLAIM
LEFT WHEN HE GOT HERE.

1353
01:01:22,747 --> 01:01:24,148
THAT FIGURES.

1354
01:01:24,182 --> 01:01:26,417
WHAT WAS HE MINING ON EARTH?

1355
01:01:26,450 --> 01:01:27,985
GOLD. SOME SILVER.

1356
01:01:28,018 --> 01:01:30,655
LAST THING HE FOUND
WAS COPPER UP IN MONTANA.

1357
01:01:30,688 --> 01:01:33,825
SOLD OUT CHEAP
TO A BIG COMPANY.

1358
01:01:33,858 --> 01:01:35,158
HE ALWAYS THINKS THERE'LL BE

1359
01:01:35,192 --> 01:01:37,195
A BIGGER AND BETTER STRIKE
OVER THE NEXT HILL.

1360
01:01:37,228 --> 01:01:39,597
HE CAME OVER A BIG HILL
THIS TIME.

1361
01:01:39,630 --> 01:01:41,665
- FUNNY.
- YOUR FATHER?

1362
01:01:41,698 --> 01:01:43,835
HE BLEW HIMSELF UP
FIVE YEARS AGO.

1363
01:01:43,868 --> 01:01:45,637
DYNAMITING FOR EMERALDS
IN THE ANDES.

1364
01:01:45,670 --> 01:01:48,605
- AND YOUR MOM?
- I HARDLY KNEW HIM.

1365
01:01:48,638 --> 01:01:50,007
HE WAS ALWAYS OFF SOMEWHERE,

1366
01:01:50,040 --> 01:01:52,843
DIGGING A NEW HOLE
OVER A NEW HILL.

1367
01:01:52,877 --> 01:01:55,613
YOU'RE THE BILL KEMP
WHO WAS THE FIRST MAN ON MARS.

1368
01:01:55,647 --> 01:01:56,847
THAT'S RIGHT.

1369
01:01:56,880 --> 01:01:59,750
THAT'S FUNNY,
MEETING YOU LIKE THIS.

1370
01:01:59,783 --> 01:02:01,718
DRIVING A HIRED MOON BUG?

1371
01:02:01,752 --> 01:02:03,153
NO.

1372
01:02:03,187 --> 01:02:04,555
I CAN REMEMBER
WHEN WE GOT THE NEWS

1373
01:02:04,588 --> 01:02:05,890
THAT YOU'D LANDED ON MARS.

1374
01:02:05,923 --> 01:02:07,792
I WAS JUST
A SCHOOLGIRL THEN.

1375
01:02:07,825 --> 01:02:09,693
AND I WASN'T VERY INTERESTED
IN SPACE-TRAVEL.

1376
01:02:09,727 --> 01:02:13,397
OKAY, OKAY.
RUB IT IN, I'M OLD.

1377
01:02:13,430 --> 01:02:15,900
THEN THE ASTRONOMY TEACHER
SHOWED US MARS ONE NIGHT.

1378
01:02:15,933 --> 01:02:17,835
HE TOLD US HOW FAR IT WAS.

1379
01:02:17,868 --> 01:02:20,572
IT STILL IS.

1380
01:02:20,605 --> 01:02:22,740
I REMEMBER YOUR NAME
FROM THEN.

1381
01:02:22,773 --> 01:02:24,275
THE MAN WHO'D
FLOWN A SPACESHIP

1382
01:02:24,308 --> 01:02:26,477
FOR 40 MILLION MILES.

1383
01:02:26,510 --> 01:02:29,180
OKAY, YOU'RE 12, I'M 100.
I GET IT ALREADY.

1384
01:02:29,213 --> 01:02:32,383
OH, I COULD STILL RECITE YOU
THE NAMES OF THE CREW.

1385
01:02:32,417 --> 01:02:34,418
THAT'S MORE THAN I COULD.

1386
01:02:34,452 --> 01:02:37,120
YOU EVER THINK ABOUT RENTING OUT
YOUR FOREHEAD FOR ADVERTISING?

1387
01:02:37,153 --> 01:02:39,657
WHY'D YOU GIVE IT UP?
EXPLORING.

1388
01:02:39,690 --> 01:02:41,425
IT GAVE ME UP.

1389
01:02:41,458 --> 01:02:43,527
AFTER MARS AND JACK HARVEY
GOT ON VENUS,

1390
01:02:43,560 --> 01:02:45,195
THE CORPORATION DECIDED

1391
01:02:45,228 --> 01:02:48,498
THAT PASSENGERS
WAS WHERE THE MONEY WAS.

1392
01:02:48,532 --> 01:02:50,067
SURE, IT WOULD'VE TAKEN
SOME MONEY

1393
01:02:50,100 --> 01:02:51,468
AND SOME NEW INVENTIONS, TOO,

1394
01:02:51,502 --> 01:02:54,672
TO GET TO MERCURY AND...

1395
01:02:54,705 --> 01:02:57,107
JUPITER'S MOONS.

1396
01:02:57,140 --> 01:03:00,545
JUPITER, THAT'S A PLANET,
ISN'T IT?

1397
01:03:00,578 --> 01:03:02,680
ANYWAY, I WASN'T
A PASSENGER PILOT,

1398
01:03:02,713 --> 01:03:04,382
SO I QUIT.

1399
01:03:04,415 --> 01:03:07,385
OKAY, I LIED. THEY GOT ME
ON A MORALS CHARGE.

1400
01:03:07,418 --> 01:03:09,820
- I UNDERSTAND.
- YOU DO?

1401
01:03:09,853 --> 01:03:12,357
CHINESE GOOD FOR YOU?

1402
01:03:12,390 --> 01:03:13,958
- HEY, IT'S A SOUVENIR BANK.
- ALWAYS SOMETHING

1403
01:03:13,992 --> 01:03:16,127
OVER THE NEXT HILL.

1404
01:03:16,160 --> 01:03:19,163
- I KNOW.
- AND ALWAYS ON BORROWED MONEY.

1405
01:03:20,363 --> 01:03:23,667
BUT THERE IS SOMETHING
OVER THE HILL.

1406
01:03:23,700 --> 01:03:26,037
THAT'S THE TROUBLE
FOR A WOMAN.

1407
01:03:26,070 --> 01:03:27,705
ALL SPACE TRAVEL
IS JUST A BIG WAY

1408
01:03:27,738 --> 01:03:29,707
OF GETTING OUT OF THE HOUSE
ON A SATURDAY EVENING.

1409
01:03:29,740 --> 01:03:31,508
WELL, IF YOU DON'T HAVE
ANYTHING BETTER TO DO.

1410
01:03:31,542 --> 01:03:35,378
AND WE SURE DON'T.

1411
01:03:45,055 --> 01:03:46,457
♪ I WANNA BE
HIS WIENER WIFE ♪

1412
01:03:46,490 --> 01:03:48,292
♪ I WANNA JOIN
HIS WIENER LIFE ♪

1413
01:03:48,325 --> 01:03:49,960
HEY, NICE STEPS.

1414
01:03:49,993 --> 01:03:53,463
LOOKS LIKE THEY SHOULD HAVE
BOXING GLOVES AT THE END OF 'EM.

1415
01:03:53,497 --> 01:03:54,765
LOOKS LIKE THEY'RE
KIND OF CRAWLING OUT

1416
01:03:54,798 --> 01:03:57,167
OF THE TUPPERWARE ORANGE.

1417
01:04:02,005 --> 01:04:03,975
NOW, THOSE SUITS
ARE DIFFERENT COLORS

1418
01:04:04,008 --> 01:04:07,945
SO YOU CAN TELL WHO'S WHO.

1419
01:04:07,978 --> 01:04:09,347
IF SHE GETS CONFUSED,

1420
01:04:09,380 --> 01:04:13,083
SHE SHOULD JUST REMEMBER
THAT SHE'S HER.

1421
01:04:13,117 --> 01:04:15,052
HUH?

1422
01:04:20,357 --> 01:04:21,992
UH, THEY LEFT
THEIR DOME LIGHT ON.

1423
01:04:22,025 --> 01:04:24,828
SOMEONE'S GONNA
HAVE TO GET A JUMP-START.

1424
01:04:26,697 --> 01:04:28,798
TRIPLE-A'S EVEN GONNA
CHARGE 'EM FOR THAT ONE.

1425
01:04:28,832 --> 01:04:31,035
OH, BROTHER.

1426
01:04:31,068 --> 01:04:33,703
HER BROTHER LIVED
IN A PORTA-POTTY.

1427
01:04:39,077 --> 01:04:40,377
WOW, LOOK AT IT IN THERE.

1428
01:04:40,410 --> 01:04:43,147
YOUR BROTHER
WAS REALLY A SLOB.

1429
01:04:43,180 --> 01:04:44,515
HEY, IS THERE AIR
COMING OUT OF YOUR SUIT,

1430
01:04:44,548 --> 01:04:46,783
OR ARE YOU PLAYING
A TRUMPET?

1431
01:04:49,353 --> 01:04:51,355
SKIN SAMPLE.

1432
01:04:51,388 --> 01:04:54,958
LOOKS VALUABLE.

1433
01:04:54,992 --> 01:04:56,693
WISH I HAD ME
ONE OF THEM PLOWS.

1434
01:04:56,727 --> 01:04:58,928
--FOUND SOMETHING.

1435
01:04:58,962 --> 01:05:00,397
TWO DRIVEWAYS.

1436
01:05:00,430 --> 01:05:04,168
- WHERE ARE YOU?
- AROUND THE CORNER.

1437
01:05:04,202 --> 01:05:08,005
DON'T WANDER OFF.
YOU'VE GOTTA STAY IN SIGHT.

1438
01:05:08,038 --> 01:05:09,540
I'M SORRY.

1439
01:05:09,573 --> 01:05:12,208
A SET-UP LIKE THAT IS BOUND
TO SCARE OFF TRICK-OR-TREATERS.

1440
01:05:12,242 --> 01:05:14,545
- DO YOU KNOW WHAT THIS IS?
- A PIECE OF ROCK.

1441
01:05:14,578 --> 01:05:16,713
LOOKS LIKE YOUR BROTHER'S
KNEECAP.

1442
01:05:16,747 --> 01:05:18,948
WITH A VEIN OF NICKEL IN IT,
AND A VERY RICH ONE.

1443
01:05:18,982 --> 01:05:21,352
WALLY DID FIND SOMETHING.

1444
01:05:21,385 --> 01:05:22,687
ARE YOU SURE?

1445
01:05:22,720 --> 01:05:24,222
I KNOW A LITTLE
ABOUT GEOLOGY.

1446
01:05:24,255 --> 01:05:25,690
WELL, WE ALL KNOW
A LITTLE BIT.

1447
01:05:25,723 --> 01:05:27,190
WHERE COULD HE HAVE GONE?

1448
01:05:27,223 --> 01:05:29,727
NOT FAR, OR HE WOULD'VE
TAKEN HIS BUG-DOZER.

1449
01:05:31,695 --> 01:05:33,397
NOW JUST HOW DISAPPOINTED
WOULD YOU BE

1450
01:05:33,430 --> 01:05:36,600
IF YOU NEVER SAW
YOUR BROTHER ALIVE AGAIN?

1451
01:05:39,803 --> 01:05:42,873
LOOK, THERE'S SOMEONE THERE!

1452
01:05:42,907 --> 01:05:44,775
OH, HIM, HE'S ALWAYS THERE.

1453
01:05:44,808 --> 01:05:47,378
IT'S A SPACE LAWN JOCKEY.

1454
01:05:47,412 --> 01:05:49,447
EVERYONE'S GOT 'EM AT
THE END OF THEIR DRIVEWAY.

1455
01:05:49,480 --> 01:05:51,615
NOW, REMEMBER, THERE
WILL BE THREE OF US NOW.

1456
01:05:51,648 --> 01:05:53,383
AND YOU'RE THE ONE
THAT'S YOU,

1457
01:05:53,417 --> 01:05:56,220
IN THE BLUE, ALL RIGHT?

1458
01:05:59,790 --> 01:06:02,560
OH, HE'S LOST WEIGHT.
HE LOOKED MUCH BETTER HEAVY.

1459
01:06:09,767 --> 01:06:12,102
I SUPPOSE HE JUST
MADE A MISTAKE.

1460
01:06:12,135 --> 01:06:14,705
HE MANAGED FOR TWO YEARS
WITHOUT MAKING ONE.

1461
01:06:14,738 --> 01:06:16,373
AND HE DIDN'T
PUNCTURE HIS SUIT.

1462
01:06:16,407 --> 01:06:19,177
HE HAD TO HAVE OXYGEN
TO LOOK LIKE--

1463
01:06:19,210 --> 01:06:21,112
TO GO AS HE DID.

1464
01:06:21,145 --> 01:06:23,947
ONE FULL. ONE EMPTY.

1465
01:06:23,980 --> 01:06:26,883
WHICH ONE
DO YOU THINK HE USED?

1466
01:06:26,917 --> 01:06:29,553
JUST A STUPID MISTAKE.

1467
01:06:29,587 --> 01:06:31,688
WELL, I BET
HE'LL NEVER DO IT AGAIN.

1468
01:06:31,722 --> 01:06:34,758
LET'S USE OUR PRECIOUS OXYGEN
AND BURY HIM.

1469
01:06:38,662 --> 01:06:40,732
SEE THIS? IT'S HIS NINTENDO.

1470
01:06:40,765 --> 01:06:42,232
HE WOULD'VE
WANTED ME TO HAVE IT.

1471
01:06:42,265 --> 01:06:44,435
WELL, IF HE'D HAVE KNOWN ME.

1472
01:06:46,403 --> 01:06:48,105
I'M KEEPING IT.

1473
01:06:53,243 --> 01:06:55,947
HONEY, COOKIES ARE DONE.

1474
01:06:58,415 --> 01:07:00,283
HOLD IT.

1475
01:07:00,317 --> 01:07:01,718
OOPS.

1476
01:07:01,752 --> 01:07:03,053
LOOKS LIKE WE GOT COMPANY.

1477
01:07:03,087 --> 01:07:06,023
IT'S THE UNWELCOME WAGON.

1478
01:07:08,692 --> 01:07:12,095
YOU OUT THERE,
IDENTIFY YOURSELVES.

1479
01:07:12,128 --> 01:07:13,963
OKAY, WILL THIS HELP?
THEY CALL ME SHOOTER.

1480
01:07:13,997 --> 01:07:15,800
GET DOWN.

1481
01:07:22,807 --> 01:07:25,308
DAMN MOON GOONS!

1482
01:07:37,988 --> 01:07:41,092
HEY, THEY COME IN
GREAT FLAVORS, TOO.

1483
01:07:41,125 --> 01:07:43,160
THERE'S RASPBERRY RED,
BURNT UMBER,

1484
01:07:43,193 --> 01:07:46,330
AND, OF COURSE, CHARTREUSE.

1485
01:07:46,363 --> 01:07:49,967
OH, MAN, AND I BET THAT MOON
BUGGY WAS ON HIS CARD, TOO.

1486
01:08:00,912 --> 01:08:04,182
EXCUSE ME, I'M NERVOUS.

1487
01:08:04,215 --> 01:08:06,550
I'M SORRY,
YOU'LL HAVE TO EXCUSE ME.

1488
01:08:15,825 --> 01:08:17,293
WE'RE ON TELEPHONE NOW.

1489
01:08:17,327 --> 01:08:19,930
THEY CAN'T HEAR US, BUT DON'T
SAY ANYTHING ON RADIO.

1490
01:08:19,963 --> 01:08:22,365
- THEY'RE PICKING IT ALL UP.
- IS THERE A SEVEN-SECOND DELAY?

1491
01:08:22,398 --> 01:08:24,468
CAN I SWEAR?

1492
01:08:26,403 --> 01:08:29,540
COME ON OUT, BOTH OF YOU,
OR WE'LL DRILL YOU LIKE A SIEVE.

1493
01:08:29,573 --> 01:08:31,275
WHAT KIND OF SIEVE?
THAT OUGHT TO KEEP THEM BUSY.

1494
01:08:31,308 --> 01:08:34,110
DON'T SHOOT.
THE GIRL'S HURT.

1495
01:08:34,143 --> 01:08:36,180
YOU'VE GOTTA HELP ME.

1496
01:08:36,213 --> 01:08:37,815
DOES THIS HELP?

1497
01:08:42,252 --> 01:08:45,488
TIMPANI GUN.

1498
01:08:45,522 --> 01:08:48,825
WORKS EVERY TIME.

1499
01:08:48,858 --> 01:08:50,327
WELL, YOU GOT LIME GREEN.

1500
01:08:50,360 --> 01:08:53,663
JUST RASPBERRY RED
AND LEMON YELLOW TO GO.

1501
01:08:53,697 --> 01:08:56,133
BUT REMEMBER,
TRIX ARE FOR KIDS.

1502
01:09:02,205 --> 01:09:04,608
NOW JUST REMEMBER,
THEY'RE THE GUYS IN COLOR.

1503
01:09:14,352 --> 01:09:16,153
THERE'S ANOTHER WAY OUT.

1504
01:09:18,855 --> 01:09:21,225
HEY, THERE'S
A BARRACUDA IN HERE.

1505
01:09:21,258 --> 01:09:23,293
IF WE DON'T DIE, YOU WANNA
CATCH A MOVIE OR SOMETHING?

1506
01:09:23,327 --> 01:09:25,728
I MEAN, IF YOU'RE NOT ALIVE,
I TOTALLY UNDERSTAND.

1507
01:09:25,762 --> 01:09:28,665
IT WON'T HURT MY FEELINGS
OR ANYTHING.

1508
01:09:37,207 --> 01:09:39,075
BACK IN THE CAVES.

1509
01:09:44,548 --> 01:09:46,017
HEY, PLOW YOUR DRIVEWAY,
MISTER?

1510
01:09:46,050 --> 01:09:47,985
JEEZ.

1511
01:09:50,653 --> 01:09:53,090
OH, HE KILLED
A BLOW-UP DOLL.

1512
01:09:53,123 --> 01:09:55,392
SOUP'S ON, HE SAID FLATLY.

1513
01:10:03,867 --> 01:10:06,403
LOOKS LIKE HE'S GOING AFTER
A CRACK HOUSE.

1514
01:10:09,038 --> 01:10:11,675
WOW, LAWN AND GARDEN
ATTACHMENTS.

1515
01:10:11,708 --> 01:10:14,143
THAT GUY'S GOT
ALL THE CANDY.

1516
01:10:16,247 --> 01:10:19,850
UH, JUST TAKE A LITTLE
OFF THE TORSO, PLEASE.

1517
01:10:38,868 --> 01:10:41,338
THIS IS LIKE
A BAD MUSIC FESTIVAL.

1518
01:10:45,308 --> 01:10:48,378
HEY, SHUT THE DOOR.
WHAT, ARE YOU BORN IN A VACUUM?

1519
01:10:48,412 --> 01:10:50,480
HEY, SLIPPERY GUY,
HE'S PLAYING POSSUM.

1520
01:10:55,685 --> 01:10:58,688
TOLD YOU.

1521
01:10:58,722 --> 01:11:01,758
- WHOOPS.
- [MAN PANTS]

1522
01:11:01,792 --> 01:11:03,993
HEY. HURT, LITTLE FELLA?

1523
01:11:06,397 --> 01:11:07,832
QUICKLY, GIVE ME
YOUR BROTHER'S PACK.

1524
01:11:07,865 --> 01:11:09,333
HOW DO I KNOW IT'S YOU?

1525
01:11:09,367 --> 01:11:11,368
I'M WEARING WHITE,
YOU IDIOT!

1526
01:11:15,505 --> 01:11:17,407
WHAT GOOD IS IT
IF THEY'RE ON THE MOON

1527
01:11:17,440 --> 01:11:20,643
IF THEY JUST RE-ENACT
THE ATROCITIES FROM EARTH?

1528
01:11:24,715 --> 01:11:26,650
THAT'S A GOOD
SEAL IMPRESSION.

1529
01:11:43,267 --> 01:11:46,037
THIS ONE'S GOING
BACK TO THE STORE.

1530
01:11:46,070 --> 01:11:47,503
- YES?
- I THINK I MAY JUST PUT ON

1531
01:11:47,537 --> 01:11:49,338
THE WASTE CONTAINER.

1532
01:11:49,372 --> 01:11:52,275
WHATEVER'S IN HERE,
IT ISN'T AIR.

1533
01:11:52,308 --> 01:11:53,577
HOW DO WE GET OUT OF HERE?

1534
01:11:53,610 --> 01:11:57,013
OUR BUG'S RIDDEN OFF.

1535
01:11:57,047 --> 01:11:59,248
LET'S TRY THIS ONE.

1536
01:11:59,282 --> 01:12:01,352
YEAH, IT'S GOT
LAWN ATTACHMENTS

1537
01:12:01,385 --> 01:12:02,953
AND A BLAUPUNKT STEREO.

1538
01:12:02,987 --> 01:12:05,655
FACTORY AIR. THE WORKS.

1539
01:12:13,297 --> 01:12:15,798
OH MAN, IT SMELLS LIKE
A MUSHROOM FACTORY IN HERE.

1540
01:12:15,832 --> 01:12:19,603
THOSE GUYS WERE REALLY EVIL.

1541
01:12:19,637 --> 01:12:20,937
LEAVE YOUR SUIT ON.

1542
01:12:20,970 --> 01:12:22,807
IT'S 200 DEGREES
BELOW ZERO IN HERE.

1543
01:12:22,840 --> 01:12:24,207
WHAT'S THE WIND CHILL,
THOUGH?

1544
01:12:24,240 --> 01:12:26,543
CAN'T WE TURN
THE HEATING ON?

1545
01:12:31,915 --> 01:12:33,250
OH, IT'S ALL SHOT TO HELL.

1546
01:12:33,283 --> 01:12:34,585
WHAT, THE PLOT?

1547
01:12:34,618 --> 01:12:36,753
AND WE'VE ONLY GOT POWER
FOR ABOUT 150 MILES.

1548
01:12:36,787 --> 01:12:39,490
BUT NOT FOR HEATING
AND COOLING AS WELL.

1549
01:12:39,523 --> 01:12:41,692
WE'LL HAVE TO STAY
IN OUR SUITS ALL THE WAY.

1550
01:12:41,725 --> 01:12:43,293
WE CAN'T DO THAT EITHER.

1551
01:12:43,327 --> 01:12:45,928
OUR CHARGES WON'T LAST
MORE THAN A FEW HOURS.

1552
01:12:45,962 --> 01:12:47,463
150 MILES.

1553
01:12:47,497 --> 01:12:49,398
- LET'S BEAT IT.
- THAT'S OVER 200 MILES--

1554
01:12:49,432 --> 01:12:51,402
MY CHARGE IS
WEARING OUT, TOO.

1555
01:12:51,435 --> 01:12:52,937
--BUT THIS THING'S BUILT
TO GO OVER MOUNTAINS.

1556
01:12:52,970 --> 01:12:54,370
OH, HE ALWAYS SAYS THAT

1557
01:12:54,403 --> 01:12:57,640
WHEN HE GETS IN TROUBLE
AND GETS LOST.

1558
01:13:09,953 --> 01:13:11,655
BOY, SERVO,
WHAT A GREAT MOVIE.

1559
01:13:11,688 --> 01:13:12,990
GREAT ACTRESSES, TOO.

1560
01:13:13,023 --> 01:13:14,992
I LIKE THE BABE
WITH THE GREAT HAIRCUT.

1561
01:13:15,025 --> 01:13:17,727
THE ONE WITH THE EDDIE MUNSTER
PAGE BOY LOOK?

1562
01:13:17,760 --> 01:13:19,763
NAH, I LIKE
THE GATOR-HEADED CHICK.

1563
01:13:19,797 --> 01:13:21,898
THE ONE WITH THE EEL-SKIN
SKULL CAP? NO WAY.

1564
01:13:21,932 --> 01:13:23,233
- UGH.
- HEY, WATCH IT!

1565
01:13:23,267 --> 01:13:24,902
YOU'RE TALKING ABOUT
THE WOMAN I LOVE HERE.

1566
01:13:24,935 --> 01:13:27,003
SHE'S GOT STYLE.
SHE'S GOT LOOKS.

1567
01:13:27,037 --> 01:13:28,805
SHE'S GOT A .45
STRAPPED TO EACH THIGH,

1568
01:13:28,838 --> 01:13:30,540
AND SHE KNOWS
HOW TO USE 'EM.

1569
01:13:30,573 --> 01:13:31,908
SHE'S A DARN SIGHT
BETTER THAN

1570
01:13:31,942 --> 01:13:34,277
THAT TWIGGY LITTLE STICK-WOMAN
YOU HAVE YOUR EYES ON.

1571
01:13:34,310 --> 01:13:35,812
HEY, WHAT ARE YOU SAYING?

1572
01:13:35,845 --> 01:13:38,782
ALL I'M SAYING IS THAT
YOU LITTLE THIN-LIMBED

1573
01:13:38,815 --> 01:13:40,517
SCRAWNY EMPTY-HEADED TYPES

1574
01:13:40,550 --> 01:13:42,118
SEEM TO STICK TOGETHER
SO WELL.

1575
01:13:42,152 --> 01:13:44,855
YOU WANNA PIECE OF ME?
I'M STANDING RIGHT HERE.

1576
01:13:44,888 --> 01:13:48,392
WHEN THIS IS OVER, YOU AND ME
GOING ROUND AND ROUND.

1577
01:13:48,425 --> 01:13:49,727
BOTTO-Á-BOTTO.

1578
01:13:49,760 --> 01:13:51,060
HEY, COME ON, YOU GUYS.

1579
01:13:51,093 --> 01:13:53,063
WHAT'S GOING ON?
BREAK IT UP HERE.

1580
01:13:53,097 --> 01:13:55,165
- WHAT'S THE PROBLEM?
- HEY, STAY OUT OF THIS, JOEL.

1581
01:13:55,198 --> 01:13:57,902
THIS IS BETWEEN ME
AND THE FIREPLUG.

1582
01:13:57,935 --> 01:13:59,468
THAT'S IT, THAT'S IT!
STAND BACK, JOEL!

1583
01:13:59,502 --> 01:14:01,872
YOU'RE USING MY OXYGEN!
COME ON, LET'S GO.

1584
01:14:01,905 --> 01:14:03,907
LISTEN, YOU GUYS,
IF THERE'S GONNA BE A FIGHT,

1585
01:14:03,940 --> 01:14:06,410
WE'RE GONNA DO IT MY WAY.

1586
01:14:06,443 --> 01:14:08,945
NOT THAT--

1587
01:14:14,818 --> 01:14:16,987
I'LL... GET...

1588
01:14:17,020 --> 01:14:18,988
YOU...

1589
01:14:19,022 --> 01:14:21,192
I WANT YOUR HEAD...

1590
01:14:21,225 --> 01:14:23,827
ON A PLA-- AH!...

1591
01:14:32,068 --> 01:14:34,705
[BOTS SHOUT]

1592
01:14:38,142 --> 01:14:39,577
STAY OUT OF THIS...

1593
01:14:39,610 --> 01:14:43,347
JOEL...

1594
01:14:43,380 --> 01:14:45,315
TURN IT OFF!...

1595
01:14:51,788 --> 01:14:53,490
WHOA!

1596
01:14:53,523 --> 01:14:55,825
KIDS, WHEN YOU GOT A BEEF,

1597
01:14:55,858 --> 01:14:58,328
DON'T TAKE THE LAW
INTO YOUR OWN HANDS.

1598
01:14:58,362 --> 01:15:00,597
TAKE IT TO ZERO-G.

1599
01:15:00,630 --> 01:15:02,598
ANTI-GRAVITY.

1600
01:15:02,632 --> 01:15:05,635
IT'S NOT JUST
FOR BREAKFAST ANYMORE.

1601
01:15:14,110 --> 01:15:16,280
WE'RE GOING TO MAKE IT.

1602
01:15:16,313 --> 01:15:18,748
WHAT, ARE THEY DRIVING
THROUGH SNACK CANYON?

1603
01:15:25,255 --> 01:15:27,123
FEH ON YOU.

1604
01:15:35,832 --> 01:15:38,768
THIS IS WHERE IT STARTS.

1605
01:15:38,802 --> 01:15:41,972
IT'LL TAKE
A LITTLE TIME YET.

1606
01:15:42,005 --> 01:15:44,473
AUTOMATIC PILOT.

1607
01:15:51,648 --> 01:15:53,050
BOY, I MUST HAVE
THE ZACTLIES.

1608
01:15:53,083 --> 01:15:55,918
MY SUIT'S PRETTY STEAMY.

1609
01:15:55,952 --> 01:15:57,687
YOU'D BETTER TURN
YOUR INSULATION OFF

1610
01:15:57,720 --> 01:15:59,155
TO SAVE THE LAST
OF THE CHARGE.

1611
01:15:59,188 --> 01:16:01,692
WE MIGHT NEED IT LATER ON.

1612
01:16:05,095 --> 01:16:07,363
OW, THERE'S HAIR BACK THERE.

1613
01:16:07,397 --> 01:16:09,700
HOW FAR NOW?

1614
01:16:12,802 --> 01:16:14,103
ABOUT 80 MILES.

1615
01:16:14,137 --> 01:16:15,938
IT LOOKS AS THOUGH
THE WORST IS OVER.

1616
01:16:15,972 --> 01:16:17,975
SEEMS PRETTY FLAT FROM HERE.

1617
01:16:18,008 --> 01:16:19,442
JUST WHEN WE NEED THE SHADE.

1618
01:16:24,715 --> 01:16:26,248
TAKE OFF YOUR MOON SUIT.

1619
01:16:26,282 --> 01:16:27,950
HE ASKED HER, HE ASKED HER!

1620
01:16:27,983 --> 01:16:31,087
BOY, I WISH I WAS HIM.

1621
01:16:31,120 --> 01:16:33,090
WHAT'RE YOU GONNA DO NOW?

1622
01:16:33,123 --> 01:16:34,992
NOW THAT YOU'RE NOT GONNA
WORK WITH YOUR BROTHER.

1623
01:16:35,025 --> 01:16:37,160
- I'M GOING TO DISNEYWORLD.
- BACK TO EARTH?

1624
01:16:37,193 --> 01:16:40,963
UH, WHO SAID SHE'S NOT
WORKING WITH HER BROTHER?

1625
01:16:40,997 --> 01:16:42,332
HER BROTHER'S DEAD.

1626
01:16:42,365 --> 01:16:44,868
ANY JOBS GOING FOR A GOOD
SPACESHIPPING CLERK UP HERE?

1627
01:16:44,902 --> 01:16:46,135
- OH.
- COULD BE.

1628
01:16:46,168 --> 01:16:48,605
THAT'S A BAD THING.

1629
01:16:52,742 --> 01:16:54,410
THANKS.

1630
01:16:54,443 --> 01:16:56,880
OH, THAT FEELS GOOD, THANKS.

1631
01:16:56,913 --> 01:17:00,750
I'M SORRY I DRAGGED YOU
INTO ALL OF THIS.

1632
01:17:00,783 --> 01:17:02,552
I'M NOT.

1633
01:17:02,585 --> 01:17:04,053
IT'D BE A BIT SILLY
FOR BILL KEMP

1634
01:17:04,087 --> 01:17:05,722
TO DIE JUST HERE.

1635
01:17:05,755 --> 01:17:07,157
ON THE MOON.

1636
01:17:07,190 --> 01:17:09,927
AFTER ALL THE PLACES
YOU'VE BEEN, I MEAN.

1637
01:17:09,960 --> 01:17:13,063
IT'D BE A BIT SILLY FOR
BILL KEMP TO DIE ANYPLACE,

1638
01:17:13,097 --> 01:17:15,432
AS FAR AS I'M CONCERNED.
SO SIT DOWN,

1639
01:17:15,465 --> 01:17:18,735
AND START TELLING ME
HOW MUCH FARTHER WE HAVE TO GO.

1640
01:17:23,038 --> 01:17:25,908
GOTTA GET PAST
HIS ATTITUDE FIRST.

1641
01:17:25,942 --> 01:17:28,278
WHOA, JOEL, GIVE ME A HAND,
I'M SHORTING OUT HERE--

1642
01:17:28,312 --> 01:17:29,612
- WHAT IS THIS?
- OH, IT'S JUST THE FILM.

1643
01:17:29,645 --> 01:17:31,382
- DON'T WORRY, SERVO.
- FOCUS!

1644
01:17:31,415 --> 01:17:33,650
WHOO.

1645
01:17:33,683 --> 01:17:37,120
OH, HONEY, COULD YOU PUT
SOME MORE WATER ON THOSE ROCKS?

1646
01:17:38,888 --> 01:17:41,525
WHOO, NOTHING BETTER
THAN THIS.

1647
01:17:41,558 --> 01:17:44,227
- THIS IS THE LIFE.
- IS THERE ANY WATER LEFT?

1648
01:17:44,260 --> 01:17:46,863
JUST THE GALLONS
YOU'RE PUTTING OUT.

1649
01:17:54,737 --> 01:17:56,272
CHINESE AGAIN.

1650
01:18:02,278 --> 01:18:05,048
- THAT'S MY SPECIMEN.
- IT'S DAMN NEAR BOILING.

1651
01:18:11,588 --> 01:18:12,988
WELL? WHAT'S THE MATTER?

1652
01:18:13,022 --> 01:18:15,425
- YOWZA.
- NOTHING FROM WHERE
I'M STANDING.

1653
01:18:15,458 --> 01:18:17,927
[CROW WHISTLES]

1654
01:18:17,960 --> 01:18:20,030
NOT A THING.

1655
01:18:20,063 --> 01:18:21,632
I KNEW THERE HAD TO BE
A GOOD PART OF THIS MOVIE.

1656
01:18:21,665 --> 01:18:22,965
IF IT GETS ANY HOTTER,

1657
01:18:22,998 --> 01:18:24,902
I'LL VERY LIKELY
TAKE THE REST OF IT OFF.

1658
01:18:24,935 --> 01:18:26,770
HEY, PRAY FOR HEAT, HUH?

1659
01:18:26,803 --> 01:18:28,070
[BOTS] YEAH.

1660
01:18:28,103 --> 01:18:29,672
[BOTS BUZZ]

1661
01:18:34,277 --> 01:18:35,812
HOW MUCH FARTHER?

1662
01:18:35,845 --> 01:18:38,715
WELL, THE SCRIPT SAYS
A FEW MORE MILES.

1663
01:18:41,317 --> 01:18:42,785
ONLY A FEW MILES.

1664
01:18:42,818 --> 01:18:45,355
HOW MANY FEW?

1665
01:18:45,388 --> 01:18:47,290
I DON'T KNOW. SEVEN? TEN?

1666
01:18:47,323 --> 01:18:49,492
- WHICH IS IT? SEVEN OR TEN?
- ♪♪ [TRUMPET]

1667
01:18:49,525 --> 01:18:51,093
I'M SORRY, BUT SEVEN MEANS
WE MIGHT MAKE IT.

1668
01:18:51,127 --> 01:18:53,230
- TEN MEANS WE WON'T.
- WHAT'S THE TRUMPET MEAN?

1669
01:18:53,263 --> 01:18:55,032
LOOK, WE'VE GOT POWER
FOR ANOTHER COUPLE OF MILES.

1670
01:18:55,065 --> 01:18:56,800
THEN WE WALK.
WE'VE GOT AN HOUR'S

1671
01:18:56,833 --> 01:18:59,268
INSULATION CHARGE
LEFT IN THE SUITS.

1672
01:19:07,277 --> 01:19:08,945
SHUT UP THAT JAZZ COMBO.

1673
01:19:08,978 --> 01:19:10,413
I'M NERVOUS ENOUGH AS IT IS.

1674
01:19:10,447 --> 01:19:13,048
THE OVERHEATING HAS MELTED
THE PRESSURE FLOOD.

1675
01:19:13,082 --> 01:19:14,852
I ONLY HOPE--

1676
01:19:17,853 --> 01:19:19,522
QUICK! INTO YOUR SUIT.

1677
01:19:19,555 --> 01:19:21,858
OH, DAMN, I THOUGHT WE WERE
TAKING THE SUITS OFF.

1678
01:19:30,100 --> 01:19:33,970
SUICIDE DOOR.

1679
01:19:34,003 --> 01:19:36,507
THOSE EXPLODER BOATS
COME IN HANDY.

1680
01:19:36,540 --> 01:19:38,040
OF COURSE
IT'S GONNA EXPLODE.

1681
01:19:38,073 --> 01:19:39,575
THEY PARKED OVER A CAMPFIRE.

1682
01:19:44,413 --> 01:19:47,483
QUICK, IN THE CRACK.

1683
01:19:47,517 --> 01:19:50,720
WAIT! OH, THE JAZZ COMBO
WAS STILL IN THERE.

1684
01:19:50,753 --> 01:19:54,523
THE DAY THE MUSIC DIED.

1685
01:19:54,557 --> 01:19:56,560
GUESS THEY
WON'T TRY THAT AGAIN.

1686
01:19:59,862 --> 01:20:01,865
WHO DECIDED FREE-FORM JAZZ

1687
01:20:01,898 --> 01:20:04,133
WAS THE RIGHT THING
FOR THE SOUNDTRACK?

1688
01:20:07,437 --> 01:20:08,838
LOOK!

1689
01:20:11,440 --> 01:20:14,443
IT'S FAR SIDE FIVE. COME ON.

1690
01:20:14,477 --> 01:20:17,280
THEY MAKE A GREAT BURGER.
LET'S BEAT CHEEKS.

1691
01:20:17,313 --> 01:20:18,648
ALL RIGHT, BILL.

1692
01:20:18,682 --> 01:20:21,852
- YOU'RE UNDER ARREST.
- BEAT THE RUSH.

1693
01:20:21,885 --> 01:20:23,320
FINE.

1694
01:20:23,353 --> 01:20:26,890
NOW, HAS ANYBODY GOT
A NICE, COOL DRINK?

1695
01:20:26,923 --> 01:20:28,625
DON'T SAY HI.

1696
01:20:28,658 --> 01:20:30,760
HOPE HE LIKES ROCKET FUEL.

1697
01:20:37,500 --> 01:20:40,370
SHE JUST FLOPPED DOWN
ON THAT FORMICA.

1698
01:20:40,403 --> 01:20:42,405
--SUDDENLY APPEARED.

1699
01:20:42,438 --> 01:20:45,142
SHE ALWAYS GETS
HER MAN, BILL.

1700
01:20:47,210 --> 01:20:48,512
WELL, YOU'VE REALLY BEEN

1701
01:20:48,545 --> 01:20:50,713
RUNNING UP AN ACCOUNT
THIS TIME.

1702
01:20:50,747 --> 01:20:52,782
YEAH, AND YOU'RE THE ONE
WITH THE FUNNY SKULL.

1703
01:20:52,815 --> 01:20:54,783
--BREACH THE PRESSURE
OF AN OUTSIDE ROOM.

1704
01:20:54,817 --> 01:20:56,820
MALICIOUS DAMAGE
TO HOTEL PROPERTY.

1705
01:20:56,853 --> 01:21:00,723
MS. TAPLIN'S BROTHER
HAS BEEN MURDERED OUT THERE.

1706
01:21:00,757 --> 01:21:02,858
COME ON.

1707
01:21:02,892 --> 01:21:05,728
YOU CAN DO BETTER THAN THAT.

1708
01:21:05,762 --> 01:21:07,630
YES, WELL, THREE OTHER
CHARACTERS GOT KILLED,

1709
01:21:07,663 --> 01:21:09,098
BUT I DID THAT MYSELF.

1710
01:21:09,132 --> 01:21:10,800
WHEN YOU GET INTO TROUBLE,

1711
01:21:10,833 --> 01:21:13,603
YOU REALLY JUMP OFF
THE TOP BOARD, DON'T YOU.

1712
01:21:13,637 --> 01:21:15,838
SHE'S REALLY GOT SORT OF
A JULIE ANDREWS QUALITY,

1713
01:21:15,872 --> 01:21:18,040
- DOESN'T SHE?
- YEAH, I THINK SHE GOT
THAT SKULL CAP

1714
01:21:18,073 --> 01:21:20,543
FROM THOROUGHLY MODERN MILLIE.

1715
01:21:22,445 --> 01:21:24,913
ONE THING WE CAN CHECK
RIGHT NOW.

1716
01:21:24,947 --> 01:21:26,650
WALLY TAPLIN WAS KILLED

1717
01:21:26,683 --> 01:21:30,420
WITH ONE OF THESE.

1718
01:21:30,453 --> 01:21:32,788
TELL ME WHAT YOU THINK
IT SMELLS LIKE.

1719
01:21:32,822 --> 01:21:34,723
- CHEESE BALLS.
- UH, PINE FOREST?

1720
01:21:34,757 --> 01:21:36,592
- WATERMELON?
- WET CANVAS?

1721
01:21:36,625 --> 01:21:39,695
JUST ONE SNIFF.

1722
01:21:39,728 --> 01:21:41,197
COULD BE CYANIDE.

1723
01:21:41,230 --> 01:21:44,600
CYANIDE? THAT'S MY FAVORITE.

1724
01:21:44,633 --> 01:21:47,103
FUNNY, I JUST TOOK IT OFF
MY OWN SUIT.

1725
01:21:47,137 --> 01:21:48,738
SMELLS LIKE ME.

1726
01:21:48,772 --> 01:21:50,840
AND I DIDN'T LIKE
THAT WET CANVAS CRACK EITHER.

1727
01:21:50,873 --> 01:21:53,910
--FRESH AIR TO ME.

1728
01:21:53,943 --> 01:21:56,813
BUT YOU THOUGHT
IT WAS CYANIDE.

1729
01:21:56,847 --> 01:21:58,348
NOW, YOU SOLD HIM
HIS AIR BOTTLES.

1730
01:21:58,382 --> 01:22:00,717
YOU SELL ALL AIR BOTTLES
AROUND HERE.

1731
01:22:00,750 --> 01:22:02,185
UH, YEAH,
BUT I DISTINCTLY REMEMBER

1732
01:22:02,218 --> 01:22:03,953
NOT SELLING THAT AIR BOTTLE.

1733
01:22:03,987 --> 01:22:06,957
YOU'D BETTER ANSWER HIM.

1734
01:22:06,990 --> 01:22:08,358
THEY-- THEY MADE ME.

1735
01:22:08,392 --> 01:22:10,093
THEY WANTED TAPLIN'S CLAIM.

1736
01:22:10,127 --> 01:22:11,828
IT WAS DUE TO EXPIRE!

1737
01:22:11,862 --> 01:22:13,463
IT SEEMS
THEY'D FOUND SOMETHING.

1738
01:22:13,497 --> 01:22:15,498
AND THEY HAD TO HAVE IT.

1739
01:22:15,532 --> 01:22:17,367
WHAT FOR?

1740
01:22:20,637 --> 01:22:23,640
- TELL HIM.
- TO LAND AN ASTEROID ON IT.

1741
01:22:25,708 --> 01:22:28,077
PIZZA'S READY.

1742
01:22:28,110 --> 01:22:30,313
IT'S A BRAND NEW CAR!

1743
01:22:35,585 --> 01:22:37,953
MR. HUBBARD,
THEY FOUND OUT ABOUT IT.

1744
01:22:37,987 --> 01:22:39,688
YOU'VE GOT TO GET ME
OFF THE MOON.

1745
01:22:39,722 --> 01:22:41,323
[CROW AS KLINK]
HOGAN, I WOULDN'T SAY ANY MORE

1746
01:22:41,357 --> 01:22:43,860
ABOUT THAT IF I WERE YOU.

1747
01:22:43,893 --> 01:22:46,930
YOU'VE REACHED
THE CONFESSION STAGE.

1748
01:22:46,963 --> 01:22:50,433
AND IN FRONT OF
THE BUREAU OF INVESTIGATION.

1749
01:22:50,467 --> 01:22:52,702
IS THAT WRONG?
SHOULD I HAVE NOT DONE THAT?

1750
01:22:52,735 --> 01:22:54,737
I'M GLAD WE GOT HERE
ON TIME, MR. KEMP.

1751
01:22:54,770 --> 01:22:56,438
I WAS AFRAID
SOME OF MY ASSOCIATES--

1752
01:22:56,472 --> 01:22:58,140
NEVER TRUST A MAN
WITH A COLLAR

1753
01:22:58,173 --> 01:22:59,542
MADE OF SHINYL VINYL.

1754
01:22:59,575 --> 01:23:02,345
--THIS PROJECT AND WOULD HAVE
DISPOSED OF YOU.

1755
01:23:02,378 --> 01:23:04,113
THEY TRIED.

1756
01:23:04,147 --> 01:23:06,515
REALLY? ALL THREE OF THEM?

1757
01:23:06,548 --> 01:23:07,883
ALL THREE.

1758
01:23:07,917 --> 01:23:10,487
EVEN RASPBERRY RED?

1759
01:23:10,520 --> 01:23:11,855
I REALLY DID

1760
01:23:11,888 --> 01:23:14,690
UNDERESTIMATE YOU,
MR. KEMP.

1761
01:23:14,723 --> 01:23:18,428
SO WE'RE THREE MEN
SHORT, THEN.

1762
01:23:18,462 --> 01:23:20,063
WE SHOULD MAKE
A NOTE TO ENGAGE.

1763
01:23:20,097 --> 01:23:22,465
MR. HUBBARD?

1764
01:23:22,498 --> 01:23:24,567
YOU'RE UNDER ARREST.

1765
01:23:24,600 --> 01:23:26,870
I DON'T THINK SO.

1766
01:23:26,903 --> 01:23:28,438
DO YOU, HARRY?

1767
01:23:28,472 --> 01:23:31,073
UH, I'M SORRY, I WAS
DREAMING ABOUT RABBITS.

1768
01:23:34,443 --> 01:23:35,978
LET ME GET THIS STRAIGHT.

1769
01:23:36,012 --> 01:23:37,847
YOU GOT THAT LOUSE
TO MURDER MY BROTHER

1770
01:23:37,880 --> 01:23:39,948
JUST SO THAT YOU COULD HAVE
A PLACE TO LAND AN ASTEROID?

1771
01:23:39,982 --> 01:23:41,818
UH, IN A NUTSHELL, YEAH.

1772
01:23:41,852 --> 01:23:43,152
OH!

1773
01:23:43,185 --> 01:23:44,853
SPEAKING OF NUTSHELLS.

1774
01:23:52,162 --> 01:23:54,797
OH, WELL, I'LL GET THAT.
THAT'S OKAY, NOT A PROBLEM.

1775
01:23:54,830 --> 01:23:56,265
MR. KENT, PLEASE.

1776
01:23:56,298 --> 01:23:58,000
DON'T GET YOURSELF KILLED

1777
01:23:58,033 --> 01:24:00,237
- UNNECESSARILY.
- UH, OKAY.

1778
01:24:00,270 --> 01:24:02,405
HEY, ARE THOSE FRENCH CUFFS?

1779
01:24:06,075 --> 01:24:08,945
I SUPPOSE I LOOK
RATHER SILLY TO YOU, BILL.

1780
01:24:08,978 --> 01:24:11,280
DON'T THINK...

1781
01:24:11,313 --> 01:24:13,983
I'M GONNA BE ABLE TO GET YOU
OUT OF THIS ONE.

1782
01:24:14,017 --> 01:24:16,318
- THIS TIME, BILL.
- DON'T TALK, LIZ.

1783
01:24:18,253 --> 01:24:19,922
I'M GONNA--

1784
01:24:19,955 --> 01:24:22,092
GONNA MISS YOU, BILL.

1785
01:24:22,125 --> 01:24:24,427
EVEN THE--

1786
01:24:24,460 --> 01:24:27,663
THE ROWS WERE GOOD.

1787
01:24:27,697 --> 01:24:30,967
BURY MY TURTLE HAT
AT WOUNDED KNEE.

1788
01:24:34,370 --> 01:24:35,905
WE'RE QUITE SAFE, SIR.
NONE OF THE SHOTS

1789
01:24:35,938 --> 01:24:37,607
PIERCED THE DOME.

1790
01:24:37,640 --> 01:24:39,375
YES, WELL, I BELIEVE
WE NEED TO TAKE OFF

1791
01:24:39,408 --> 01:24:43,245
FOR THE ASTEROID
IN JUST UNDER ONE HOUR.

1792
01:24:43,278 --> 01:24:44,813
IF YOU THINK I'M GONNA

1793
01:24:44,847 --> 01:24:46,482
LAND THAT THING
FOR YOU NOW, YOU'RE--

1794
01:24:46,515 --> 01:24:49,052
BUT I DO.

1795
01:24:49,085 --> 01:24:51,420
WHITSUN,
WHEN WAS THE LAST TIME

1796
01:24:51,453 --> 01:24:54,257
WE ABANDONED A PROJECT
WITHOUT ANY PROFIT?

1797
01:24:54,290 --> 01:24:55,658
- STONEHENGE.
- OH, YES, I REMEMBER.

1798
01:24:55,692 --> 01:24:56,927
THERE WAS NO OIL THERE,
WAS THERE?

1799
01:24:56,960 --> 01:24:58,260
- NO, SIR.
- NO, BUT THERE IS SAPPHIRE

1800
01:24:58,293 --> 01:25:01,130
IN THIS ASTEROID,
MR. KEMP, SO...

1801
01:25:01,163 --> 01:25:03,232
IF SHE'S DEAD,
I COULD SCOOP HER OUT

1802
01:25:03,265 --> 01:25:05,235
AND MAKE A TERRARIUM
OUT OF HER.

1803
01:25:08,638 --> 01:25:12,075
SOMEBODY SAY SOMETHING.

1804
01:25:12,108 --> 01:25:13,743
HARRY.

1805
01:25:13,777 --> 01:25:16,212
SHOOT THE YOUNG LADY.

1806
01:25:16,245 --> 01:25:18,047
UH, WHICH ONE?

1807
01:25:18,080 --> 01:25:20,048
THE ONE THAT'S NOT DEAD,
YOU IDIOT!

1808
01:25:20,082 --> 01:25:22,152
OH, YEAH-YEAH-YEAH.
RIGHT, RIGHT.

1809
01:25:25,020 --> 01:25:26,655
ALL RIGHT, OKAY, DON'T MOVE.

1810
01:25:38,133 --> 01:25:40,237
THAT'S BETTER.

1811
01:25:40,270 --> 01:25:42,005
MUCH.

1812
01:25:53,082 --> 01:25:54,883
$200,000

1813
01:25:54,917 --> 01:25:57,653
IN THE GEM MARKET.

1814
01:25:57,687 --> 01:25:59,722
YOU KIDS BE CAREFUL
DOWN THERE.

1815
01:25:59,755 --> 01:26:01,290
--FOR FULL RETRO EFFECT.

1816
01:26:01,323 --> 01:26:04,093
WE CAN ARRANGE THAT
BY FIRING TWO ENGINES EARLY.

1817
01:26:04,127 --> 01:26:05,795
ONE OF THEM WILL
HAVE TO BE NUMBER THREE.

1818
01:26:05,828 --> 01:26:07,197
JUST REMEMBER THAT.

1819
01:26:07,230 --> 01:26:09,898
- YEAH-YEAH-YEAH, I KNEW THAT.
- --ANTICIPATED THAT.

1820
01:26:09,932 --> 01:26:11,333
GOT MY GUM BACK.

1821
01:26:11,367 --> 01:26:14,370
NUMBER THREE CONTROLS
THE FIRING OF THE OTHERS.

1822
01:26:14,403 --> 01:26:16,005
COME OUT HERE,
WHERE THE BOYFRIEND

1823
01:26:16,038 --> 01:26:18,507
CAN SEE YOU, LOVE.

1824
01:26:18,540 --> 01:26:20,843
SORT OF ENCOURAGE HIM
IN HIS WORK.

1825
01:26:23,545 --> 01:26:25,382
THAT'S IT, BILL.
KEEP IT UP, BUDDY.

1826
01:26:25,415 --> 01:26:28,852
YOU'RE LOOKING GREAT.

1827
01:26:28,885 --> 01:26:30,387
--FOUR AND SEVEN MINUTES,

1828
01:26:30,420 --> 01:26:31,887
IT'LL STILL LAND
ON THE PLAIN.

1829
01:26:31,920 --> 01:26:34,990
NOW, COULD SOMEONE GET ME
A MEDIUM SHERRY?

1830
01:26:35,023 --> 01:26:36,960
VERY NICE ONE? THANK YOU.

1831
01:26:36,993 --> 01:26:38,527
IF I'M GOING
TO STAY DOWN HERE

1832
01:26:38,560 --> 01:26:40,228
AND THUMP
NUMBER THREE AGAIN--

1833
01:26:40,262 --> 01:26:43,198
- I'LL NEED A MAGAZINE.
- I'LL NEED A LONG LINE.

1834
01:26:43,232 --> 01:26:44,733
LIKE A SOLILOQUY
OR A MONOLOGUE?

1835
01:26:44,767 --> 01:26:47,803
MS. TAPLIN?

1836
01:26:47,837 --> 01:26:50,907
THEY'RE UP IN
THE PASSENGER DECK.

1837
01:26:50,940 --> 01:26:53,677
WELL, SHOULD I MAKE COFFEE TOO,
MR. HEFNER?

1838
01:26:58,280 --> 01:27:00,148
THIS IS ONE OF MY
BEST ESCAPE TRICKS EVER.

1839
01:27:00,182 --> 01:27:02,218
I CHAIN MYSELF
TO THIS LADDER, SEE?

1840
01:27:02,252 --> 01:27:03,953
AND THEN-- OH, HI.

1841
01:27:14,430 --> 01:27:15,665
WHAT CAN I DO?

1842
01:27:15,698 --> 01:27:19,502
INTO THE CONTROL DECK,
BILL'S CHAIR.

1843
01:27:19,535 --> 01:27:21,637
DECK, YOU MEAN?

1844
01:27:21,670 --> 01:27:24,507
I THINK THAT'S
EVERYTHING, SIR.

1845
01:27:24,540 --> 01:27:27,510
IT WILL LAND 16 MINUTES
AFTER FIRING.

1846
01:27:27,543 --> 01:27:28,912
GIVE OR TAKE A MILLIONTH
OF A SECOND.

1847
01:27:28,945 --> 01:27:31,080
EXCELLENT TIMING, WHITSUN.

1848
01:27:31,113 --> 01:27:32,882
MR. TAPLIN'S CLAIM EXPIRED

1849
01:27:32,915 --> 01:27:35,117
HALF AN HOUR AGO.

1850
01:27:35,150 --> 01:27:37,053
NO LEGAL PROBLEMS.

1851
01:27:39,555 --> 01:27:41,023
ARE YOU THERE?

1852
01:27:41,057 --> 01:27:42,192
YES.

1853
01:27:42,225 --> 01:27:45,795
ON YOUR RIGHT,
TWO ROWS OF SWITCHES.

1854
01:27:45,828 --> 01:27:49,198
BOTTOM ROW.

1855
01:27:49,232 --> 01:27:52,368
HAS THAT GUY EVER SPOKEN
A COMPLETE SENTENCE?

1856
01:27:52,402 --> 01:27:55,237
- ALL RIGHT?
- WHAT NOW?

1857
01:27:55,270 --> 01:27:56,805
ON YOUR LEFT,

1858
01:27:56,838 --> 01:27:59,742
THE BIG FRONT LEVER.

1859
01:27:59,775 --> 01:28:01,810
PULL IT ALL THE WAY BACK.

1860
01:28:01,843 --> 01:28:05,382
BUT BEFORE YOU DO THAT--

1861
01:28:05,415 --> 01:28:08,483
NOW.

1862
01:28:12,255 --> 01:28:14,123
OH, NO SMOKING
IN YOUR PRESSURE SUIT.

1863
01:28:14,157 --> 01:28:17,060
FIRST RULE IN THE BOOK.

1864
01:28:17,093 --> 01:28:19,662
HOTHEAD.

1865
01:28:19,695 --> 01:28:22,232
I BET HE WON'T
TRY THAT AGAIN.

1866
01:28:22,265 --> 01:28:24,400
CUT THE THROTTLE.

1867
01:28:24,433 --> 01:28:27,337
THE ENGINEER
MUST HAVE GOT FREE.

1868
01:28:27,370 --> 01:28:29,005
[JOEL AS PETER LORRE]
YES...

1869
01:28:29,038 --> 01:28:31,340
--YOU THINK THE GIRL
IS FLYING THAT THING.

1870
01:28:31,373 --> 01:28:34,543
IN THE MAINTENANCE LOCKER,
THERE IS A BUZZSAW.

1871
01:28:34,577 --> 01:28:37,147
MR. KENT, CAN YOUR ENGINEER

1872
01:28:37,180 --> 01:28:39,148
LAND THAT THING ON HIS OWN?

1873
01:28:39,182 --> 01:28:41,117
WELL, HE'S NOT GOOD
AT PARALLEL PARKING,

1874
01:28:41,150 --> 01:28:43,820
BUT IF IT'S A DIAGONAL SPOT,
HE CAN DO IT.

1875
01:28:43,853 --> 01:28:45,220
I DON'T THINK SO.

1876
01:28:45,253 --> 01:28:47,723
THEN HE NEEDS YOU

1877
01:28:47,757 --> 01:28:50,025
AS MUCH AS WE NEED THE SHIP.

1878
01:28:50,058 --> 01:28:51,127
AND VICE-VERSA.

1879
01:28:51,160 --> 01:28:53,395
MR. KAMINSKI,

1880
01:28:53,428 --> 01:28:56,165
IF YOU HEAR ME,

1881
01:28:56,198 --> 01:28:58,868
- ARE YOU READY TO--
- HE COULD'VE JUST GRABBED THAT.

1882
01:29:01,270 --> 01:29:02,572
GO GET HIM, HARRY.

1883
01:29:02,605 --> 01:29:06,042
THAT'S RIGHT, HARRY,
COME AND GET ME.

1884
01:29:06,075 --> 01:29:07,310
HE'S GOT A GUN, MR. HUBBARD.

1885
01:29:07,343 --> 01:29:09,178
I KNOW THAT.

1886
01:29:09,212 --> 01:29:10,947
IT'S YOUR GUN.

1887
01:29:10,980 --> 01:29:13,282
NOW START EARNING YOUR PAY
FOR ONCE.

1888
01:29:13,315 --> 01:29:16,518
UH, I CAN'T SPEND IT
IF I GOT A HOLE THROUGH ME.

1889
01:29:23,927 --> 01:29:25,327
BE REASONABLE, MR. KEMP.

1890
01:29:25,360 --> 01:29:28,430
WE JUST WANNA GET BACK
TO THE MOON SAME AS YOU DO.

1891
01:29:28,463 --> 01:29:30,433
SO LET'S HAVE
NO MORE TROUBLE, PLEASE.

1892
01:29:30,467 --> 01:29:31,733
WATCH YOUR HEAD, HARRY.

1893
01:29:31,767 --> 01:29:33,402
HOW CAN A PERSON
WATCH THEIR OWN HEAD?

1894
01:29:33,435 --> 01:29:35,638
HUH?

1895
01:29:35,672 --> 01:29:38,507
UGH...

1896
01:29:38,540 --> 01:29:41,577
YOU DIDN'T HIT MY HEAD...

1897
01:29:41,610 --> 01:29:44,913
MUSIC TO SHOOT THUGS BY.

1898
01:29:44,947 --> 01:29:48,852
NOW, LET'S BE REASONABLE,
MR. KEMP.

1899
01:29:48,885 --> 01:29:50,753
COME HERE.

1900
01:30:15,110 --> 01:30:18,848
LIGHT BULBS.

1901
01:30:18,882 --> 01:30:20,483
THEY'RE SURFING.

1902
01:30:20,517 --> 01:30:23,218
I CAN FLY! I CAN FLY!

1903
01:30:23,252 --> 01:30:25,922
I'M THE LUCKIEST BOY
IN THE WORLD!

1904
01:30:25,955 --> 01:30:29,392
WELL, STOP IT!

1905
01:30:32,195 --> 01:30:34,230
KLINK, YOU IDIOT!

1906
01:30:34,263 --> 01:30:36,065
- THE BUILDUP OF POWER--
- I WON! I WON!

1907
01:30:36,098 --> 01:30:38,100
I'M THE BEST! I'M THE BEST!

1908
01:30:40,737 --> 01:30:42,872
WORKS EVERY TIME.

1909
01:30:45,675 --> 01:30:48,577
HIGH FIVE? NO,
JUST A HAND IS FINE, THANKS.

1910
01:31:04,860 --> 01:31:07,263
WELL, THEY'LL BE ON THE MOON
BEFORE WE ARE.

1911
01:31:07,297 --> 01:31:09,265
SEAL HER UP.

1912
01:31:09,298 --> 01:31:10,867
WE'LL FOLLOW AS FAR AS WE CAN.

1913
01:31:10,900 --> 01:31:12,568
AND TAKE LOTS OF PICTURES.

1914
01:31:20,342 --> 01:31:22,612
SO LONG, SUCKERS.

1915
01:31:29,018 --> 01:31:31,487
PRESSURE NORMAL. NO LEAKS.

1916
01:31:31,520 --> 01:31:33,788
A FEW LENTILS, THOUGH.

1917
01:31:33,822 --> 01:31:35,892
GOOD ONE.

1918
01:31:35,925 --> 01:31:38,093
SOUP LOVERS WILL GET IT.

1919
01:31:43,865 --> 01:31:45,167
UNITED NATIONS SPACE--

1920
01:31:45,200 --> 01:31:46,902
SHE MISSED HIS FOREHEAD.
THAT'S PRETTY TOUGH TO DO.

1921
01:31:46,935 --> 01:31:50,807
--99B, NO SEX
IS PERMITTED IN SPACE.

1922
01:31:50,840 --> 01:31:53,008
IT'S PROBABLY BECAUSE
OF THE FIBERGLASS SUITS.

1923
01:31:53,042 --> 01:31:55,812
--MOST OF THEM.
NOBODY ELSE HAS READ IT, EITHER.

1924
01:31:58,080 --> 01:32:00,548
WOW, APPARENTLY I'M DEAD.

1925
01:32:00,582 --> 01:32:03,552
THEY'LL REACH THE MOON
IN EXACTLY ONE MINUTE.

1926
01:32:03,585 --> 01:32:05,187
- ON TARGET?
- ON TARGET.

1927
01:32:05,220 --> 01:32:07,390
AND WHOEVER TAKES OVER
FROM HUBBARD

1928
01:32:07,423 --> 01:32:10,258
GETS 6,000 TONS OF SAPPHIRE.

1929
01:32:10,292 --> 01:32:13,195
THAT MAKES YOU
A VERY ATTRACTIVE WOMAN.

1930
01:32:13,228 --> 01:32:15,130
I'M ALREADY ATTRACTIVE.

1931
01:32:15,163 --> 01:32:17,367
--WAS MURDERED,
AND THAT HE'D FOUND NICKEL.

1932
01:32:17,400 --> 01:32:19,168
- YEAH, GO ON.
- --ALLOWED,

1933
01:32:19,202 --> 01:32:20,703
PROFIT BY MURDER.

1934
01:32:20,737 --> 01:32:23,872
- HMM.
- FIVE SECONDS.

1935
01:32:23,905 --> 01:32:25,708
FOUR.

1936
01:32:25,742 --> 01:32:27,510
THREE.

1937
01:32:27,543 --> 01:32:28,877
YEAH! YEE-HA!

1938
01:32:28,910 --> 01:32:31,013
- YOU'RE FIRED, SPARKY.
- YAHOO!

1939
01:32:31,047 --> 01:32:34,150
- WHOO!
- WHOO-HOO-HOO!

1940
01:32:34,183 --> 01:32:35,885
♪ MOON ZERO TWO ♪

1941
01:32:35,918 --> 01:32:39,188
--MADE HIS MARK
ON THE MOON, ALL RIGHT.

1942
01:32:39,222 --> 01:32:42,658
FUNNY.

1943
01:32:42,692 --> 01:32:44,793
COURSE FOR MOON CITY.

1944
01:32:47,262 --> 01:32:48,497
OH, BY THE WAY,

1945
01:32:48,530 --> 01:32:51,467
WHAT'S YOUR ROOM
AT THE HOTEL LIKE?

1946
01:32:52,735 --> 01:32:56,305
WHY DON'T YOU FIND OUT?

1947
01:32:56,338 --> 01:32:57,640
I DON'T GET IT,
WHAT DO YOU MEAN?

1948
01:32:57,673 --> 01:32:59,375
ALL RIGHT!

1949
01:32:59,408 --> 01:33:00,943
SHE WANT HIM TO PAINT
OR SOMETHING?

1950
01:33:00,977 --> 01:33:02,612
YEAH.

1951
01:33:02,645 --> 01:33:06,115
THEY ALSO HAVE
A PAINT CONTRACTING OUTFIT.

1952
01:33:06,148 --> 01:33:08,317
I HOPE THIS TURNS BACK
INTO A CARTOON,

1953
01:33:08,350 --> 01:33:10,118
KIND OF TO SEAL
THE WHOLE THING UP.

1954
01:33:10,152 --> 01:33:11,720
- YEAH.
- BOOKEND IT.

1955
01:33:11,753 --> 01:33:13,155
- WHAT?
- KIND OF BOOKEND IT.

1956
01:33:13,188 --> 01:33:15,992
YEAH. YEAH.

1957
01:33:16,025 --> 01:33:18,793
WHAT IS THAT ONE SONG?

1958
01:33:18,827 --> 01:33:20,395
OH, THE WIENER MAN SONG?

1959
01:33:20,428 --> 01:33:21,797
YEAH, HOW DOES THAT GO?

1960
01:33:21,830 --> 01:33:23,798
- OH, UM--
- OH, WE HAVE TO GET
OUT OF HERE.

1961
01:33:23,832 --> 01:33:25,433
♪ I WANNA BE
YOUR WIENER MAN ♪

1962
01:33:25,467 --> 01:33:26,702
♪ I WILL BE
YOUR WIENER FAN ♪

1963
01:33:26,735 --> 01:33:29,472
- YEAH.
- ♪ WIENERS... ♪

1964
01:33:41,450 --> 01:33:43,185
ALL RIGHT, IT'S THE END
OF THE MOVIE.

1965
01:33:43,218 --> 01:33:44,620
HEY, GYPSY, HOW YOU DOING?

1966
01:33:44,653 --> 01:33:46,155
- OH, FINE.
- GOOD, OKAY,

1967
01:33:46,188 --> 01:33:48,390
- IT'S GOOD TO HAVE YOU BACK.
- I LOVE YOU, JOEL.

1968
01:33:48,423 --> 01:33:50,058
THANK YOU, GYPSY.
YOU'RE GOOD. OKAY.

1969
01:33:50,092 --> 01:33:51,593
NOW, YOU KNOW
WHAT WE'RE GONNA DO NEXT

1970
01:33:51,627 --> 01:33:53,628
IS DO MOVIE REVIEW GAME.

1971
01:33:53,662 --> 01:33:55,832
AND THAT MEANS,
TELL ME A GOOD THING

1972
01:33:55,865 --> 01:33:57,800
AND A BAD THING
ABOUT THE MOVIE.

1973
01:33:57,833 --> 01:34:00,068
AND YOU GET A RAM CHIP.

1974
01:34:00,102 --> 01:34:01,970
- [BOTS CHEER]
- RIGHT, A RAM CHIP.

1975
01:34:02,003 --> 01:34:04,373
OKAY, TOM SERVO.
YOU GO FIRST.

1976
01:34:04,407 --> 01:34:07,242
WELL, THIS MOVIE
MADE MY GORGE RISE.

1977
01:34:07,275 --> 01:34:09,078
OKAY, AND A BAD THING?

1978
01:34:09,112 --> 01:34:11,347
OKAY, SERIOUSLY.

1979
01:34:11,380 --> 01:34:13,915
I THOUGHT THAT THE MOVIE
PROVIDED AN OPPORTUNITY FOR US

1980
01:34:13,948 --> 01:34:15,683
TO EXAMINE
THE VARIOUS INACCURACIES

1981
01:34:15,717 --> 01:34:18,020
OFTEN PORTRAYED
IN ERSATZ SPACE MOVIES,

1982
01:34:18,053 --> 01:34:19,355
SUCH AS THIS ONE.

1983
01:34:19,388 --> 01:34:21,457
I SEE, YOU'RE REALLY
BUCKING FOR THAT RAM CHIP,

1984
01:34:21,490 --> 01:34:23,058
- AREN'T YOU, PAL?
- RAM CHIP, RAM CHIP.
- YEAH.

1985
01:34:23,092 --> 01:34:25,193
WELL, UH, I LIKE IT.
YOU'RE A GOOD SELF-STARTER,

1986
01:34:25,227 --> 01:34:26,662
AND I LIKE
THE CUT OF YOUR JIB.

1987
01:34:26,695 --> 01:34:28,263
HERE'S YOUR RAM CHIP, PALLY.

1988
01:34:28,297 --> 01:34:31,333
ALL RIGHT. ALL RIGHT, CROW.
HOW YOU DOING?

1989
01:34:31,367 --> 01:34:33,268
- AH, FINE.
- DO YOU WANNA TELL ME

1990
01:34:33,302 --> 01:34:35,603
A GOOD THING AND A BAD THING
ABOUT THE MOVIE?

1991
01:34:35,637 --> 01:34:37,607
UH, IT WAS GROOVY.

1992
01:34:37,640 --> 01:34:39,275
AND I MEAN THAT
IN A GOOD WAY.

1993
01:34:39,308 --> 01:34:41,377
OKAY, AND THE BAD THING?

1994
01:34:41,410 --> 01:34:42,945
IT WAS GROOVY.

1995
01:34:42,978 --> 01:34:44,680
RIGHT, AND YOU MEAN THAT
IN A BAD WAY, RIGHT?

1996
01:34:44,713 --> 01:34:46,015
- YEAH, EXACTLY.
- OKAY, ALL RIGHT.

1997
01:34:46,048 --> 01:34:47,817
EXACTLY, OKAY. READY?

1998
01:34:47,850 --> 01:34:49,252
- ARE YOU READY, GIRL?
- YEAH.

1999
01:34:49,285 --> 01:34:52,187
OKAY, TELL ME A GOOD THING
AND A BAD THING ABOUT THE MOVIE.

2000
01:34:53,855 --> 01:34:55,523
RICHARD BASEHART?

2001
01:34:55,557 --> 01:34:57,727
- [BOTS MOAN]
- RICHARD BASEHART?

2002
01:34:57,760 --> 01:34:59,695
OKAY, WELL,
YOU GET A RAM CHIP.

2003
01:34:59,728 --> 01:35:02,498
- WHAT? THAT'S WRONG.
- YEAH, OKAY, GOOD.

2004
01:35:02,532 --> 01:35:04,267
ALL RIGHT, OKAY, WELL.

2005
01:35:04,300 --> 01:35:06,235
WE GOT ANOTHER LETTER
TO READ.

2006
01:35:06,268 --> 01:35:07,737
AND THANKS FOR EVERYBODY

2007
01:35:07,770 --> 01:35:09,238
WHO'S WRITTEN IN SO FAR.

2008
01:35:09,272 --> 01:35:11,707
YOU REALLY HELP US
KEEP GOING UP HERE IN SPACE.

2009
01:35:11,740 --> 01:35:14,110
CAMBOT, COULD WE HAVE THAT
UP ON THE SCREEN?

2010
01:35:14,143 --> 01:35:15,543
THIS ONE COMES FROM

2011
01:35:15,577 --> 01:35:17,880
A GUY NAMED RYAN WIESBROCK

2012
01:35:17,913 --> 01:35:19,682
FROM ILLINOIS.

2013
01:35:19,715 --> 01:35:21,583
DEAR JOEL, TOM SIRBOL--

2014
01:35:21,617 --> 01:35:24,353
- HUH?
- AND CROW. TOM SIRBOL.

2015
01:35:24,387 --> 01:35:26,255
I'M 14 YEARS OLD.
I LOVE YOUR SHOW.

2016
01:35:26,288 --> 01:35:27,690
I START LAUGHING SO HARD

2017
01:35:27,723 --> 01:35:29,458
WHEN YOU MAKE COMMENTS
DURING THE MOVIE.

2018
01:35:29,492 --> 01:35:31,293
TEARS COME TO MY EYES.

2019
01:35:31,327 --> 01:35:33,428
TOM SIRBOL IS THE BEST,

2020
01:35:33,462 --> 01:35:34,930
- BECAUSE HIS VOICE IS SO DEEP--
- THANK YOU.

2021
01:35:34,963 --> 01:35:37,332
WHEN HE MAKES A JOKE,
IT SOUNDS FUNNY.

2022
01:35:37,365 --> 01:35:39,335
LIKE WHEN HE SAID,
"OH, I HATE TO SHOOT

2023
01:35:39,368 --> 01:35:40,803
A BUTT LIKE THAT."

2024
01:35:40,837 --> 01:35:43,372
OH, I HATE TO SHOOT
A BUTT LIKE THAT.

2025
01:35:43,405 --> 01:35:45,140
- RIGHT, ANYWAY,
HE LATER ASKS--
- MAGICAL.

2026
01:35:45,173 --> 01:35:47,810
ABOUT BEING SIRBOL,
AND IT'S TOM SERVO.

2027
01:35:47,843 --> 01:35:49,345
BUT IT'S AN HONEST MISTAKE.

2028
01:35:49,378 --> 01:35:51,413
ANYWAY, THERE'S
A PICTURE HERE, TOO.

2029
01:35:51,447 --> 01:35:52,782
SHOW THAT, CAMBOT.

2030
01:35:52,815 --> 01:35:55,083
HE'S REALLY
A GOOD ARTIST, ACTUALLY.

2031
01:35:55,117 --> 01:35:57,920
SO ANYWAY, THAT ENDS THE
EXPERIMENT FOR TODAY.

2032
01:35:57,953 --> 01:35:59,255
WHAT DO YOU THINK, SIRS?

2033
01:35:59,288 --> 01:36:01,757
WHAT ABOUT THE ADDRESS?

2034
01:36:01,790 --> 01:36:04,527
I GOT IT. I GOT IT, OKAY.

2035
01:36:04,560 --> 01:36:07,597
SEND IT TO THE MYSTERY SCIENCE
THEATER 3000 FAN CLUB.

2036
01:36:07,630 --> 01:36:09,965
P.O. BOX 5325.

2037
01:36:09,998 --> 01:36:11,233
HOPKINS, MINNESOTA.

2038
01:36:11,267 --> 01:36:14,170
55343.

2039
01:36:14,203 --> 01:36:16,138
SEND 'EM QUICK.

2040
01:36:16,172 --> 01:36:17,673
WELL, NOT BAD. NOT BAD.

2041
01:36:17,707 --> 01:36:19,708
HEY, HOW'S MY HAIR NOW?

2042
01:36:19,742 --> 01:36:22,645
GO LIKE THIS.

2043
01:36:22,678 --> 01:36:24,213
YOU LOOK LIKE BIG BOY.

2044
01:36:24,247 --> 01:36:27,148
FILE THAT.

2045
01:36:27,182 --> 01:36:29,718
UNTIL NEXT TIME,
FLABBY-CAKES.

2046
01:36:32,520 --> 01:36:36,158
♪♪ [THEME]
